inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_4 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:33Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:33 lap 1 grain: still paused on PIPELINES-GREEN; today's state of that dep: spiral, dice, polyglot, alphabet, x, eoie all red on the 06:48 push for causes fixed in working trees (rustix Linux cfg, dir-tree-html UTF-8, mix deps.get, x protocol.spi, eoie partial src commit); i574n.github has no Actions runs at all (gh run list 404) Next: resume when PIPELINES-GREEN shows the next push runs green; check whether i574n.github needs a workflow at all")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_5 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:25Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:25 lap 2 grain, corrects lap 1 (i574n.github has no Actions runs at all): the local C:\\home\\git\\i574n.github checkout is the i574n/.github repo (git remote origin), not i574n/i574n.github (which does not exist, hence the 404). i574n/.github has a workflow (gh-pages.yml + actions.lock) and runs: the 10-18 17:49Z push run was green (1h40m) and deployed; the 22:13Z push run failed after 1h18m but its Ubuntu-leg publish still deployed at 23:32Z (Pages built at i574n.github.io/.github/). So it does need its workflow (it is the backlog and workflow.livemd host) and is one more repo PIPELINES-GREEN must see green. Still paused on PIPELINES-GREEN; the list of repos to watch is spiral, dice, polyglot, alphabet, x, eoie, blog, dir-tree-html, tibia and i574n/.github. Next: when PIPELINES-GREEN reports the next push wave, read each repo's newest push run conclusion with gh run list -R i574n/<repo> -L 1")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_6 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 6u32, "2026-10-19T14:01Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:01 lap 3 grain: the reference chain made explicit. i574n.github/scripts/workflow.ps1 runs init.ps1 (clones spiral, dir-tree-html, polyglot, dice, alphabet, tibia beside it) then workflow.livemd = build.ps1, outdated.ps1, publish.ps1, and build.ps1 builds spiral, dir-tree-html, polyglot (Stop on failure), then dice, alphabet, tibia with -OnError Continue. Its CI twin is i574n/.github's gh-pages workflow, so that run is the end-to-end oracle. Its last red run (39171310951, 10-18 22:13Z, Ubuntu leg) shows the open breakages in order: a polyglot step referencing an undefined PackageManager variable (Continue), Cells mix step exit 1 under spiral/apps/cells (Continue), spiral/apps/wasm run printing usage (-e, --exception), alphabet exits 100 and 70, near wallet test:e2e timing out on config.webServer after 60 s, and the publish whose half dist turned the page 404 (TREE-PAGES note 11). So the order of fixes for this item is the PIPELINES-GREEN list plus near-wallet e2e and alphabet's 100/70. Still paused on PIPELINES-GREEN. Next: after the next .github run, diff its failed steps against this list")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_7 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:31Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 10:31 lap 4 grain: read the alphabet part of the reference run's last red log (39171310951). The exit 100s are by design: alphabet/scripts/init.ps1:32-35 runs apt-get update and apt install pandoc fonts-nanum-coding once with sudo and once without (container fallback), all -OnError Continue, so the no-sudo pair always fails on a runner (Permission denied) and the Windows leg's WSL apt cannot find fonts-nanum-coding; harmless noise. The real alphabet failure is exit 70 from cargo binstall -y tectonic (init.ps1:38): binstall falls back to cargo install tectonic 0.17.0, which fails (exit 101) without the TeX/harfbuzz system libraries, while alphabet's own workflow avoids that with wtfjoke/setup-tectonic@v3.1.5 before its build. The reference workflow lacked that step, so alphabet's PDF documents could never build there. Fixed in the tree: i574n/.github gh-pages.yml gains the same setup-tectonic step before pwsh scripts/workflow.ps1, and gh actions-lock pinned it in .github/workflows/actions.lock (8a63d07, additions only), per the lockfile rule. Needs the user's push. Next: on the next .github run, check that alphabet's documents build passes and that the cargo binstall tectonic line reports the preinstalled binary")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_8 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 8u32, "2026-10-19T15:18Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:18 lap 5 grain: found and fixed the near wallet e2e failure of the reference run (39171310951, Ubuntu leg): playwright runs webServer.command through sh, and the command was pwsh -c with a double-quoted script holding dollar-job, so sh expanded dollar-job to nothing and pwsh got = Start-Job ... (log: [WebServer] The term = is not recognized), the server never came up and playwright timed out after 60 s on config.webServer. On Windows cmd leaves the dollar alone, which is why it only failed on Linux. Fix in the spiral tree: lib/spiral/near/wallet/serve.ps1 (new, same steps: cd dist, Start-Job bunx --bun ssl-serve --ssl, 60 s, stop, receive) and playwright.config.ts runs pwsh -NoProfile -File serve.ps1, so no shell sees a dollar sign. Parse-checked, LF; not run (playwright e2e needs the built dist; it runs in spiral's and .github's CI after the user's push). Also checked: the PackageManager line of lap 3 no longer exists in any script under C:\\home\\git (no match), so that step is gone from the list. Remaining from the reference run: Cells mix exit 1, spiral/apps/wasm usage print, alphabet tectonic (fixed lap 4, unpushed), half-dist publish (fixed, unpushed).")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_9 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 9u32, "2026-10-19T15:36Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:36 lap 6 grain, the Cells mix step of the reference run has two causes, one per leg. Ubuntu: mix spiral.html ran in spiral/apps/cells before any mix deps.get (Unchecked dependencies: kino not available). The working tree's scripts/core.ps1 already has the fix (Invoke-PwshNotebook runs local.hex, local.rebar and deps.get when deps/kino is missing; uncommitted, 8 lines). Windows: Cannot remove symlink .../polyglot/deps/spiral/apps/cells/_build/dev/lib/spiral_cells/priv: not owner. The same Cells tree was reached through polyglot/deps/spiral (a symlink to spiral) and through spiral itself, so mix kept relinking priv under two paths. Fixed in the tree: core.ps1 now computes cellsDir with ResolveLink, so mix always runs from the real spiral/apps/cells path (checked: polyglot/deps/spiral/scripts/../apps/cells resolves to C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\apps\\cells, and the direct route is unchanged). Edit to spiral scripts/core.ps1 noted for the other lanes. Still open: spiral/apps/wasm build.ps1 run prints clap usage (Usage: spiral_wasm.exe --wasm <wasm>) because it runs with no --wasm argument; next lap.")
inl note_of_workflow_end_to_end_10 () = Note ("WORKFLOW-END-TO-END", 10u32, "2026-10-19T15:49Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:49 lap 7: the last item of the reference-run list is already resolved in HEAD. The spiral/apps/wasm usage print came from running spiral_wasm with no arguments. Since 668568ac (10-19 02:48) apps/wasm/build.ps1 runs it with --help as a deliberate run check: exit 0 and the --wasm argument expected, otherwise RUST-FAILED. So the Usage lines are now the passing check, not an error. Every breakage of run 39171310951 now has a fix in a tree: polyglot PackageManager (gone), Cells mix (deps.get guard + ResolveLink, unpushed), apps/wasm (HEAD), alphabet tectonic (unpushed), near wallet e2e (serve.ps1, unpushed), half-dist publish (unpushed). The next .github run after the user's push is the test; the item stays Paused on PIPELINES-GREEN until then.")
