inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_12 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 12u32, "2026-10-15T01:48Z", "lane-b", "21:48 lane B: eoie run 38666180814 (push 530d032) GREEN on ubuntu (13m50s) and windows (12m38s): planning_cli and proxy-edit fixes confirmed; note the backlog repo's GitHub name is i574n/.github (gh -R i574n/.github), not i574n.github")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_13 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 13u32, "2026-10-15T02:02Z", "lane-b", "22:02 lane B: spiral 38666165169 red on ubuntu, CuPy fix confirmed (no targets-disagree lines): lib/spiral 39 files, 315 passed, 14 failed, all 14 in sm'.spi and all one cause: gleam build 'Hex API failure: The rate limit for the Hex API has been exceeded' (every Kino gleam test project is a fresh package without manifest.toml, so each gleam build resolves versions through the Hex API; 3 attempts each); windows was cancelled by fail-fast (its playwright browser download 400s are retried noise); MemAvailable never under 10.7 GB; apps/wasm passed (no rustup E0463 race). Fix in progress (Kino targets.ex): resolve once per dependency set under a :global lock and copy the locked manifest.toml (spiral-bin/kino-gleam-locks/<hash>.toml) into every later gleam project")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_14 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 14u32, "2026-10-15T02:20Z", "lane-b", "22:20 lane B: .github 38666190579 red for the same reason (sm'.spi gleam builds hit the Hex API rate limit: ellipsis, index_of, replicate_2, replicate_3); gleam lock proof: a gleam project with the copied manifest.toml builds and runs with the network blocked (dead proxy), the same project without it fails resolving gtempo on repo.hex.pm")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_15 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 15u32, "2026-10-15T02:23Z", "lane-b", "22:23 lane B: polyglot 38666169741: ubuntu GREEN (26m47s, incl. Tasks.spi migration); windows-2025 died at 49 min with 'hosted runner lost communication' (no log; same symptom as alphabet's windows job this morning), cause unknown (runner starvation is the hypothesis, not acted on)")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_16 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 16u32, "2026-10-15T03:01Z", "lane-b", "23:01 lane B: Hex rate-limit fix LANDED (uncommitted): apps/kino targets.ex gleam_build resolves once per dependency set under a :global lock and copies the locked manifest.toml from spiral-bin/kino-gleam-locks/<sha>.toml into every later gleam project (key = target + [dependencies], not the project name), toolchain.ex cache_dir public (opts :bin_cache_dir), targets_test lock-key test; Kino suite on a private copy with it: 235 tests, 5 failures, all environment artifacts of the copy (3 dice/alphabet siblings missing, private MIX_BUILD_PATH path assert, one slots timing assert under load), none in targets/memo/daemon tests")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_17 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 17u32, "2026-10-15T05:19Z", "lane-b", "01:19 lane B: correction: the landed gleam lock had a bug the copy suite did not reach: :global.trans got a 3-tuple id ({module, :gleam_resolve, path}) where it needs {resource, requester}, so every gleam build without a kept lock raised 'no function clause matching in :global.set_lock/4' (found by the pack-1g corpus check: 48 gleam-target tests failed in parsing/runtime/sm'/testing); fixed to {{Targets, :gleam_resolve, path}, self()} and covered by a new targets_test case that runs a real gleam build twice (first resolves under the lock and keeps the manifest, the second builds from it); targets_test 20/20")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_18 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 18u32, "2026-10-15T09:07Z", "lane-b", "05:07 lane B summary for the 21:31 push: eoie GREEN; spiral and .github red only on the gleam Hex rate limit (fixed in Kino, uncommitted, proven by the 1g corpus rerun 127/0 incl. every sm' gleam test and a real-gleam regression test); polyglot ubuntu green, windows runner lost; dice/alphabet not pushed (windows contract needs spiral_wasm in WSL, lands last); next: user commits Kino targets.ex/toolchain.ex, then read spiral/.github runs (windows jobs still lack evidence because fail-fast cancelled them)")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_19 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 19u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: no push since 10-14 21:31 (latest eoie run 38666180814 green). Unblocking order: commit lane B's Hex-lock fix, push, read spiral and .github windows jobs (never ran: fail-fast); dice/alphabet stay last behind the WSL spiral_wasm build.")
inl note_of_ci_after_spi_migration_20 () = Note ("CI-AFTER-SPI-MIGRATION", 20u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: the user push of 10-16 22:14 is green on i574n/dice (1h10m), x (9m), eoie (20m); polyglot and alphabet green since 10-16 00:27. i574n/spiral 38994173933 failed in 0 s: the job-level env used the runner context (not allowed there), so GitHub rejected the file; fixed in the tree (.github/workflows/gh-pages.yml exports SPIRAL_BIN_CACHE_DIR through GITHUB_ENV). Waiting only on the next push.")
