inl samples_to_test_blocks () = Task ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", "Folder samples (apps/compiler/tmp/samples, ~3,770 matrix rows) become test blocks in .spi files, the way lib/spiral did on 2026-10-12: one file per family, each test block names its backends (///> targets) and its expected exit/stdout inline; the matrix reads expectations from source instead of the cache-only EXPECTED.tsv; start with one low-signal family (heap_/closure_/union_ combinatorics, TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS) and measure suite time before/after; negative samples become test blocks expecting a diagnostic", Story, P1, D6, 40u32, Active, "TEST-SIGNAL-METRICS,TEST-RUN-REPORT", "samples,tests,harness,main,lab-held", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_samples_to_test_blocks () = Planning ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", Minutes 1800u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_1 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:39Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:39 touch: first family chosen by size and uniformity: ebpf_* (31 samples, 166 rows, all expected exit 0); conversion must keep the 166 rows byte-identical before the folders go")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_2 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: baseline 10-15: 1,216 sample .spi files, 0 contain a test block; first family still ebpf_* (31 dirs). Enabler now available: the host --source-blocks/--test-blocks (pack-1g) give exact block spans, so the harness can run test blocks without line heuristics.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_3 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 3u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night: first family slice: ebpf_arith, ebpf_shift, ebpf_bool as 3 test blocks in one file (body = the old main, ///> c and zig) pass beside samples/core (draft job tmp/night/ebpf-blocks).")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_4 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:20Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 08:20 lap 1 grain: the first family slice (ebpf_arith, ebpf_shift, ebpf_bool as 3 test blocks, c + zig, failwith on a wrong exit) moved from job tmp/night/ebpf-blocks into spiral/lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS with packageDir ../../apps/compiler/tmp/samples (the job-tmp copy failed Package not loaded; the in-tree run had passed) Next: HEAVY QUEUE: Cells gate of the lab copy; then the remaining 28 ebpf_* samples as blocks and a suite-time before/after")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_5 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 5u32, "2026-10-19T14:16Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:16 lap 2 grain: lab gate of ebpf_family.spi fails 3/3 on c (zig not_run), 0 type errors; from the lab the package resolves samples/core through packageDir ../../apps/compiler/tmp/samples, but the samples' C builds take matrix C flags and c-shim headers that Cells' C target does not pass, a likely cause Next: HEAVY QUEUE 2 rerun with -NotebookOut; if it is the C flags, give Cells' c target the matrix -fwrapv/-std=c11 flags or move the family under lib's core")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_6 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 6u32, "2026-10-19T14:49Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:49 lap 3 grain: raw rerun: all 3 tests fail with PackageErrors from Cells' generated package.spiproj, the uppercase-mount bug (lab folder SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS mounted as an uppercase package name), fixed today in Cells mounts.ex (CELLS-LAB-PACKAGE note 12); not a test problem Next: re-gate after the core switch (queue 3)")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_7 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 7u32, "2026-10-19T18:17Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 14:17 lap 4 grain: the 3-test ebpf slice passes 3/3 from its lab home after the mounts fix and the core switch (queue 3, 10-19); the data the matrix needs already exists: mix spiral.notebook --gate --metrics <dir> writes tests.tsv with one (test, target, status) row each, which probe-lib.ps1 reads today Next: the SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES row-kind patch reads that tests.tsv into matrix rows; then convert the next family (dynamic_array_* C ABI samples are poor candidates; pick a pure family like tagged_union_*)")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_8 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 8u32, "2026-10-21T23:30Z", "main", "19:30 second family converted and gated: lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS/tagged_union_family.spi holds the 4 tagged_union_* samples (enum, heterogeneous, scalar, three_case) as test blocks on c and zig, each program () returning 0 as the sample's main did. Unions, cases and score functions get per-sample prefixes (phase, mixed_, scalar_, three_), because the samples reuse outcome/Hit/score, which would collide in one module. Registered in the lab package.spiproj. Cells gate (job main-tagged-union-gate2, probe-lib through capped-run): 4/4 passed, 0 type errors, 43 s wall, peak 1.1 GB. The originals stay in samples/ until the row-kind patch reads tests.tsv into matrix rows (SELF-CHECKING-SAMPLES).")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_9 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 9u32, "2026-10-21T23:33Z", "main", "19:33 third family: lab tuple_family.spi (tuple_pair, tuple_mixed, nested_tuple as test blocks on c and zig; names prefixed where they collided: classified_score, make_nested, nested_score). Gate (job main-tuple-gate): 3/3 passed, 0 type errors, 123 s wall on a loaded box, peak 573 MB. ts_tuple_mixed is a byte-identical copy of tuple_mixed's source (a TypeScript-list duplicate), so it needs no separate test. Converted so far: ebpf 3 + tagged_union 4 + tuple 3 = 10 samples.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_10 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 10u32, "2026-10-21T23:36Z", "main", "19:36 fourth family: lab string_family.spi (string_eq, string_ord, static_string, string_utf8 as test blocks on c and zig; static_string's helper renamed same_text). Gate (job main-string-gate): 4/4 passed, 0 type errors, 58 s wall, peak 1.1 GB. The UTF-8 byte semantics (StringLength of é = 2, StringIndex bytes, slices) agree on c and zig as in the matrix. Converted so far: 14 samples in 4 families (ebpf 3, tagged_union 4, tuple 3, string 4).")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_11 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 11u32, "2026-10-21T23:40Z", "main", "19:40 fifth family, generated: lab to-family.ps1 now converts any list of samples mechanically (helpers above main stay top-level, main becomes program () inside test <sample>_returns_zero, one ///> line per target; it refuses when two samples define the same top-level name, so collisions are renamed by hand as in tagged_union and tuple). small_int_family.spi (small_int_scalar, small_int_ops, unsigned_mod, method_i8; 106 lines) gated by job main-small-int-gate: 4/4 passed, 0 type errors, peak 579 MB. Total converted: 18 samples in 5 families. gate-family.ps1 -File <family>.spi is the reusable gate wrapper.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_12 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 12u32, "2026-10-21T23:45Z", "main", "19:45 sixth family + converter upgrades: to-family.ps1 -Prefix renames every top-level name and union case of a sample to <sample>_<name> (word-boundary, so samples that each define create/get/set coexist), and each test now asserts the sample's C exit from the accepted baseline (spiral-bin/baseline/EXPECTED.tsv, C rows that ran) instead of assuming 0: array_create_reads_zero returns 5 by design (unwritten slot reads 0, plus written 5), which the first gate run flagged. array_family.spi (array_bool, array_cell, array_create_reads_zero, array_f32, array_fun, array_heap_f32, array_heap_heap) gated by job main-array-gate2: 7/7 passed, 0 type errors. Total converted: 25 samples in 6 families, all gated green on c and zig.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_13 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 13u32, "2026-10-21T23:47Z", "main", "19:47 seventh family: union_family.spi (union_array, union_array_mix, union_bool, union_call, union_case_record_field_order, union_cell_mix, union_f32_text, union_f64s, union_fun_mix, union_heap) gated 10/10, 0 type errors (job main-union-gate2). Converter fix found by the first run: Spiral reads a lowercase identifier as a variable, so prefixed union cases became unbound; cases now get a PascalCase sample prefix (Held -> UnionArrayHeld), other names keep <sample>_<name>. Total converted: 35 samples in 7 families, all green on c and zig.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_14 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 14u32, "2026-10-21T23:50Z", "main", "19:50 mut family: 10 mut_* samples (heap, pair, union nesting, f32/i64 text) into lab mut_family.spi via to-family -Prefix; gate c+zig 10/10, type errors 0. Total 45 samples in 8 families.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_15 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 15u32, "2026-10-21T23:53Z", "main", "19:53 closure family: 10 closure_* samples (apply, curry, depth, heap nesting) into closure_family.spi; gate c+zig 10/10, type errors 0. Total 55 samples in 9 families; 767 eligible left, contract_* (328) is the bulk.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_16 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 16u32, "2026-10-21T23:55Z", "main", "19:55 heap family: 10 heap_* samples (array, bool, closure, f32 variants) into heap_family.spi; gate c+zig 10/10, type errors 0. Total 65 samples in 10 families.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_17 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 17u32, "2026-10-22T00:00Z", "main", "20:00 suite time before/after (lab suite-time.ps1, reruns from the same data): matrix single-flight-20261021-031858 on the 74 converted samples x c,zig = 148 rows, 146 s serial (compile 22 + native 118 + run 6), 0.99 s per row. Cells gates of 7 families = 122 test rows, 646 s serial (compile 361 + target 285), 5.29 s per row: 5.4x the matrix. Compile does not grow with file size (mut_family 413 lines has the lowest mean, 3.3 s); its floor is 1.2 s per cell against 0.15 s per matrix row, so the gap is fixed per-cell overhead plus contention (gates ran beside tibia-build-pace2 and eoie-release; queue averaged 15 s per cell). probe-lib sets SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0 by design, so a warm rerun (mut, 48.6 s vs 66.6 s cold) gains only from a warm box. method_family ran 10/10 too: 75 tests, 74 unique samples in 11 families. RULE (fixed now, before more data): no more families and no removal list for originals until suite-time.ps1 shows Cells at most 2.0x matrix per row on a quiet box (no heavy slot held); the lever is the per-cell floor (KINO-HOT-PATHS resident server, CELLS-PACK-NEXT); re-measure after that pack installs. Converted lab families stay as the fixture.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_18 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 18u32, "2026-10-22T00:52Z", "main", "20:52 suite-time.ps1 now reads archived gate data (lab gates-20261021, 20 files) including the three earlier gates (tagged_union, tuple, string): 82 cells, 144 test rows, 767 s serial (compile 420 + target 347), 5.33 s per row against the matrix's 0.99: still 5.4x. Correction to note 17: the compile floor is 457 ms (one cell of the 19:29 tagged_union gate, the quietest run), not 1.2 s, so part of the per-cell cost seen tonight is load and queue, not fixed overhead; the floor is still 3x a matrix row's 0.15 s. The 2x rule stands and is judged on a quiet box.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_19 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 19u32, "2026-10-22T01:48Z", "main", "21:48 lab folder moved whole to spiral/target/lab-attic/2026-10-21/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS (LAB-SWEEP-SPIRAL note 4): 11 family files, to-family.ps1, gate-family.ps1, suite-time.ps1 and gates-20261021. When the 2x rule clears, move it back to spiral/lab (suite-time.ps1 reads gates-20261021 relatively, so the folder moves intact); the attic keeps days for 14 days.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_20 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 20u32, "2026-10-22T01:52Z", "main", "21:52 REVERSED: the attic was drift (user via x: target folders get deleted often to free disk). All 160 files moved back from spiral/target/lab-attic/2026-10-21 to their original spiral/lab paths (sha256 equal for every file), and the attic folder is removed; ignore the attic path in the earlier note. Healing is finishing the items that hold these folders (user 21:5x).")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_21 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 21u32, "2026-10-22T05:37Z", "main", "01:36 main: lab run outputs moved to the run cache, per the lab rule that run outputs never sit in lab: 20 file(s) (logs, notebooks, diffs, metrics/gate/timing TSVs) are now under %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runs\\lab-outputs\\SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS\\ at the same relative paths, sha256 checked. Scripts and probes stay in lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS until the item lands.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_22 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 22u32, "2026-10-22T07:12Z", "main", "03:12 main: repaired references my drains broke. (1) suite-time.ps1's default -NotebookDir now points at %LOCALAPPDATA%\\spiral-bin\\runs\\lab-outputs\\SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS\\gates-20261021, where the 01:36 output move put the gate notebooks. (2) gate-string.ps1, gate-tagged-union.ps1 and gate-tuple.ps1 called lab/CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE/probe-lib.ps1 (promoted to apps/cells/spi/lib_gate.ps1 on 10-21); they now call lib_gate.ps1. (3) lib_gate.ps1's new -Lib guard accepts any folder with lib/spiral at or above it, as this lab folder inside the spiral repo has. Checked: lab family dir, tree lib and TEMP copies pass; a path with no lib above it throws.")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_23 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 23u32, "2026-10-23T18:03Z", "main", "2026-10-23 14:03 main: the matrix row kind for test blocks exists now, as its own script rather than inside test.ps1 (1,143 lines, already past the 1k limit; and test.ps1's native code is the native-memo key): apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/test-blocks.ps1 [-Lib <package dir> -Files <spi...>] [-Reports <*.tests.tsv>] [-Out <run dir>]. It runs Cells lib_gate per file (or takes existing reports) and writes a results.tsv in the matrix schema: id testblocks/<file>/<test>, backend = target, suite testblocks, exit 0/1, oracle agree / DISAGREE against the test's inline expectation, not-run-<status> otherwise; exit 1 on any DISAGREE. Dry-proven on 4 existing family reports (80 rows, agree 80), and compare-runs.ps1 reads two such run dirs: a flipped test shows as exit + oracle cells and 'DISAGREE rows on right: 1'. The real -Lib run over the 11 lab/SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS family files is queued at the chain end (job-1792778604345, after the float wiring gate).")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_24 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 24u32, "2026-10-24T03:08Z", "main", "2026-10-23 23:08 main grooming: main-test-blocks-families finished 0 at 22:05: test-block rows 150, agree 150, DISAGREE 0, not run 0 (run dir spiral-bin\\runs\\testblocks-20261023-215838).")
inl note_of_samples_to_test_blocks_25 () = Note ("SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS", 25u32, "2026-10-24T06:48Z", "main", "2026-10-24 02:48 main: families moved toward their real place. The 11 family files (150 test-block rows, all agreeing in run testblocks-20261023-215838) are copied, hash-equal, to apps/compiler/tmp/tests/families with package.spiproj's packageDir rewritten to ../../samples (same core). Nothing in apps, scripts or .github referenced the lab path. After tibia's block, test-blocks.ps1 -Lib that folder must reproduce 150/150; then the lab copies and its gate-*.ps1 runners (superseded by test-blocks.ps1) go, and to-family.ps1 (the converter for further families) moves to apps/compiler/tmp/scripts. Retiring the folder samples these families replace is a separate rule-based step.")
inl test_expect_persist () = Task ("TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST", "Expect-test mode for test blocks (user 2026-10-12): a run may write each block's observed result into the source (toggleable dev mode, ppx_expect / insta style) and clears it after a successful run; needs a result syntax under the test header that the parser skip already ignores; user decision 2026-10-12 18:53: rewrite the source, opt-in: a dev-mode flag (--accept) rewrites the _assert_eq literal in the .spi in place after a run, under a lock; without the flag a mismatch fails; git shows the diff, the user commits; 2026-10-12 19:22: dependency on SAMPLES-TO-TEST-BLOCKS removed (it applies to the test blocks lib already has; the user picked it for the next session's lanes); 20:07 Kino lane (uncommitted, Spiral.Kino.Accept): --accept (.spi only, also via the warm daemon) rewrites, for each failed test whose output holds __assert_eq { actual = A; expected = E }, the single _assert_eq E literal in that test's block to A (type suffix kept), under <file>.accept.lock; rows report status accepted (counted as executed), the run exits 0 when nothing else failed; refusals per test (accept_refused: none or several matching literals, non-plain actual); without the flag a mismatch fails and the file is untouched; real run: plain exit 1, --accept exit 0 accepted 1 (_assert_eq 5i32 -> 4i32 in place), re-run 3/3 passed with memo_hits 2", Story, P1, D5, 100u32, Done, "TEST-RUN-REPORT", "tests,kino,samples", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_test_expect_persist () = Planning ("TEST-EXPECT-PERSIST", Minutes 600u32, Load Medium, Assigned Pair)
