inl kino_wgsl_target () = Task ("KINO-WGSL-TARGET", "///> wgsl (and zig) targets in Kino: today Builders knows rust, fsharp, typescript, python, cuda, cpp, gleam, lua, c, delphi; wgsl runs through spiral-wgsl (exit code, prints nothing) (skip if the Kino lane already tracks it); 16:25 Kino lane: ///> zig compiles the Zig backend and runs zig run main.zig (SPIRAL_ZIG or zig on PATH; missing zig = unsupported); ///> wgsl compiles the Wgsl backend and validates with naga when present (SPIRAL_NAGA), else the compile is the check; unit tests green, no real Zig/WGSL cell run yet (first end-to-end use: the tibia lane); review (tibia lane, 16:30): compile/naga-only can never fail an assertion (KINO-C-FALSE-PASS shape); requested from the Kino lane: run spiral-wgsl (SPIRAL_WGSL_RUN or toolchains/wgsl-run): exit 0 pass, 2 fail, 3 = no adapter = unsupported, other non-zero fail; no runner = unsupported, never passed; wgsl test bodies end in an i32 status expression (no lib testing strings); 16:45 Kino lane: ///> wgsl now executes: naga validates when found, then spiral-wgsl runs the shader; exit 0 pass, 3 / missing runner = unsupported (never pass), any other exit fails with output; stub-runner unit test (targets_test.exs) covers 0/1/2/3 + missing runner; end-to-end check (incl. a broken expectation) handed to the tibia lane; verified 17:20 by the tibia lane: ///> wgsl xtea_published_vector_on_gpu passes (compile 838 ms, target 4272 ms), with the expected value broken 1232991184 -> 1232991185 it fails (spiral-wgsl exit 1, run exit 1); ///> zig xtea_published_vector_on_zig passes (target 34.6 s, zig 0.18-dev), broken the same way it fails (zig exit 1); no false pass", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,wgsl,tibia", "current", "current")
