inl note_of_tibia_latest_track_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: checked GitHub: canary v3.6.1 (2026-07-01), otclient 4.1 (2026-08-15), nExBot v4.0.4 (2026-07-15, main pushed 2026-09-01) are still the latest releases; we run all three.")
inl note_of_tibia_latest_track_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK", 2u32, "2026-10-18T16:10Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 12:10 checked GitHub again: canary v3.6.1 (2026-07-01; main pushed 2026-10-17, no newer release), otclient 4.1 (2026-08-15, mehah and opentibiabr show the same), nExBot v4.0.4 (2026-07-15, last push 2026-09-01), mesa-dist-win 26.2.4 (2026-10-04, which CI pulls as latest): all current. Stale: spiral's wgsl runner (apps/compiler/tmp/tests/native-shims/wgsl-run) pins wgpu = '24' and pollster 0.4, while wgpu is at v30.0.1 (2026-08-22). The upgrade crosses API changes (adapter and device requests, the poll/Maintain API, the device-lost callback) and touches native-shims, which the compiler lane keeps fixed between its review and the accept run, so it waits for them; then rebuild and rerun the tibia GPU twins (gpu_sim, hunt_sim) on lavapipe and the local NVIDIA.")
inl note_of_tibia_latest_track_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK", 3u32, "2026-10-18T17:40Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 13:40 CI actions brought to latest in tibia gh-pages.yml (uncommitted, actions.lock regenerated with gh actions-lock): checkout v6.1.0 -> v7.0.1, upload-artifact v5.0.0 -> v7.0.2 (v5 still ran on Node 20; spiral's runs carry the Node 20 deprecation annotation for it and for mlugg/setup-zig v2.2.1, which has no newer release), download-artifact v6.0.0 -> v8.0.2, setup-dotnet v5.4.0 -> v6.0.0, setup-python v6.3.0 -> v7.0.0. Release notes checked for breaks: download v8 now fails on a hash mismatch and skips unzipping non-zip files; upload v7 adds archive: false (opt-in); setup-python v7 removed the pip-install input; checkout v7 blocks fork checkouts under pull_request_target/workflow_run. tibia uses none of the changed inputs. Already latest: cache v6.1.0, setup-beam v1.24.1, setup-bun v2.2.0, setup-rust v1.3.0, actions-gh-pages v4.1.0. spiral/dice/alphabet workflows still pin the older majors (their lanes).")
inl note_of_tibia_latest_track_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK", 4u32, "2026-10-19T06:26Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-19 02:26 user direction: Rust nightly everywhere, pinned to a recent date as the default, and lowered only for the cases that still fail, across all repos. The rollout across repos was relayed to main. Tibia's part is done (uncommitted): gh-pages.yml moonrepo/setup-rust channel nightly-2025-05-09 -> nightly-2026-10-18 (no new uses:, so actions.lock is unchanged); new root rust-toolchain.toml with the same channel plus clippy, rust-src, rustfmt and wasm32-unknown-unknown, all available on that date; apps/map/run.ps1 runs rustc from the repo root so it picks up the file. Verified: apps/map/run.ps1 on rustc 1.101.0-nightly (8006091eb 2026-10-17) passes all three checks (dump identical, live scan 251/252, terrain.spi 4/4). Cells ///> rust tests still use Kino's +1.99.0 pin, which is main's to move.")
inl note_of_tibia_latest_track_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK", 5u32, "2026-10-20T05:02Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 01:02 checked GitHub (gh api): canary v3.6.1 (2026-07-01, main pushed 2026-10-17), otclient 4.1 (2026-08-15), nExBot v4.0.4 (2026-07-15), mesa-dist-win 26.2.4 (2026-10-04), wgpu v30.0.1 (2026-08-22): all current, and the wgsl runner is on wgpu 30 since WGSL-RUN-WGPU-30. tibia gh-pages.yml setup-beam now pins OTP 29 / Elixir 1.20 / Gleam 1.19.2 / rebar3 3.27.3 like the other repos (uncommitted, no new uses:). Closing for the Tibia parking: re-check these five when Tibia is resumed.")
inl note_of_tibia_latest_track_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-LATEST-TRACK", 6u32, "2026-10-23T04:06Z", "tibia-lane", "Check 2026-10-23 00:06 (gh release list, read-only): Canary v3.6.1 (2026-07-01) and OTClient Redemption 4.1 (2026-08-15) are still the latest releases; nothing to migrate.")
inl kino_cross_target_agreement () = Task ("KINO-CROSS-TARGET-AGREEMENT", "Automatic cross-target agreement: a test listing several targets (///> rust, ///> c, later ///> wgsl) compares their stdout and value against the oracle target, instead of each target only having to exit 0; today agreement holds only because every target asserts the same pinned values (apps/tibia hunt_sim.spi golden_seed_7: .rs and .c both print 7/140/69, verified 2026-10-12 after the KINO-C-FALSE-PASS fix); a cell's ///> lines are its whole target list by design; user decision 2026-10-12 19:09: default compares outputs: every listed target must pass and agree with the first listed target, fail on difference; a ///- --no-agree escape for intentionally different outputs; 20:46 Kino lane (uncommitted): a test with several ///> targets passes only if every target passes and prints the same as the first target that printed anything; mismatch fails with 'targets disagree: X printed ..., Y printed ...' and the row says disagrees; opt-out test x no_agree = (cell ///- --no-agree, round-trips); outputs normalized before comparing (blank lines dropped, String(\"...\") unwrapped, trailing status line 0 dropped, numbers at 6 decimals; a target with no captured output is not compared) because strict text failed math's 4 multi-target tests on harness formatting alone; math 15/15 with agreement on; note: 6-decimal normalization can hide real float disagreements beyond 1e-6", Story, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "CONFIGURABLE-ORACLE", "kino,tests,oracle", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_cross_target_agreement () = Planning ("KINO-CROSS-TARGET-AGREEMENT", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl wgsl_nullary_unions () = Task ("WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS", "First union step for WGSL: payload-free unions (enums) as u32 tags; today a runtime `union direction = North | East | South | West` fails with \"The WGSL backend doesn't support the type {North : () | East : () | South : () | West : ()} yet\"; records already flatten and compile-time unions erase (probe 2026-10-12: a record step with a static heading ran on spiral-wgsl, exit 0; lowbias32 mix32 and Chebyshev distance agree with Rust and C on the GPU); then payload unions, then arrays as storage buffers; 17:59 main (uncommitted, not yet built): codegenWgsl maps a union whose tag_cases are all unit to u32, TyUnionBox -> tag literal (h.Item.tags.[tag_id], works in both cores), TyUnionUnbox -> if/else-if chain on the tag (keeps self-tail continue legal), fallback or last case as final else; payload unions raise \"unions with payloads\"; probe tmp/wgsl/nullary_union/main.spi expects exit 170; build + spiral-wgsl + C cross-check + Wgsl harness rows handed to the compiler lane after its bless; 18:45: probe: C exit 170 as expected; WGSL raised 'doesn't support TyUnionUnbox' because union equality unboxes two scrutinees at once; the branch now accepts any number of scrutinees (tag tests joined with &&); rebuild + probe queued; 18:53 verified on the GPU: single-flight Debug build of 18:47 (0 errors) compiles tmp/wgsl/nullary_union/main.spi (constructors, a match with fallback, a match without, union equality = two-scrutinee unbox) to a 1,761-byte shader; spiral-wgsl exits 170, the C backend's build exits 170; remaining for Done: the probe as samples/wgsl_nullary_union on the Wgsl list (harness rows vs C) and a hopac build of the multi-scrutinee change; 20:03: samples/wgsl_nullary_union on the Wgsl list (spiral-wgsl 170 = C)", TaskKind, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "wgsl,compiler,tibia", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_wgsl_nullary_unions () = Planning ("WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl c_signed_overflow_ub () = Task ("C-SIGNED-OVERFLOW-UB", "The C backend emits signed arithmetic as plain + (v1 = v0 + 1l) while Rust emits wrapping_add: signed overflow is undefined behaviour in C, so the oracle could disagree under optimization; a probe (i32 max + 1 < max) agreed at -O0 and -O2 on 2026-10-12, but nothing guarantees it: add -fwrapv to the harness and Kino C builds or emit unsigned-cast arithmetic; unsigned u32 already wraps on both; 07:30 chosen fix (no codegen change, C stays upstream-shaped): the harness builds C and eBPF with -fwrapv (signed overflow wraps, matching Rust's wrapping ops); Kino's C flags get -fwrapv from the Kino agent; pack 1's suites run with it; 2026-10-13 09:52 main: pack 1 verified (both Release cores, both suites DISAGREE 0, sf vs hopac differ only on the expected Delphi format_any row) and blessed (3843 rows reproduced row for row; baseline 3936 -> 3949 lines)", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "c,backend,oracle", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_signed_overflow_ub () = Planning ("C-SIGNED-OVERFLOW-UB", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_hunt_sim_wgsl () = Task ("TIBIA-HUNT-SIM-WGSL", "Run apps/tibia/hunt_sim.spi simulate on WGSL and pin golden_seed_7 on the GPU: since 2026-10-12 the hunt draws a Troll from creatures.spi and uses the Canary melee formula from damage.spi, golden seed 7 = 10 kills, 178 gold, 81 health after 600 ticks (Rust and C agree; earlier values 7/140/69 are obsolete); needs runtime unions (vitality typestate, spell groups) in WGSL; the first end-to-end proof that one Spiral source simulates identically on CPU and GPU; 2026-10-13 03:53 done: hunt_sim golden_seed_7_on_gpu and scripted_beats_random_control_on_gpu pass on spiral-wgsl with the same numbers as Rust and C (pack-0004 WGSL-RECORD-JOIN-POINTS); all 12 apps/tibia modules now carry a ///> wgsl test (policy decisions, combat 2000-swing statistics bit-identical to Rust/C)", TaskKind, P2, D4, 100u32, Done, "WGSL-NULLARY-UNIONS,WGSL-PAYLOAD-UNIONS,KINO-WGSL-TARGET,WGSL-RECORD-JOIN-POINTS", "tibia,wgsl", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_hunt_sim_wgsl () = Planning ("TIBIA-HUNT-SIM-WGSL", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl zed_definition_impact () = Task ("ZED-DEFINITION-IMPACT", "Run test at cursor on a definition row runs only the tests that depend on that definition (today test-at-row.ps1 falls back to every test in the file: hunt_sim.spi row 86 inl advance -> all 6 tests); needs dependency information from the compiler (QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER) or Kino's per-test prefix plan; 2026-10-14 03:45 lane 1 (uncommitted, apps/zed/tasks/test-at-row.ps1): a definition row now runs only the tests that reach it: blocks follow the compiler's block rule (a column-0 non-comment line starts a statement, comment lines never start one), each test's direct references are the identifiers (and operator spellings) of earlier definitions (inl/let/and/type/union and its cases/nominal/prototype/instance) in its body, closed transitively over the definition graph; instances count as reached by every later test (instance resolution is implicit) and so does whatever they reference; a row on a test runs that test, a comment/blank row just above a block belongs to it, a definition no test reaches prints 'no test ... reaches X' and runs nothing, other rows run the whole file; -ImpactTable prints definition -> selected tests; analysis 3-4 s per file in PowerShell; tables: stream.spi (17 tests incl. the prelude) stream 16, fold 6 (from_list,sum,sum_2,sum_3,indexed,unzip), fold_back 4, try_item/item 10, take_while 3 (sum_2,sum_3,sum_4), map 2, zip 1, io/reader definitions 0; am'.spi (11 tests) length/index/generic_equable/equable/append 10 (the equable instance reaches them), init/init_base 6, choose/sum/last/slice 1 each, vec helpers 0; soundness by mutation (scratch copy of lib/spiral, a definition's body starts with failwith, then every test runs, memo off, Invoke-Heavy): stream take_while: failed exactly sum_2,sum_3,sum_4 = selected; stream fold: failed exactly the 6 selected; am' slice: failed exactly slice; am' init: failed choose,sum,last,try_pick, a subset of the 6 selected (init_series and indexed reach init lexically but never evaluate it); no failing test outside a selection in any of the 4 mutations; time (loaded machine, fresh private daemon per run): stream all 137 s vs take_while 17 s and fold 53 s; am' all 279 s vs slice 62 s, init 280 s (no saving: 6 of 10 tests plus cold daemon start dominated); the gutter task in .zed/tasks.json uses the same script; 2026-10-14 04:29 review fixes: Get-BlockAtRow returned through a range over [int]::MaxValue for rows after the last block (pwsh: Array dimensions exceeded supported range) and read the script's lines: it now returns -1 before slicing and takes the lines as a parameter; // comment stripping cut URLs inside strings: Remove-LineComment skips // inside double-quoted strings (escape-aware); proven on a scratch file (rows 9, 10 and 50 after the last block run the whole file instead of crashing; a definition whose string holds https://example.com//path still reaches the helper called after it on the same line); stream/am' impact tables unchanged; 2026-10-14 05:59 lane 1: wired to the reach-based step memo (KINO-SOTA): run test at cursor on take_while (stream.spi row 181, 3 tests) took 130 s cold and 12 s when nothing it reaches changed (3/3 memo hits, no compile; the 12 s are pwsh + selection about 2 s, mix boot about 6 s, memo context about 3 s; the warm-daemon path of run_notebook.ps1 skips the mix boot once the shared daemon runs this Kino); the task now passes --no-html (the html export only cost time; the ipynb in temp stays); the faster reach index (name -> definitions dictionary) gives the same tables; remaining limits documented: lexical over-approximation (never fewer tests), definitions after the last test are only compiled by full builds", TaskKind, P3, D5, 100u32, Done, "ZED-TEST-RUNNABLES,QUERY-CACHE-COMPILER", "zed,kino,tests", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_zed_definition_impact () = Planning ("ZED-DEFINITION-IMPACT", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_storage_boundary () = Task ("TIBIA-STORAGE-BOUNDARY", "Measured 2026-10-12: backend-neutral Spiral (records, u32/i32 arithmetic, compile-time unions) already compiles to Rust, C and WGSL with identical results without any prototype; prototypes are only needed at the storage boundary (Rust Vec/arrays vs WGSL storage buffers, one simulation per GPU invocation); design that boundary as a prototype with Rust and WGSL instances, modeled on mrakgr's corebase sa/da instances (type-level length via real_core.type_lit_to_lit), instead of making rules code backend-aware", Story, P3, D4, 0u32, Paused, "WGSL-STORAGE-ARRAYS,TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", "tibia,wgsl,prototypes", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_storage_boundary () = Planning ("TIBIA-STORAGE-BOUNDARY", Minutes 360u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_storage_boundary_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-STORAGE-BOUNDARY", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: the compiler lane's WGSL parallel lanes (one seed per thread, chunked dispatch, pack-1e) already run gpu_sim with scratch arrays bit-exact, so the boundary is no longer blocking; lowered to P3 until a second GPU workload needs it.")
inl note_of_tibia_storage_boundary_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-STORAGE-BOUNDARY", 2u32, "2026-10-21T11:20Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 07:20 Parked with the Tibia lane's closing pass (TIBIA note 13): Planned -> Paused; resume when a second GPU workload needs storage arrays (gpu_sim already runs bit-exact without it).")
inl note_of_tibia_storage_boundary_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-STORAGE-BOUNDARY", 3u32, "2026-10-23T11:11Z", "tibia-lane", "Retirement grooming 07:1x: outside the end estimate unless AGENT M3 makes a second GPU workload, which is its resume condition.")
inl tibia_headless_client () = Task ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", "Headless game client in Spiral (Rust target) for agents and the arena live layer: Canary 3.6.1 keeps the classic login protocol on loginProtocolPort 7171 (raw RSA private exponentiation over a 128-byte block with the datapack key.pem, then XTEA with the client key and Adler-32 checksums, src/server/network/protocol/protocollogin.cpp:125-135), so no HTTP login service is needed; allowOldProtocol=false; Canary accepts exactly CLIENT_VERSION 1511 (src/core.hpp:18), or 11.00 when allowOldProtocol is set; per-agent typed view (15x11 tiles) as the only observation; action-rate cap enforced at the protocol layer for parity; 2026-10-13 02:44 user: keep harnessing OTClient to the end (the baseline bots run as Lua inside it, and Spiral's Lua backend can run our policy there too); deferred until many parallel sessions are actually needed", Feature, P4, D6, 0u32, Paused, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD,SPIRAL-BIGNUM-MODEXP,TIBIA-TCP-BYTES", "tibia,protocol", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_headless_client () = Planning ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", Minutes 1800u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_headless_client_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: still deferred (user 2026-10-13: harness OTClient to the end); the OTClient harness now runs three competitors and two baselines, so there is no pressure to resume.")
inl note_of_tibia_headless_client_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", 2u32, "2026-10-22T03:38Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-21 23:38 Resume condition (retirement grooming; user 2026-10-13 'harness OTClient to the end'): every other TIBIA item is Done or Paused. Until then the OTClient harness carries the arena.")
inl note_of_tibia_headless_client_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", 3u32, "2026-10-23T11:11Z", "tibia-lane", "Retirement grooming 07:1x: outside the end estimate. The user decided OTClient to the end (10-13), so this chain (with TIBIA-GAME-HANDSHAKE, TIBIA-TCP-BYTES, SPIRAL-BIGNUM-MODEXP) does not gate retirement.")
inl tibia_oracle_rng () = Task ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", "Canary draws every random number from one global std::mt19937 seeded by std::random_device (src/utils/tools.cpp:449 getRandomGenerator; uniform_random/normal_random/boolean_random, 110 call sites in 18 files: combat.cpp 16, monster.cpp 17, game.cpp 13, ...); std::uniform_int_distribution is implementation-defined (MSVC and libstdc++ differ), so no simulator RNG can match it bit for bit: fidelity for RNG mechanics is distributional (sample each formula, compare with a goodness-of-fit test), and only deterministic mechanics are diffed exactly; a seed override (env var) in a locally built Canary still helps reproduce single scenarios; the C++ build is heavy (vcpkg), schedule it through the gate", TaskKind, P3, D4, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,oracle,canary", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_oracle_rng () = Planning ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", Minutes 300u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Pair)
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: re-checked against the local source: getRandomGenerator is still tools.cpp:449 in Canary 3.6.1. Distribution tests (PR-style) have replaced exact RNG diffs in practice; lowered to P3.")
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 2u32, "2026-10-20T15:41Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 11:41 first distributional fidelity check done without a seeded server: cyclops melee damage per landed hit, live 5204 values vs the model's charged/uncharged pmfs; the shape fits (chi-square 17.1 on 17 df fully charged), the mixture weight is the measurable difference (live 0.945 charged). Method: lab/tibia-potion-fidelity/charge_mix.py (MLE mixture weight + binned chi-square, cells with expected >= 5). Next candidates with the same method: knight hits on cyclops ('A cyclops loses N'), troll hits (PR-15 logs once run).")
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 3u32, "2026-10-20T15:43Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 11:43 second distributional check: knight melee on cyclops (lab/tibia-potion-fidelity/knight_fit.py on pr12-knight-landed.txt, 2427 landed hits from the 80 PR-12 logs, the 237 killing blows excluded as the last hit before each 'You gained' line because Canary caps them at the remaining health). Model roll (level 30, attack 21, axe 60, balanced 75%: raw 6..86, cyclops defense 20 and armor 20 always blocking): mean per landed hit 23.10, max 66; live 22.52, max 64; binned chi-square 13.1 on 15 df, so the formula and the monster block fit Canary. The offensive-mode alternative (raw max 113) is rejected (chi-square 1052.7 on 16 df), confirming both competitors fight balanced. Two of the model's RNG mechanics now pass a goodness-of-fit test against live; the only measured RNG-side difference is the block-charge share (note before).")
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 4u32, "2026-10-20T15:45Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 11:45 third distributional check: hunter hits on the knight (lab/tibia-potion-fidelity/hunter_fit.py on hunter-landed.txt, 518 landed hits from the 25 hunter logs of PR-13, the diagnostic block and PR-14). Model arrow: raw 0..100 truncated normal, no shield, armor 17 block: mean 40.57; live 39.58, max 87; chi-square 4.9 on 10 df. Mixture with uncharged melee 0..20: arrow share 1.000 (interval 0.980-1.000), so landed hunter damage is all arrows. The alternative where arrows meet the shield is rejected (model mean 32.74, chi-square 54.1 on 9 df), confirming the model's 'arrows skip the shield' rule (Canary combat type: distance hits bypass the shield block). Three RNG mechanics now pass: cyclops melee on the knight (shape), knight melee on cyclops, hunter arrows.")
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 5u32, "2026-10-20T20:36Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 16:36 fourth distributional check: knight melee on trolls (troll defense 10, armor 10) from the 10 PR-15 hunts: 107 non-lethal landed hits (142 killing blows excluded). A naive fit is badly off (model 33.04 vs live 24.02) because a 50 hp troll dies to most big hits, so the surviving hits are censored low; simulating whole troll fights in the model and keeping only non-lethal hits gives 24.89 vs 24.02, chi-square 11.4 on 7 df (lab/tibia-potion-fidelity/troll_censored_fit.py with knight_fit.py, args 'x 10 10'). Four RNG mechanics now fit live: cyclops melee on the knight (shape), knight melee on cyclops, knight melee on trolls (censored), hunter arrows. Remaining in this item: a seeded local Canary for single-scenario replays (heavy C++ build), not needed for distributional fidelity.")
inl note_of_tibia_oracle_rng_6 () = Note ("TIBIA-ORACLE-RNG", 6u32, "2026-10-21T02:01Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-20 22:01 grooming: closing. The item's own conclusion is that RNG fidelity is distributional; four mechanics now pass goodness-of-fit against live (cyclops melee shape, knight on cyclops, knight on trolls with censoring, hunter arrows), and the one measured difference (block-charge share) is tracked under TIBIA-POTION-FIDELITY. A seeded local Canary build is not needed for that and would cost a heavy C++ build; reopen only if a single-scenario replay becomes necessary.")
inl tibia_numeric_standard () = Task ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", "Server formulas computed in double are reimplemented as exact integer arithmetic so they stay bit-exact on CPU and on WGSL (no f64 there): first case 2026-10-12, Canary Weapons::getMaxWeaponDamage melee offensive std::round(0.085 * attackFactor * attackValue * attackSkill + level / 5) == (85*v*s*2 + 1000) / 2000 + level / 5 for every (value 1..120 step 7, skill 10..130 step 3, level 1/8/100/777) case, 2,788 combinations, 0 differences against a PowerShell double reference (apps/tibia/damage.spi); attackFactor is a float (1.2f is not 1.2), so balanced/defensive modes need the exact binary value of the factor as a rational and a sweep before use; overflow budget: products stay inside i32 for attack <= 200 and skill <= 150, larger formulas need u64 emulation on WGSL", Story, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-STANDARDS", "tibia,standards,wgsl", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_numeric_standard () = Planning ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", Minutes 300u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_numeric_standard_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: the only float left in apps/tibia is creatures.spi:37, Canary's step-speed formula 857.36*log(speed+261.29)-4795.01 in f64 (not WGSL-safe). Next: replace with an exact integer table over the speeds the arena uses, with a test against the f64 values.")
inl note_of_tibia_numeric_standard_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", 2u32, "2026-10-15T11:11Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:11 creatures.spi: canary_step_speed is now exact integer arithmetic (19 linear pieces over /4096, products < 5e6), equal to Canary's double formula for every speed 1..408 (canary_step_speed_exact_up_to; C test integer_step_speed_equals_canary_double_formula_for_every_speed_up_to_its_exact_limit, WGSL row integer_step_speed_on_gpu; creatures 8/8). The double formula survives only as that test's oracle. Melee max (damage.spi) replayed against Canary's doubles in Python over attack 1..200 x skill 1..150 x 3 modes x 5 levels: 450000 cases, 19 differ, all balanced-mode .5 ties where 0.085*0.75f in double lands just below (7 attack/skill pairs, attack 20/40/80 with skill 100/50/90/25/45/85/95); the simulated weapons (21/60, 20/30) never tie. Left: pin those tie pairs if a scenario ever uses them.")
inl note_of_tibia_numeric_standard_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-NUMERIC-STANDARD", 3u32, "2026-10-18T17:30Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 13:30 tie pairs characterized, closing. Recomputed against Canary's Weapons::getMaxWeaponDamage, std::round(0.085 * attackFactor(float) * value * skill + level / 5), over attack 1..200 x skill 1..150: exact .5 cases are offensive 635, balanced 229 and defensive 423, and doubles round them down only in balanced, at exactly 7 attack/skill pairs: 20/100, 40/50, 40/90, 80/25, 80/45, 80/85, 80/95. Across levels 1..2000 it depends on the level bonus: 20/100, 40/50 and 80/25 differ only at levels 1-4 (bonus 0); 40/90 and 80/45 at 108 levels up to 134; 80/95 at 112 up to 139; 80/85 at 316 up to 394. In between, adding the bonus sometimes lands the double exactly on .5. No rounding rule reproduces this short of emulating double arithmetic, and the difference is +1 max damage on pairs no scenario uses (the steel axe is attack 21, the knight level 8), so damage.spi keeps the exact-rational integer formula. Reopen only if a scenario puts a weapon of attack 20/40/80 on one of these skills.")
inl kino_shared_daemon_queue () = Task ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", "Every lane and session talks to one compile daemon on port 13905, which serializes compiles: concurrent Kino runs from different sessions queue behind each other (2026-10-12: two math runs waited ~20 min with no compiles logged while clients waited); options: per-session ports by default (SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER_PORT already exists), a daemon pool sized by free memory, or fair queuing per client; measure with xsim (several BEAMs sharing one daemon) before and after; user decision 2026-10-13 07:08: no model chosen up front; experiment with each (per-session ports, a memory-sized pool with fair queuing, one daemon with round-robin) under xsim load (several BEAMs, multiple lanes) and keep iterating until state of the art; measure wait time, throughput, peak memory per model; 2026-10-13 12:15 Kino lane measured four models with a load harness (3 BEAM sessions x 6 lib compiles, 3 in flight each, warm daemons, 2 rounds, machine shared with other lanes): one FIFO daemon 60-69 s wall, 0.26-0.30/s, queue p50 26.5 s, peak compiler 575-647 MB; per-session ports 44-48 s, 0.38-0.41/s, queue p50 9.6-13.3 s, peak 1.0-1.2 GB (plus a cold daemon per session); pool of 3 fair 41.3 s, 0.44/s, queue p50 9.8 s p95 13.1 s, peak 1.1 GB when memory allowed growth (round 2 under a parallel lib sweep stayed at 1 compiler by the free-memory gate: 103 s); round-robin on 1 compiler 54-87 s; unequal sessions (12 vs 2 vs 2 requests): light sessions finish at 12-17 s under FIFO and fair alike (a session never has more than its own concurrency in flight), fair finished the heavy one 4-12 s earlier; decision: one daemon with a memory-sized pool (up to 3 compilers, a new one only when free memory >= SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_SERVER_MB 1000 + SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_RESERVE_MB 1500) and fair per-client queues, now the default (SPIRAL_KINO_DAEMON_POOL=off|N|auto); per-worker recycle cap = max(2500/workers, 1200) MB; retire waits for queued and running pool compiles and stops the extra compilers; clients send their OS pid as the client id; tests in compiler_pool_test.exs; 2026-10-13 12:19 end-to-end with the default (pool auto): 18/18 in 49 s, 0.37/s, queue p50 10.5 s, peak 1.09 GB (grew to 3 compilers at 4.6-5.5 GB free); retire stopped all 3 compilers (no orphans)", TaskKind, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "KINO-DAEMON-MEMORY", "kino,perf,daemon", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_shared_daemon_queue () = Planning ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", Minutes 240u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kino_shared_daemon_queue_1 () = Note ("KINO-SHARED-DAEMON-QUEUE", 1u32, "2026-10-16T03:11Z", "claude", "(2026-10-15 23:11 -04:00, Claude b7595ac3) the xsim measurements now live in the i574n/x repo (apps/sim). Kino test runs from a sibling repo work with SPIRAL_KINO_COMPILER=process (no daemon left behind).")
inl kino_memo_key_scope () = Task ("KINO-MEMO-KEY-SCOPE", "Memo key scope (tibia lane measurement 2026-10-12: second pass mostly missed): package prints by size+mtime of every .spi in an included dir and an md5 of every Kino module invalidated far too much; 17:30 Kino lane, in apps/kino memo.ex (uncommitted): a package enters the key as sha256 of package.spiproj + content of exactly the listed modules (folder entries + children, .spi and .spir) + path dependencies recursively, test blocks included (correctness first), core package the same way; unlisted files/size/mtime no longer matter; Kino identity = md5 of result-path modules only (Spiral.Kino, Builders, Cell, Directives, Display, Domain + Gleam domain beam, Memo, Mounts, Notebook, Result, Runner, Targets, Toolchain), excluding SmartCell, Document, CompilerClient/Daemon, Fsi*, Slots, FileLock, mix tasks; memo_test.exs covers unlisted-file edit keeps the key, listed module/folder module/project edit changes it; entries written before miss once; correction: the landing note above is from 17:14, not 17:30; verified by the tibia lane (port 13935): fill hunt 36.2 s / hunt_sim 27.3 s; touching the unlisted wire.spi (content + mtime) -> hunt 6.8 s memo_hits 4/4, hunt_sim 6.4 s 5/5; touching the listed geometry.spi (trailing newline) -> hunt memo_hits 0, 33.2 s; whitespace-only edits invalidate (safe; a token-level hash is a possible later refinement)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,perf,memo", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_memo_key_scope () = Planning ("KINO-MEMO-KEY-SCOPE", Minutes 90u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_kino_memo_key_scope_1 () = Note ("KINO-MEMO-KEY-SCOPE", 1u32, "2026-10-14T23:20Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-14 19:20 Tibia lane observation: apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi reported 22 memo hits of 24 right after hunting_pack.spi (a module the tests open) gained a new function, so the memo key seems to leave out the content of opened package modules; a test whose own text is unchanged could pass from memo after its dependency changed behavior. Today's SPIRAL_KINO_MEMO=0 rerun was also 24/24, so no wrong pass here. Worth checking whether dependency modules are part of the key.")
inl kino_not_run_reason () = Task ("KINO-NOT-RUN-REASON", "When a test in a --test list fails, later tests are reported not_run (fail-fast) without saying why; the report row should carry the reason (e.g. \"not_run: stopped after <test> failed\") (tibia lane, 2026-10-12); 20:46 done (uncommitted): every not_run row carries reason: 'the run stopped before this test: <first line of the error>' or 'no step ran for this cell'", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,tests,report", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_kino_not_run_reason () = Planning ("KINO-NOT-RUN-REASON", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_offscreen_probes () = Task ("TIBIA-OFFSCREEN-PROBES", "Scripted OTClient probes as the first arena harness, all in C:\\Users\\i574n\\tibia-local (outside the repos): run-offscreen.ps1 starts the client on a separate Windows desktop (CreateDesktop + CreateProcess lpDesktop, nothing visible; window hide from Lua is not enough, the engine re-shows it), muted (enableAudio false in config.otml plus g_sounds.setAudioEnabled(false)); run-probe.ps1 swaps otclientrc.lua with a probe script; probes log to %APPDATA%\\otcr\\otclient\\otclient\\tibia-probe.log; 2026-10-12: probe-summon.lua (GOD: /pos 1932, 1352, 7 then /m green frog,3,,2) and probe-hunt.lua (Knight Sample attacks the nearest monster with chase mode, path-walks with player:autoWalk while refused) killed a green frog: loot 8 christmas tokens, knight 185 -> 10 health (unarmed, 5 frogs); next: port the probe logic to the Spiral headless client and log structured events instead of text; 2026-10-13 06:14 in daily use: run-probe.ps1 / run-policy-scenario.ps1 run policy, measure and step probes off-screen and muted; the scenario script restarts the world, resets the character offline and stops canary at the end", Feature, P1, D4, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,client,harness", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_offscreen_probes () = Planning ("TIBIA-OFFSCREEN-PROBES", Minutes 600u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_login_15x () = Task ("TIBIA-LOGIN-15X", "Canary 3.6.1 classic login (port 7171) rejects every client except the old 11.00 protocol (protocollogin.cpp getCharacterList: `else if (!oldProtocol) disconnectClient`), and OTClient reports it only as a lost connection (ERROR 10054); 15.11 clients log in over HTTP (login.php, not part of Canary) and then present the session key, which Canary builds as `email + \"\\n\" + password`; the probes skip the HTTP service and call g_game.loginWorld('@god', 'god', 'OTServBR-Global', '127.0.0.1', 7172, character, '', '@god\\ngod') directly; modern accounts log in by email ('@god' in schema.sql); write a tiny local login service (Spiral) when several accounts are needed; 2026-10-13 06:14 solved since 2026-10-12: direct g_game.loginWorld on the game port with session key '@god\\ngod', used by every probe", TaskKind, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,protocol", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_login_15x () = Planning ("TIBIA-LOGIN-15X", Minutes 180u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl tibia_canary_pitfalls () = Task ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", "Canary setup pitfalls found 2026-10-12: scoop lua51 sets LUA_PATH/LUA_CPATH, which override Canary's require paths (\"no field package.preload['data-otservbr-global.lib.core.quests']\"), so clear them for canary.exe (tibia-local/world.ps1 does); the release zip holds only canary.exe/pdb, the datapack comes from the v3.6.1 source tag; the global datapack (otservbr.otbm, 176 MB) needs well over 1.2 GB while loading, the small data-canary datapack (canary.otbm 18.8 MB, 67 monster types, no rat, no spawns) starts in 30 s at 112 MB and suits arena scenarios that define their own spawns; /m on the player's own tile fails in the temple (\"There is not enough room\"), the radius form /m name,count,,radius places monsters around; experience stayed 4200 after a kill because data-canary green_frog.lua sets monster.experience = 0; its targetDistance = 6 makes it keep six tiles away, which looked like fleeing in the probes (health 25, melee 0..25 every 2000 ms before armor, observed hits 2..12): pick arena creatures with targetDistance 1 and non-zero experience, and treat each creature's Lua definition as the oracle for the simulator's creature table", TaskKind, P3, D1, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-LOCAL-WORLD", "tibia,canary", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls () = Planning ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: new pitfalls from 2026-10-15: (1) any follow packet clears the player's attack target without telling the client (Game::playerFollowCreature); (2) with classicAttackSpeed=false a player step cancels the scheduled swing (Player::onWalk, PC-3); (3) OTClient Redemption crashes (0xC0000374) on native nested dofile and on errors under pcall around it in the bot sandbox; (4) a scenario exception leaves canary.exe running and run-arena hangs on the inherited pipe.")
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 2u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 biggest pitfall of the day, login protection: Canary 3.6.1 keeps monsters off a fresh login for 10 s (loginProtectionTime) and ends it on the player's own move, auto-walk, turn, speech, item use or attack cancel (Game::playerMove/playerAutoWalk/playerTurn/playerSay/playerUseItem*/playerSetAttackedCreature with id 0); starting an attack does not. A probe that only attacks keeps it, bots that turn or talk lose it, and the difference decided PR-9. Harness now ends it for everyone (parity.lua).")
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 3u32, "2026-10-15T22:49Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 18:49 ramps: stepping onto a tile whose item has a floorchange direction (e.g. item 6913 'ramp', floorchange south at 1940,1372,7) moves the walker one floor up and one tile on (to 1940,1373,6); monsters only target players on their own floor, so a retreat onto a ramp ends the fight. otbm-walkability.py --items-xml/--floor-changes lists such tiles; mind self-closing <item/> tags when parsing items.xml.")
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_4 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 4u32, "2026-10-18T16:11Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 12:11 status of each pitfall, where it lives in code: LUA_PATH/LUA_CPATH are cleared in tibia-local world.ps1 and live/run-policy-scenario.ps1; the arena creature rules (targetDistance 1, non-zero experience) and the creature tables are typed in src/creatures.spi with Canary-data tests; follow-clears-target, the step-cancels-swing rule and the dofile crash are handled in the probes and run-policy-scenario.ps1 (the pcall(dofile) shim). Fixed now (uncommitted, not yet run live): pitfall 4. run-policy-scenario.ps1 started canary.exe and only stopped it at the end, so a throw anywhere between (login timeout, probe error, bot seeding) left canary running holding run-arena's inherited pipe. Everything after the start is now in try/finally, and the finally restores otclientrc.lua and stops canary (whitespace-ignoring diff: +4 -1, parses). The remaining text is knowledge already in the tibia memory and code, so this item can close once a live block confirms the finally path.")
inl note_of_tibia_canary_pitfalls_5 () = Note ("TIBIA-CANARY-PITFALLS", 5u32, "2026-10-18T19:42Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 15:42 pitfall 4 fix verified live (lab/tibia-start-sync/stray-canary-check.ps1): with the OTClient exe renamed away, run-policy-scenario.ps1 brought the world online, then failed at run-offscreen's CreateProcess (error 2) inside the new try; the finally stopped canary (no canary process left) and restored otclientrc.lua; the script renames the exe back in its own finally. Every pitfall now lives in code, tests or memory, so closing.")
inl tibia_fidelity_walk () = Task ("TIBIA-FIDELITY-WALK", "First oracle-backed test: apps/tibia/geometry.spi steps_match_canary_walk_probe_2026_10_12 pins the server-confirmed positions of a N/E/S/W walk from (1942, 1346, 7) (north y-1, east x+1, south y+1, west x-1); run it once Kino is available again; collect more probe traces (diagonal steps, floor changes, blocked tiles) the same way; 2026-10-13 06:14 N/E/S/W and diagonal steps pinned from server-confirmed probes (geometry.spi); floor changes and blocked tiles not yet measured", TaskKind, P2, D1, 100u32, Done, "TIBIA-TYPED-RULES", "tibia,oracle", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_fidelity_walk () = Planning ("TIBIA-FIDELITY-WALK", Minutes 15u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_walk_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY-WALK", 1u32, "2026-10-15T11:00Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 07:00 grooming: blocked tiles are now covered by live checks (PC-1: a cyclops routes around a wall exactly as the router predicts); floor changes are the only unmeasured case left.")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_walk_2 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY-WALK", 2u32, "2026-10-15T14:10Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-15 10:10 first live floor change seen (by accident, PC-3 run 3): stepping onto the ramp at 1940,1372,7 (item 6913, floorchange south) put the knight at 1940,1373,6. otbm-walkability.py now lists floor-change tiles (--items-xml/--floor-changes).")
inl note_of_tibia_fidelity_walk_3 () = Note ("TIBIA-FIDELITY-WALK", 3u32, "2026-10-18T17:28Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-18 13:28 floor changes pinned: geometry.spi models Canary's up-ramp rule from Tile::queryDestination (TILESTATE_FLOORCHANGE: z-1, then north y-1, south y+1, east x+1, west x-1, south_alt y+2, east_alt x+2) as union up_ramp plus climbed. Test stepping_onto_the_south_ramp_matches_the_live_floor_change_2026_10_15 pins the live observation (onto 1940,1372,7, landed 1940,1373,6), and every_up_ramp_climbs_one_floor_and_shifts_like_canary_query_destination covers the other five shifts. geometry 13/13 through scripts/build.ps1. Blocked tiles were already measured: terrain comes from the server map and was checked against the live client scan (251/252 cells), and terrain.spi pins the arena ramps as walls for monsters. The down branch (holes, which depends on the tile below) is not modeled, because no scenario has one. Closing.")
inl tibia_game_handshake () = Task ("TIBIA-GAME-HANDSHAKE", "First game-port message for the Spiral headless client, from Canary 3.6.1 protocolgame.cpp:814-900: u16 operating system, u16 protocol version (1511), u32 client version, string client version, string asset hash (version >= 1334), u8 preview state, then an RSA block with the XTEA key (4 x u32), u8 game-master flag, string session key (email + \"\\n\" + password, split unless authType is \"session\"), string character name; checksum method is sequence numbers when the declared OS is an OTClient one (<= CLIENTOS_OTCLIENT_MAC) and Adler-32 otherwise (old protocol always Adler-32); apps/tibia/wire.spi (2026-10-12) already has XTEA encrypt/decrypt (published vector 497df3d072612cb5) and Adler-32 (Wikipedia = 0x11E60398) in u32 arithmetic, and the same XTEA loop reproduces the published vector on WGSL (spiral-wgsl) and C, Adler-32 steps too (probe 2026-10-12); missing: byte buffers (needs arrays), RSA raw exponentiation with key.pem (bignum), TCP", TaskKind, P4, D4, 0u32, Paused, "TIBIA-HEADLESS-CLIENT", "tibia,protocol,spiral", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_tibia_game_handshake () = Planning ("TIBIA-GAME-HANDSHAKE", Minutes 480u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
