inl eoie_friction_2026_10_12 () = Task ("EOIE-FRICTION-2026-10-12", "eoie friction found by the eoie lane 2026-10-12: fs-write lacks create-or-replace; the corrected: line of fs-write/text-replace repeats usage instead of a corrected command; source-stats lacks a per-crate line breakdown (gate headroom unreadable); migrate-tags --dry-run is classified as a mutation and blocked by an expired lease; no dyn in no-core packages; migrate-tags dry run: one line in src/command_spec_domain/model.spi (add agile:migrate-tags/1| to the inspection list in command_subcommand_effect_code) makes a root-only migrate-tags an inspection; an explicit --dry-run still reads arg 3 (the root) as the mode, so move the flag before the root or use a typed subcommand (migrate-tags preview|apply <root>); needs a command_spec_domain regen, CLI build and renewal; user decision 2026-10-12 19:00: typed subcommands migrate-tags preview <root> (inspection) and migrate-tags apply <root> (mutation); 2026-10-13 13:08 Kino lane: migrate-tags is now typed (user decision 19:00): eoie agile migrate-tags preview <root> (an inspection: agile:migrate-tags:preview in the command spec's Inspect list, receipt 'preview') and migrate-tags apply <root>; the old <root> [--dry-run|--apply] forms are rejected with the new usage; edits in agile_planning_migration, eoie_agile_mutation (usage + operand shape), command_spec_domain (help + effect); planning_cli test uses the typed forms; dev.ps1 regenerated and tested the 4 owners, published, build.ps1 published eoie.exe 13:07; left: fs-write create-or-replace, corrected: line, source-stats per-crate breakdown, dyn in no-core packages; 2026-10-13 15:28 fs-write create-or-replace done: eoie proxy fs-write <root> <relative> --create-or-replace [--] <text> writes whether or not the file exists (receipt mode=create|replace, create_or_replace=1); the write decision moved out of the legacy blob into native Spiral (legacy_operations_entry/entry.spi: proxy_write_action union over typed flags, exported proxy_write_action_binding; the blob only parses, does IO and maps the action); --expect-hash/--expect-nonempty still require an existing file, --expect-nonempty still rejects an empty target; usage in the command spec and the blob; CLI regression test in eoie_cli/tests/windows.rs (kept to one line for the 1000-line crate gate); dev.ps1 published 3 owners, build.ps1 published eoie.exe; 2026-10-13 15:33 the fs-write CLI tests moved out of eoie_cli into a new Spiral-authored contract crate src/eoie_fs_write_contracts (main.spi -> fs_write_contracts.rs, test-requires-cli, workspace member, Cargo.lock entry) with three normally formatted tests (create-or-replace creates then replaces, a plain write still refuses with a hint, the guards hold); eoie_cli/tests/windows.rs back to its original; build.ps1 -Test eoie-fs-write-contracts + eoie-cli: 3/3 + 4/4, topology gate passed; 2026-10-13 16:05 corrected: line done: proxy failures now print a runnable corrected command built from the user's own argv when a repair is known (typed proxy_repair union in proxy_failure_classification: AddCreateOrReplace for a refused fs-write overwrite, inserting -- when the payload followed directly; ExpectObservedMatches N for a text-replace count mismatch, dropping the flags when N=1); words are PowerShell-quoted ('it''s two words'); unknown failures keep the usage template; the contract crate is now src/eoie_proxy_edit_contracts (6 tests incl. re-running the suggested fs-write); source-stats per-crate breakdown done: eoie proxy source-stats <root> --crates prints crate=<path> lines=N headroom=1000-N sorted by size (crate_headroom_binding in eoie_source_topology_core model); found and fixed a source-stats bug on the way: an untagged target dir beside a Cargo.toml (eoie's own src/target) was walked as source, so source-stats crashed mid-build on vanishing rlibs and counted build output; build_cache_evidence union (CacheDirTagged | TargetBesideCargoManifest) now skips it, regression test ownership::an_untagged_target_beside_a_cargo_manifest_is_a_build_cache; help_catalog expectation updated; dev.ps1 published 5 owners, build.ps1 -Test (contracts 6/6, cli 4/4, topology 11/11, command spec 3/3) published eoie.exe; left: dyn in no-core packages (compiler side); 2026-10-13 16:40 gate-headroom split (main's ask): eoie_contracts 999->587 (agile CLI contracts -> new src/eoie_agile_contracts 234: agile_cache, agile_listing; release contracts -> new src/eoie_release_contracts 200: self_upgrade, hygiene_confinement with the eoie-release-hygiene dev-dep), eoie_agile_state 998->510 (the pure typed decisions -> new src/agile_state_decision_domain 502: entry kind, transient names, record catalog/preflight, attestation decision, series bindings; the state runtime imports them in its one import blob), eoie_cli 998->528 (the CLI no longer inlines bootstrap_policy's authority contracts; new src/bootstrap_authority_status 522 exports the five statuses and the CLI links it; bootstrap_policy itself unchanged at 391); dev.ps1 published 8 owners, build.ps1 -Test green incl. eoie-contracts 8 passed/7 ignored, agile 7, release 4, cli 4; topology gate passed; eoie status ok migration=987; 30 crates still have under 200 lines of headroom (top: predicate_lex_domain 996, rust_std_fs_mutation 995, patch_compat_driver 993); 2026-10-13 19:33 more gate headroom splits: predicate_lex_domain 996 -> 623 (string-literal lexing and encoding moved to new src/predicate_literal_domain 393; predicate_lex macros point there; 4 consumer crates depend on it; 8 owners regenerated and published), eoie_handoff 982 -> 772 (the typed-predicate differential tests moved to new src/typed_predicate_contracts 210, a test-only Spiral package depending on eoie-handoff); rust_std_fs_mutation (995) left alone: one module whose sections share private helpers and whose Windows tests exercise private functions; build.ps1 -Test green and topology gate passed for both; 2026-10-13 23:57 sweep lane: the last point (dyn in no-core packages) needs no compiler change: core's dyn is just inl dyn ~x = x (VS Code Plugin/core/core.spi:65) and the ~ dyn pattern is parser-level, so it works without core both as a parameter (agile_lease_terms/terms.spi:11-12, package depends only on rust_std_string, which has no packages) and as a body binding (backup_domain/main.spi:281-283 inl ~next = 0i32, package.spiproj has no packages at all); both crates build in eoie CI (run 38327253830 green on windows and ubuntu); write ~x or a local inl dyn ~x = x in a no-core package; 2026-10-14 00:22 follow-up from eoie CI 38508234661 (windows red, 3 of 6 proxy edit contracts): the corrected: command quoted any word with ~, so the runner temp root C:\\Users\\RUNNER~1\\... came back as '...' while the tests expect it bare; proxy_words (failure_classification.spi:35) now treats ~ as plain except as a word's first char (a leading ~ would expand to home in PowerShell on Unix); the contract temp roots are named eoie-proxy-edit~<label>-... so the local run covers the runner's 8.3 path shape; dev.ps1 -Package proxy-failure-classification,eoie-proxy-edit-contracts -Offline -Publish: 6/6 passed, 2 owners published (uncommitted); eoie.exe itself not republished (next build.ps1)", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "eoie,dogfood", "current", "current")
