inl alphabet_readme_hangul_pdf () = Task ("ALPHABET-README-HANGUL-PDF", "README.hangul.md.pdf is never produced in alphabet apps/documents (pre-existing, same under xelatex and tectonic): LaTeX stops with \"There's no line here to end\" at a generated \\\\ line break; find which crowbook markdown construct emits a bare \\\\ (likely an empty line or a hard break in the Hangul README) and fix the source or the template; 2026-10-14 03:08 lane 1: cause: documents.spi hangul interleaves every non-empty line with its hangulize transliteration, fence lines included, so a code block became the fence pair '`포웨르제우' + '`powershell' and each original code line twice; the stray fences shift which lines are code, one block starts with an empty line, crowbook emits {\\sloppy \\\\{} and LaTeX stops (result.tex:289 There's no line here to end), on xelatex and tectonic alike; fix (uncommitted, apps/documents/documents.spi hangul fold): fence lines and lines inside a fenced block are copied once, untransliterated (the hangulize output index still advances, so the following lines stay aligned); proof: the fixed binary (compiled from the .spi into a scratch crate) turns alphabet README.md into README.hangul.md.pdf (65124 B, tectonic, 53 s for the whole sample), and crowbook on the new README.hangul.md produces a PDF with tex.command xelatex (64781 B) and tectonic (65120 B) while the old README.hangul.md fails on xelatex too; nota.hangul.md stays byte-identical to build.ps1's expectation; build.ps1's sample run now also requires <name>.hangul.md.pdf (README and nota both produced); needs the NanumGothicCoding font, which Linux CI installs (fonts-nanum-coding) and Windows CI gets from the uncommitted alphabet scripts/init.ps1 change; documents.livemd is not updated (the .spi is the source now and the livemd is pending deletion)", TaskKind, P3, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "alphabet,documents", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_alphabet_readme_hangul_pdf () = Planning ("ALPHABET-README-HANGUL-PDF", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl spiral_cli_output_normal () = Task ("SPIRAL-CLI-OUTPUT-NORMAL", "Make the spiral <target> CLI (apps/spiral) report program output uniformly so Kino cross-target agreement needs no normalizing (found by the Kino lane 20:46): gleam runs return an empty output (program stdout lost, so agreement cannot check gleam), lua output is Debug-formatted (String(\"...\")), cuda/python append main's return value, fsharp prints +1.570796 style floats; target: raw program stdout per target, the return value reported separately; 21:16: also process_gleam assumes the source dir's parent is the package dir and the CLI exits 0 when gleam run fails (the root of KINO-GLEAM-FALSE-PASS); the CLI must propagate target failures as a non-zero exit; 22:03: also -t javascript never runs (process_gleam only bundles); 00:57 CLI parts done by the Kino lane (uncommitted): lua print/return values use Lua tostring and tab-joined args (print('x', 6*7) -> x<TAB>42); process_gleam failwiths (exit 101 + message) when gleam run fails; edits in apps/spiral/spiral.livemd via mix spiral.edit, spiral.spi re-exported, spiral.rs regenerated (~16k-line diff, mostly compiler drift: review before commit); new lua run check in apps/spiral/build.ps1 (spiral-check-lua<TAB>42), build.ps1 -fast RUST-OK; left: process_gleam's package dir = parent of the source dir (Kino no longer depends on it); 2026-10-13 13:42 Kino lane: process_gleam uses <source dir>/gleam_package (with src/main.gleam copied in) when the source is not inside a src/ directory, instead of writing gleam.toml into the parent of the source dir; erlang runs build first and then run, so the output is the program's stdout only (no dependency compile warnings); new apps/spiral/build.ps1 gleam run check expects exactly 'spiral-check-gleam 42' (scoop Erlang first on PATH for the checks: choco OTP 26 crashes gleam with a corrupt atom table); CLI rebuilt, RUST-OK, shipped; left: the cuda/python trailing main value (Python backend codegen) and fsharp float formatting (lib); 2026-10-13 14:39 the cuda/python trailing main value was Kino's own Cell.patch_python (it rewrote the python entry to print main's result for value cells); Kino test cells now keep the compiler's entry, a cuda test prints only its assertions; left: F# float format; 2026-10-13 15:24 F# float format done in lib (sm'_real format_real): floats render as the shortest round-trip decimal with .0 for integral values and NaN/Infinity/-Infinity on fsharp, rust, python/cuda, typescript, lua (gleam already did); test sm' show_floats one exact string on 6 targets; sm' 36/36, math 14/14, physics 39/39, date_time 32/32, common 5/5; C/Zig/Lean/Delphi keep their old float text; 2026-10-13 18:05 canonical floats now on every backend: C (shortest %.*g checked by strtod/strtof), Zig ({d} plus .0), Lean (one-line Id.run do, Float.ofScientific round-trip check, f32 via toFloat32; probe run with lean +leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0-rc4 --run), Delphi (global SpiralFormatFloat: FloatToStrF ffGeneral 1..17 digits until StrToFloat reads back; the old inline-if arm did not compile under fpc); show_floats asserts one string on 9 Kino targets (gleam, lua, fsharp, cuda, rust, typescript, c, zig, delphi); landed after packs 3+4 bless", TaskKind, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "spiral-cli,kino,backends", "current", "current")
