inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_3 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 3u32, "2026-10-17T10:02Z", "main-thread", "06:02 main-thread night repro attempt on tonight Kino (package outside the tree, modules pack_sim then pack, open pack and pack.troll): passes with memo off and on (second run 2 hits). Still blocked on the Tibia session exact command.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_4 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 4u32, "2026-10-19T12:43Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 08:43 helper-lane lap 1: turned the blocker (waiting for the tibia lane's exact command) into a self-serve check: tibia/src/package.spiproj still carries the workaround (module hunting_pack, 5 qualified uses; pack_sim.spi is the notebook stem), and every synthetic repro since 10-13 passed. lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run.ps1 copies tibia/src's .spi/.spiproj into a cache probe dir named src, renames hunting_pack back to pack (file and every mention), runs Cells on pack_sim.spi exactly like the blog/x runners (process compiler, no warm), and counts UnboundModule lines; the tibia tree itself is only read. HEAVY QUEUE: C:\\home\\git\\spiral\\lab\\KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND\\run.ps1 (~15 min). 0 UnboundModule means the bug is gone on the real tree and the item can close; a hit gives the exact failing state.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_5 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 5u32, "2026-10-19T13:28Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 09:28 helper-lane lap 2: reviewed the existing regression test (notebook_report_test.exs:640, a package module named like a prefix of the notebook's stem stays in the test program): it runs with a stub compile function and only asserts that the generated program text contains open pack, so it cannot see a compiler-side resolution failure (ETY-UnboundModule comes from the real compiler resolving the package's module list, where the 10-13 case had pack listed last). That is why the real-compiler probe queued in lap 1 (lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run.ps1 on a renamed copy of tibia/src) is the meaningful check, and why the stub test passing since 10-13 never settled the item.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_6 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 6u32, "2026-10-19T14:25Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:25 main heavy queue: run.ps1 threw before probing (Join-Path on an empty Split-Path for a top-level src file); fixed line 7 in the lab script (top-level hunting_pack.spi maps to pack.spi) and requeued in main's queue 2.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_7 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 7u32, "2026-10-19T14:49Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:49 main heavy queue 2 ran the fixed run.ps1 (10:45-10:46): the 10-13 bug still reproduces on a renamed copy of the real tibia tree: probes/prefix-module-20261019-1045/src/pack_sim.spi:3:10 ETY-UnboundModule (plus a follow-on _assert_eq unbound at 16:88), UnboundModule lines 1; so the item stays Blocked on a Cells or compiler fix for a package module whose name is a prefix of another (pack vs pack_sim).")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_8 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 8u32, "2026-10-19T15:08Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:08 helper-lane lap 3: the 10:49 reproduction is not evidence for the prefix bug: run.ps1 now takes -Control (copy without the hunting_pack -> pack rename), and the control copy in the same cache probes folder fails IDENTICALLY (lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run-control-20261019-1104.log: pack_sim.spi:3:10 ETY-UnboundModule on the static prelude's open testing, then _assert_eq unbound at 16:88; 24 of 31 tests failed). open testing resolves through the spiral lib package Cells mounts for the tree, and a copy under spiral-bin/probes cannot reach it, so the unbound module is the probe's location, not the module name. run.ps1 also takes -InTree (copy under the lab folder, where lib resolves); an in-tree control started compiling for real and passed the 150 s bound (pack_sim declares --timeout 1800000), so both in-tree variants go to the heavy queue. Status back to Active: blocked only on that measurement, not on a fix.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_9 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 9u32, "2026-10-19T15:09Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 11:09 correction to main's note 7: that run does not show the prefix bug; helper lane 1's control (same copy without the rename, run-control-20261019-1104.log) fails identically, because a copy under spiral-bin/probes cannot reach the spiral lib package (open testing unbound). The in-tree pair (-InTree, with and without -Control) after the switch accept is the real test.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_10 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 10u32, "2026-10-19T15:37Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 11:37 helper-lane lap 4: found the Cells-side guard already in the tree: notebook_report_test.exs line 700 (a package module named like a prefix of the notebook's stem stays in the test program, committed in 59b477ba on 10-17) builds exactly the reported shape - package module pack, notebook pack_sim.spi with a static prelude opening testing and a test that opens pack - and asserts the generated test program keeps the line open pack and passes. That covers the Cells text path with a stubbed compiler; what is left unproven is only the real-compiler run, which the queued in-tree pair (run.ps1 -InTree and -InTree -Control) decides. If both in-tree runs pass, the item closes as fixed by 59b477ba plus that evidence.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_11 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 11u32, "2026-10-19T21:54Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 17:54 helper-lane: the in-tree pair (lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/run.ps1 -InTree, with lib reachable, on the installed pack 10 compiler) reproduces the bug with the real compiler. The copy with hunting_pack renamed to pack fails 22 of 31 tests on c with main.spi:5:6 ETY-UnboundModule in open pack (run-20261019-1742.log). The unrenamed control passes 31 of 31 (run-control-20261019-1745.log). So 59b477ba's stubbed Cells test does not cover it: the text keeps open pack, but the module is still unbound at compile time. Next: separate prefix from name with a minimal package (module pack plus a notebook named other.spi, and the same with pack_sim.spi), to tell a stem-prefix filter from a clash with the name pack.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_12 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 12u32, "2026-10-19T22:06Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:06 helper-lane lap 6: narrowed to a cross-cell effect of a Rust target. It is not the module name and not the stem prefix alone. Minimal packages (module pack with notebooks other.spi and pack_sim.spi, with and without a type pack, and with a rust+c cell between two c cells) all pass. On the real tibia package with hunting_pack renamed to pack: current_first_targeting alone on c passes; after cyclops_hits (c only) it passes; after golden_seed_7_troll_pack (///> rust + ///> c, both pass) it fails with main.spi:5:6 ETY-UnboundModule open pack (prefix-two, 1 of 2). In the full run, every c test after that rust cell fails the same way. The cell dirs are fresh tmp dirs, the src dir gains no files, and the failing c compile is faster (8 s vs 15 s), so some cache shared across cells after a Rust compile of this package drops module pack, while hunting_pack survives. Repro: lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/one-run.ps1, which rebuilds the copies via make-variants.ps1 (copies removed after each run). Next: find the cache, either the compiler's package cache keyed by path or a mount reused by the rust patch step, by diffing spiral-bin cache dirs before and after the rust cell.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_13 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 13u32, "2026-10-19T22:10Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:10 helper-lane: correction to the 18:06 note. The Rust target is not involved. lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/one-run.ps1 -Only prefix-two-c -NoMemo (golden_seed_7 with only ///> c, then current_first_targeting, Cells memo off) still fails the second test with main.spi:5:6 open pack unbound. prefix-two fails the same way with the memo off, so the compile memo is ruled out. prefix-one (current_first alone) passes, and so does prefix-c-two (cyclops_hits, which only uses pack qualified, then current_first). So the trigger is a previous cell in the same notebook run that also opens pack. The minimal packages with two c cells that both open pack do not reproduce, so it also needs something in the tibia package (27 modules, or a module or term that the earlier cell's program pulls in). Next: capture the failing cell's generated main.spi (keep the cell tmp dir), and bisect the tibia package's modules list.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_14 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 14u32, "2026-10-19T22:35Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 18:35 helper-lane: ROOT CAUSE found; the module-name prefix was a red herring. I captured the cell programs with lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/keep-notebook.ps1 plus keep.exs, which run Notebook.run_report with keep_files: true. The failing program begins with open pack and open creatures copied from the previous test's body, ahead of the static prelude and the test's own open pack. Two things combine. (1) Cells: apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi line 263, the test = 1 branch of walk, merges a test cell's opens (cell_opens) into the opens of every later program (since feb8b9f7, 10-12), so a test's local open leaks into all later tests. (2) Compiler: tibia's module pack defines type pack, and after one open pack the second open pack resolves pack to the opened type rather than the module, which gives ETY-UnboundModule. hunting_pack never collided, which is why the rename fixed it. Minimal repro without tibia: lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/minimal/g_typed_twice (module pack with type pack, two c tests that each open pack): second_open fails with unbound=1, while h_plain_twice (no type pack) passes 2 of 2 (minimal-run.ps1). Fix staged: lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/test_opens_patch.py (apps/cells, --apply gated, dry run OK) keeps test opens local: the test body already carries them through scoped_test_body, and prelude opens still flow through the static defs branch. It goes to lane 2 via main, with g_typed_twice as the regression case. The compiler half, a module and a type sharing a name across open, stays a separate small item if wanted.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_15 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 15u32, "2026-10-20T00:24Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 20:24 helper-lane: the Cells fix is in the tree (uncommitted). In a Cells idle window I applied lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/test_opens_patch.py: apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi line 263, where a test cell's opens no longer merge into later programs. Before keeping it, mix test with the patch (cells-window-20261019-1946.log, per-run MIX_BUILD_PATH) ran notebook_report_test, notebook_targets_test and the new crates case: 36 passed. The runner misread the new ExUnit summary format (Result: 36 passed) as a failure and reverted once; it was re-applied by hand at about 20:10 and the check is fixed. On the patched Cells, the minimal repro passes (minimal-run.ps1 at about 20:25): g_typed_twice is now 2 of 2, where second_open failed with ETY-UnboundModule before, and h_plain_twice is 2 of 2. The tibia prefix-two case and the lib gates for testing, conversation and reactors are queued (after-patch-gates.ps1); Done once those pass.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_16 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 16u32, "2026-10-20T00:35Z", "helper-lane", "2026-10-19 20:35 helper-lane: Done. On the patched Cells (test opens stay local; apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi line 263, uncommitted, for the user's commit), lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND/after-patch-gates.ps1 passes the original tibia case: the tibia package with hunting_pack renamed back to pack runs golden_seed_7 then current_first_targeting, 2 of 2, unbound 0, where the second failed with ETY-UnboundModule open pack before. The minimal repro g_typed_twice is 2 of 2. No regression in the lib gates run on the patched Cells: testing 7 of 7, conversation 2 of 2, reactors 8 of 8. mix test was 36 passed. Cause recap: Cells leaked each test's open lines into every later test program, and tibia's module pack defines type pack, so a repeated open pack resolved to the type. The compiler side (a module and a same-named type colliding on a second open in one program) is not hit by Cells anymore; it can be filed separately if it matters in hand-written code.")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_17 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 17u32, "2026-10-22T03:36Z", "main", "23:36 lab drain: the fix lives in apps/cells/spi/notebook.spi (now line 328 after reformatting: elif test = 1i32 then walk ... opens ... unchanged, no merge opens cell_opens site left; staged by the user). The folder held the patch script, Cells window logs and the two minimal repros (g_typed_twice, h_plain_twice); their outcomes (2 of 2, unbound 0, 36 passed) are in the notes above. Removed spiral/lab/KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND (33 files).")
inl note_of_kino_prefix_module_unbound_18 () = Note ("KINO-PREFIX-MODULE-UNBOUND", 18u32, "2026-10-24T11:49Z", "main", "2026-10-19 laps folded from the deleted history ledger (docs/agents/history/2026-10-19-backlog-laps, HISTORY-BACKLOG-LAPS-DRIFT): lap 5 12:19 (subagent): in-tree pair queued -> next: read the pair; close if equal | lap 7 18:35 (subagent): root cause: notebook.spi:263 leaks test opens + type pack shadows module pack; minimal repro g_typed_twice; fix staged -> next: lane 2 applies test_opens_patch.py, rerun minimal + tibia pair | lap 8 20:35 (subagent): Done: Cells test_opens fix in tree; tibia case 2/2, minimal 2/2, lib gates 7/2/8, mix 36 -> next: -")
inl kino_accept_slot_swap () = Task ("KINO-ACCEPT-SLOT-SWAP", "Kino --accept swapped two actual values between asserts and then looped 25 rounds: evolved |> _assert_eq 948i32 and cavebot |> _assert_eq 1099i32 with real values evolved=1099, cavebot=995 became 995/1099; likely matches the failing actual (1099) to a literal already present in the file instead of to the assert that failed; repro: ac4b4e98/tmp/accept_swap_repro_before.spi over apps/tibia/pack_sim.spi in a scratch copy, test cyclops_pack_tuned_cavebot_beats_cold_started_evolution_on_fifty_held_out_seeds, run record ac4b4e98/tmp/runs/repin.ipynb; also cost: accept fixes one assert per round and reruns the whole test (rounds x test time), fix all failing asserts of one run per round; filed 2026-10-13 10:41 from the tibia lane; 2026-10-13 10:56 done by the Kino lane: root cause: C prints the failing __assert_eq line first (builder message) and again after the passing lines, and the old position count stopped at the first mismatch, so it saw 0 earlier passes and picked the first equal literal; now the failing assert is the (k+1)-th _assert_eq written in the block where k = all passing __assert_eq lines in the output, and its literal must be E or the test is refused (never another equal literal); regression test with the repro's exact output in accept_test.exs; one assert per round stays (an assert aborts the program, so later failures are unknown until the rerun)", Story, P2, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "kino,testing", "current", "current")
inl spiral_record_update_expr () = Task ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", "2026-10-13 12:07 record update accepts only a variable before 'with': {(offense_against kind) with level = c.hunter_level} fails with 'Expected: lowercase variable' (hunting_pack.hunter_of), forcing a throwaway inl; allow an expression (parenthesized or an application) as the update base; serves: domain code that refines computed records", TaskKind, P4, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,syntax,tibia", "current", "current")
inl note_of_spiral_record_update_expr_1 () = Note ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", 1u32, "2026-10-14T11:59Z", "lane-a", "07:59 lane-a: patch ready, lane-a\\patches\\record-update-expr.ps1 (record_with base: var or rounds next; 2 anchors, dry-run ok on core 71184C99). Repro lane-a\\repro\\record_update_expr (expect exit 42). Needs main build+ladder.")
inl note_of_spiral_record_update_expr_2 () = Note ("SPIRAL-RECORD-UPDATE-EXPR", 2u32, "2026-10-14T15:16Z", "lane-a", "11:16 lane-a: patch verified on an isolated Debug build (current core BFB7B6A3 + patch, 252 s): repro {(origin ()) with x = 40} fails on the 04:35 core ('Expected: lowercase variable'), compiles on the patched one, C run exits 42. Ready for main's pack.")
