inl eoie_idiomatic_core () = Task ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", "rewrite eoie's core as idiomatic Spiral the way apps/tibia is going: a GADT command algebra (operation indexed by its receipt type), existential handlers, HKT-style receipt/result views, no rust_global or !!!! macro blobs; Rust stays the compiled target (rayon for parallel walk/search); keep the 1000-line crate gate, which is paying off; foundation for the one-call verbs; source: transcript sweep 2026-10-13 22:13 over ~45k tool calls (claude 41.6k, codex 2.0k, opencode 1.1k, grok 0.2k; zed 8 threads parsed, tool shape not yet recognized); report in main's job tmp/sweep/intent-report.txt; 2026-10-14 03:56 lane 3 typed design of eoie do (not compiled; C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\eoie-do\\model.spi, 939 lines, no macros, plus cases.md): GADT statement effect receipt error with 29 constructors (Edit/Write/Copy staged_write; Show/Around/Excerpt/Search/Files/Dirs/GroupLines/Nearest/Json/Table/Diff/Hash/Env/Exists/Errors/Processes/GitHistory/GitStatus/GitLog pure_read; Run/Stop/Wait/JobStart/JobWait/GitInit/GitCommit external_effect), one receipt record and one error union per statement kind, existential handles (exists kind. handle kind * handle_target kind for process/job/output), receipt views as prototypes (receipt_tallies, receipt_lines, error_lines, error_exit), effect_policy prototype for rayon fan-out (per file/dir/repo inside a statement, across consecutive pure/staged statements between barriers, never across external effects); reuse: text-replace expectations, exact_replace and batch-write commit engine with rollback, parallel_search walk/sort, fs-read/slice/context/list, fs-copy, hash, process/observation, batch-plan step algebra, rooted paths; replaced: patch/fs-actions/fs-batch-write/batch-plan file-then-call entry points and the patch plan grammar, macro blobs move behind one Rust-boundary module per capability", Story, P1, D8, 0u32, Planned, "EOIE-STYLE-CHECKPOINT", "eoie,one-call,adoption", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_idiomatic_core () = Planning ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", Minutes 1800u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_1 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:22Z", "lane-a", "08:22 lane-a: rewrite baseline (git ls-files eoie/src): 309 packages; hand-written Rust 90 files/25.4k lines + 26 Rust test files/2.1k lines (no .spi sibling), generated 71/29.7k; rust_global 390 (top: contracts_entry 48), !!!! 2,319.")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_2 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 2u32, "2026-10-15T10:50Z", "main-thread", "06:50 groom: unchanged; lane B added one more Spiral owner tonight (eoie_dev_spiral_tests, Spiral only), and rust_global sites are 261 (source-topology 10-15).")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_3 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 3u32, "2026-10-15T10:55Z", "main-thread", "06:55 groom: a different cut than lane A's baseline (90 files/25.4k lines): 188 tracked .rs under eoie/src, of which 26 files / 2,061 lines sit in directories with no .spi at all, the hand-written islands with no Spiral owner. Those 26 are the first rewrite targets.")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_4 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 4u32, "2026-10-22T09:23Z", "eoie", "05:23 recount of the 06:55 groom's first targets: hand-written .rs islands without a .spi owner are down from 26 files to 0 outside tests; the 14 that remain are tests/*.rs (846 lines), tracked on EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS. So the rewrite starts from generated crates only: the GADT command algebra replaces rust_global blobs and host-macro clusters, guided by the EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY census (1500 macros, eoie_jobs 62 the largest).")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_5 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 5u32, "2026-10-22T22:09Z", "eoie-lane", "18:09 legacy-construct counts over src/*/*.spi (text counts, no compile). Live tree (644 files): rust_global 386, host blocks $'{ 176, concat5 1,172, Rc::<str>::from 616, lines with a host macro 1,502. GE2+H tree (682 files): rust_global 386 (unchanged), host blocks 168, concat5 556 (-52%), Rc wraps 570, host-macro lines 1,371 (-9%). The E2 heal wave halves string concatenation but does not touch rust_global, the largest block of non-idiomatic code (386 blobs). rust_global removal needs the OS boundary package (EOIE-HEAL-BOUNDARY) as the place the remaining host code moves to. These counts are the baseline for measuring each later wave.")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_6 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 6u32, "2026-10-23T23:24Z", "eoie", "19:24 eoie: design start, from apps/tibia's idiom (style reference only: tibia/src/readiness.spi). A private GADT 'ready group' can only be built by gate functions (attack_gate returns gate attack_group = Open (ready attack_group) | ClosedUntil ms), and commands take the proof (Strike : ready attack_group), so acting without passing the gate doesn't typecheck. eoie mappings where a recorded bug becomes a type error: (1) job gate: union private admitted resource = SlotAdmitted :: ticket -> admitted heavy_slot | WindowGranted :: window_id -> admitted machine_window; supervise's child start takes admitted heavy_slot * admitted machine_window, and the window request takes admitted heavy_slot, so window-before-slot (17 of 87 heavy jobs on the 10-21 binary, EOIE-WINDOW-LIVE-QUEUE note 4) can't be written. (2) agile mutation: state_written takes locked state_lock, minted only by the lock acquire, so an unlocked write is a type error. (3) release launch: land takes gates_passed stage, minted by the gate checks (today's typecheck-marker and O-installed gates). (4) tree writes: write verbs take lease_clear root, minted by the lease/window check (EOIE-TREE-READ-RECORD). First slice when this starts: (1) in eoie_job_gate, a pure-model change with the proofs in a model module and the gate loop returning them. Order: after the train's releases install, since eoie_job_gate is touched by HIJK/L.")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_7 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 7u32, "2026-10-23T23:24Z", "eoie", "19:24 eoie: slice (1)'s pure model drafted (scratch f6/src/eoie_job_admission/model.spi). A private GADT admitted resource (SlotAdmitted :: ticket -> admitted heavy_slot | WindowGranted :: id -> admitted machine_window) is minted only by slot_gate and window_gate; window_gate takes an admitted heavy_slot, and child_start takes both proofs. Tests: the slot, then window, then start path carries both names; a later ticket and a full queue wait with reasons. Typecheck runs in the post-block batch; wiring into eoie_job_gate after the train installs.")
inl note_of_eoie_idiomatic_core_8 () = Note ("EOIE-IDIOMATIC-CORE", 8u32, "2026-10-24T23:43Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 1800m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D8 at 0%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
