inl hopacsota_p1 () = Task ("HOPACSOTA-P1", "hopacsota Phase 1: -Mode hopacsota + SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA, D10 seam hooks (single-flight code moved unchanged, projection-hash equal), hopacsota-lint.ps1 G1 size + G2 banned, Deferred worklist with D3 tables/D6 merge/D8 types, 4 frontier_hopacsota_* fixtures first; gate: -Suite all 0 diffs on Inline + Deferred DFS/BFS/3 seeds, Inline <=1.05x single-flight (spiral/apps/compiler/tmp/lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md); 2026-10-14 02:15 lane 3 drafted 7 frontier fixtures in scratch (C:\\Users\\i574n\\.claude\\jobs\\5a6e53fb\\tmp\\hopacsota-fixtures, README with expected single-flight outcomes derived from PartEval line by line, not yet compiled): recursion_unannotated (Recursive join points must be annotated, 163000), mutual_pending (exit 0, annotated pending key returns its type, 162999), globals_order (main.c lines m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2), two_errors (type error 'first body fails'), if_depth_across_fork (P1: EJP0040 only via the caller's depth 600 + leaf's 600), validation_global (P2: '// nested validation global' between g1 and g2, added once through the validation cache), pending_type_join_point (P3: recursive union read by ty_is_uninhabited, exit 0); the main thread compiles them after the bless", Story, P0, D6, 100u32, Done, "HOPACSOTA-RESEARCH", "compiler,hopacsota", "current", "current")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_1 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 1u32, "2026-10-14T12:39Z", "main-thread", "08:39 compiled lane 3's 7 drafted frontier_hopacsota_* fixtures (job tmp/hopacsota-fixtures) with the installed single-flight Release DLL. 6 match their predictions: globals_order emits m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2 and exits 0; validation_global emits g1, then nested validation global once, then g2; mutual_pending and pending_type_join_point exit 0; if_depth_across_fork raises EJP0040; two_errors reports 'first body fails' at 12:10. recursion_unannotated is wrong: it compiles and exits 0, and so does a variant with the recursive call in the then branch. EJoinPoint' annot (163017) comes from the prepass's inferred type, so a plain let rec reaches peval as Some. The error at 163000 needs a join point whose type the prepass leaves None. Next: find that shape (an explicit join, or a polymorphic body) before blessing the fixture.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_2 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 2u32, "2026-10-14T12:40Z", "main-thread", "08:40 explicit 'inl rec count (n : i32) = join if ...' also compiles, with the recursive call in either branch, so the typechecker fills the join's annotation too (RawAnnot around RawJoinPoint, 55283). An annot=None join point may be unreachable from source; if so the 163000 arm is dead code for hopacsota D4, and the fixture should instead pin 'inferred annotation lets pending recursion return without waiting'. Scratch variants are in job tmp/hopacsota-fixtures/scratch_join_*.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_3 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 3u32, "2026-10-14T13:01Z", "main-thread", "09:01 settled: the typechecker's fill pass wraps every RawJoinPoint as RawAnnot(r, RawJoinPoint(...), annot r x) (spiral_compiler.fs 50402, and 52724 on the other side). Backend-switch join points (join_point_backend, 44452) take the same path, so the prepass always builds EJoinPoint' with Some annotation and peval's 'Recursive join points must be annotated' arm (163000) is unreachable from type-checked source. For hopacsota D4: keep that case as a defensive compiler error, not a scheduled waiter rule. Replace frontier_hopacsota_recursion_unannotated with a fixture where pending recursion returns its inferred type without waiting (both of lane 3's orderings already compile: exit 0).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_4 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 4u32, "2026-10-15T10:51Z", "main-thread", "06:51 groom: input from 10-15: the merge rules P1 must carry are now concrete (four memo kinds with key lists and hit markers, index rebuild after merge, inert markers after close; R4 copy tmp/hopacsota-p0/r4_deferred.ps1). Ready to start after the design note.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_5 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 5u32, "2026-10-15T11:22Z", "main-thread", "07:22 main: phase-1 design note written into lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (Phase 1 starting point): R4's gate is met and its keyed merge carries over unchanged (four global-emitting memos, references on hits, depth-first expansion, GlobalsIndex rebuild, inert after close); frontier_hopacsota_globals_order now names the two concrete cases R4 found. Next grain: the -Mode hopacsota plumbing in build/test/probe/env/projection-hash.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_6 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 6u32, "2026-10-15T14:29Z", "main-thread", "10:29 main: Phase 1 step 1 done (plumbing). -Mode hopacsota (alias hs) in env.ps1 ConvertTo-SpiralMode, build.ps1, test.ps1 (a candidate like gpt5parallel: broken rows report 'missing', UNEXPECTED-OUTPUT not fatal, -Bless refused), probe.ps1, fast-tier.ps1 (run prefix hopacsota-), test-rust-exports.ps1, projection-hash.ps1. Core fsproj defines SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA; host defines SPIRAL_CORE_SINGLE_FLIGHT plus SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA (the host sees single-flight's API). Gate check: projection-hash gives hopacsota = single-flight (cad3e1792ab19b4a, 28,150 lines). Next: a first -Mode hopacsota build after the current packs, then hopacsota-lint.ps1 (G2) and the size budget (G1), then the deferred worklist from R4i.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_7 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 7u32, "2026-10-15T14:30Z", "main-thread", "10:30 main: G1/G2 gate script added: scripts/hopacsota-lint.ps1 (-Size: layer <= 5,934 lines, no section > 1,000; -Banned: the PLAN's G2 list incl. the D2 identifiers replay/record/resume/snapshot/ledger, allowlist in-script, empty). It scans only #if SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA sides. build.ps1 -Mode hopacsota runs it and fails on a violation. Tree: 0 layer lines, 0 hits. A probe with a ConcurrentDictionary and a replayStore identifier reports both and exits 1.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_8 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 8u32, "2026-10-15T15:18Z", "main-thread", "11:18 design gap before the worklist step: D10 wants seams as hooks whose single-flight implementation is the current code moved unchanged, and also single-flight's projection hash unchanged (G6). Moving the seam code changes the call-site text in single-flight's PartEval side, so the hash cannot stay equal literally. Options: (a) G6 compares projections modulo the named seam call sites (projection-hash.ps1 learns a seam list), or (b) seams stay inline and hopacsota wraps them in a Hopacsota layer section that shadows the enclosing function. Needs a decision before the R4i worklist moves into a layer; recorded instead of improvised.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_9 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 9u32, "2026-10-15T15:49Z", "main-thread", "11:49 D10/G6 decided (main, autonomous): seams become calls into a PartEvalSeams module defined in a hopacsota layer pair before PartEval (single-flight side = the moved code, hopacsota side = the deferred worklist from R4i). G6 changes from 'projection hash unchanged' to (1) single-flight's oracle unchanged (review identical) and (2) single-flight's projection diff contains only lines that call PartEvalSeams. projection-hash.ps1 gets a -Seams check and pair-drift.ps1 accepts a one-sided PartEval change only when every changed line is a PartEvalSeams call. Next: implement those two checks, then move the first seam (type join point memo).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_10 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 10u32, "2026-10-15T15:55Z", "main-thread", "11:55 G6 seam checks implemented: pair-drift.ps1 now allows a one-sided single-flight change when every added code line calls PartEvalSeams (probe repo: seam edit passes, non-seam edit fails); projection-hash.ps1 -Seams [-Base HEAD] compares single-flight's projection to the base and fails unless every added line is a PartEvalSeams call (on today's tree it correctly flags the uncommitted pack changes). env.ps1 Get-SpiralCoreProjection takes an optional -Source. First -Mode hopacsota build: 228 s, G1 0 lines, G2 0 hits. Next: the PartEvalSeams pair and the first seam (type join point memo), in a session after today's packs are committed (the -Seams base must be clean).")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_11 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 11u32, "2026-10-16T13:53Z", "main-thread", "09:53 main: seams step built (job tmp/hopacsota-p1/seams.ps1, on a copy of the pack-1u tree): PartEvalSeams pair before PartEval; single-flight side = inline no-ops (start/defer/root/key_hit/key_body), hopacsota side = R4's deferral + keyed merge (policy SPIRAL_HOPACSOTA_POLICY inline|dfs|bfs|random:N) plus D4's error rule (failures kept as markers in the body's list, the first on the depth-first walk is raised); 9 single-flight call sites. G1 128 lines, G2 0 hits, G6 structural: 14 added projection lines, all PartEvalSeams calls or ')'. Tooling for G6: projection-hash -BaseFile, -w diff, PartEvalSeams section stripped; Get-SpiralCoreProjection resolves SPIRAL_CORE_HOPACSOTA; pair-drift -w (decision change in PLAN.md). Fixtures added: frontier_hopacsota_recursion_inferred, mutual_pending, globals_order (m1 a1 c1 a2 b1 m2), two_errors (first body fails; ExpectedErrors entry); single-flight outcomes match the drafts' predictions. globals_order does not yet cover R4's two concrete cases (nominal stub under validation, type join point hit by a deferred body); apps/spiral covers them. Running: G3 compile-only suites single-flight (G6 semantic vs bless 092123) + hopacsota inline/dfs/bfs/random:11/23/37.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_12 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 12u32, "2026-10-16T15:29Z", "main-thread", "11:29 main: GATE 1 MET (numbers in PLAN.md scoreboard). G1 131 lines, G2 0; -Suite all compile-only (6,758 rows): single-flight with seams = pack-1u oracle 092123 on every compile/residual/error cell (G6 semantic); hopacsota inline/dfs/bfs/random:11/23/37 each 0 differing cells (runs hopacsota-20261016-105126..110811); apps/spiral F# (963,180 B) and Rust (1,590,762 B) byte-identical under all 7; inline A/B (best of 3, interleaved) sum 0.996x, median 1.007x, mega roots <= 1.031x. v3 adds D4's first-error rule (two_errors failed random:23 without it) and compile-time prints as ordered markers (PrintStatic order differed under bfs/random before). Landed in the tree as pack-1v (seams.ps1 has a guard that every call-site edit sits on single-flight's PartEval side: the first print anchor had matched the gpt5parallel side). Left in Phase 1's structure: D3 Owner/Waiter capability, D8 phantom keys, globals_order pinning R4's two cases.")
inl note_of_hopacsota_p1_13 () = Note ("HOPACSOTA-P1", 13u32, "2026-10-16T15:59Z", "main-thread", "11:59 main: pack-1v installed both modes (11:22/11:28) and blessed: single-flight-20261016-112838, 6,758 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells against pack-1u's 092123; the 16 extra rows are the 4 frontier_hopacsota fixtures on Fsharp/C/Rust/Delphi (Rust and Delphi agree with C; two_errors is an error row on all four). The seams are in the tree and installed; single-flight output unchanged.")
