inl matrix_agree_fail () = Task ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", "Harness classifier hides wrong answers (found 2026-10-14 03:02 by the research lane, confirmed at apps/compiler/tmp/scripts/test.ps1:619): agree-fail treats any two nonzero exits as a shared failure, so a sample whose main returns a value (42, 235) reports a backend's wrong answer as agreement; 90 C rows exit nonzero, exposing 460 non-C rows; currently masking lua_while_union_pair [Wasm] (1 vs 235: wasmtime 39 proc_exit rejects statuses >= 126); fix: agree-fail only when both exits are failure-class; companions H2 (bless keeps 55 stale rows for backends no longer scheduled), H3 (abi_external_buffer_length_negative has no C-flags rule, its C row is a link failure), H4 (c-only label can mask a ran-but-different row); patch scripts in the job scratch after-bless/; apply after tonight's bless, then rerun -Suite all -Native and review every row that flips", Story, P0, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,harness,correctness", "current", "current")
inl note_of_matrix_agree_fail_1 () = Note ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", 1u32, "2026-10-14T10:39Z", "user", "2026-10-14 06:39 user decision: apply the after-bless fix scripts now (on top of tonight's blessed oracle), not after pack 2, in RUNBOOK.md order, then rerun -Suite all -Native single-flight, review every flipped row and rebless once; gpt5parallel no longer gates the bless")
inl note_of_matrix_agree_fail_2 () = Note ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", 2u32, "2026-10-14T11:00Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:00 review dry-run of the runbook on scratch copies of today's test.ps1 (with lane 2's -Suite fast edits) and matrix.psd1: h4, h1, wasm_fixture, h2, expected_errors_check and h3 all apply, test.ps1 parses (0 errors), harness parses; h1 flips exactly lua_while_union_pair [Wasm] 1 vs 235; HAZARD in h2: it drops oracle rows on any full bless 'whatever -Backend', and its preview now lists 2,444 rows because latest-single-flight.tsv is this morning's Bend-only restore run (single-flight-20261014-063836, -Backend Bend): a full -Bless filtered to one backend would delete every other backend's rows; fix before applying: drop only when the bless ran with no -Backend and no -Filter, and compare against that same run's job list, never latest-*.tsv")
inl note_of_matrix_agree_fail_3 () = Note ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", 3u32, "2026-10-14T11:34Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-14 07:34 correction: h2's bless logic is safe (scheduled rows come from the harness's per-sample backend lists, not from -Backend); only its dry-run preview reads latest-*.tsv, which produced the 2,444 figure")
inl note_of_matrix_agree_fail_4 () = Note ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", 4u32, "2026-10-14T12:29Z", "main-thread", "08:29 runbook run single-flight-20261014-073517: DISAGREE 0, 3089 native ran, 8 build-fail (was 9: abi_external_buffer_length_negative C now runs exit 3 via the h3 shim). Flips as predicted: lua_while_union_pair Wasm agrees, 6 package samples compile and exit 42 on C/Rust/Delphi. One surprise (brzozowski negative forge compiles) reverted, see MEGA-SAMPLES-TOGETHER. Next: -Bless run.")
inl note_of_matrix_agree_fail_5 () = Note ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", 5u32, "2026-10-14T13:54Z", "main-thread", "09:54 the first -Bless run (single-flight-20261014-083026) was spoiled and blessed anyway (DISAGREE 6). Cause, my error: the R4 policy suite (night cache, R4 DLL built from source that already had the WGSL lanes edits) started at 09:47 on the same sample tree. test.ps1's mutex is per cache dir and outputs compile in place, so it overwrote main.wgsl/.c/.rs mid-run. Result: 4 Wgsl residuals hashed foreign output, plus 6 native timeouts (new shaders on the old runner; load). R4 stopped, other heavy jobs held, lanes asked to keep the gate free; a clean -Bless run is in progress and must reproduce single-flight-20261014-073517 row for row (except the reverted brzozowski negative), which also restores the tree outputs. Lesson recorded: one suite at a time across all caches; R4 reruns from a copied tmp tree.")
inl note_of_matrix_agree_fail_6 () = Note ("MATRIX-AGREE-FAIL", 6u32, "2026-10-14T21:22Z", "main-thread", "17:22 done: h1 (agree-fail only when both exits are failure-class), h2, h3, h4 and the runbook companions are applied to test.ps1/matrix.psd1. Reviewed run single-flight-20261014-073517 (DISAGREE 0; lua_while_union_pair Wasm now agrees; abi_external_buffer_length_negative C runs, exit 3). Clean rebless single-flight-20261014-095423 reproduces it row for row apart from the restored brzozowski negative. Kept through two installs since (140125, 164608: 0 differences from their reviews). Uncommitted, on the user's commit list.")
