inl note_of_x_compat_block_weight_12 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT", 12u32, "2026-10-20T22:54Z", "main", "18:54 main: the compiler side of x's 10-19 23:38 request is written as lab X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT/postable-budget.ps1 (dry run matches both anchors; shared section, both cores). Block i (1-based top-level block) is checked against 280 - weight('c<i> 1/1' + newline) - defused dots, where a dot is defused when the char before is an ASCII letter, digit, _ or - and the char after is an ASCII letter (x splitter.spi posted_unit, glyphs.spi label_char and letter). Message: 'weight W > L (280 minus the cN k/n header and defused dots)'. Proof queued as heavy job x-budget: installed vs candidate --x-compat on x/apps/client now (expect 0 XC005; x fixed its cells) and on HEAD copies from before x's 00:55 fixes (expect about 40 new XC005 under the candidate). Follow-up: the host's runXCompatReport walks directories with SearchOption.AllDirectories, the same unpruned walk that looped on deps symlinks in the formatter.")
inl note_of_x_compat_block_weight_13 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT", 13u32, "2026-10-20T23:42Z", "main", "19:42 proof (heavy job x-budget, Debug candidate core 87B3A977D3497AA0 with the tree host incl. host-walk.ps1): --x-compat on x/apps/client HEAD (61b8fff, before x's 00:55 cell fixes, 27 files) gives installed 0 findings vs candidate 29 overweight. On the current client (36 files) both give 0, which agrees with x's xc post-thread dry run (0 cells over one post). 29 rather than the 40 measured on 10-19 fits the rule: x measured 40 with its old 'cN 99/99' header budget, and since 00:55 the splitter, and so this rule, budgets the one-digit 'cN 1/1'. The host walk fix holds: '--x-compat C:\\home\\git\\dice' (deps\\polyglot symlink in a link cycle) finishes in 1 s (396 findings, dice is not edition 3). Ships in the evening pack with candidate 8 and published-ready.")
inl note_of_x_compat_block_weight_14 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT", 14u32, "2026-10-21T01:44Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 21:44 x-lane backlog refactor: the x side is done (0 cells over one post in 36 files); what is left is main's: installing the proven postable budget (lab postable-budget.ps1, candidate 87B3A977) and the Cells-side weight check, so the 30m estimate is the install plus one x-compat rerun on the client from the x lane")
inl note_of_x_compat_block_weight_15 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT", 15u32, "2026-10-21T03:16Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 23:16 done for x (X-DONE deliberation 1): the client keeps 0 cells over one post and 0 --x-compat findings, re-proven by the pre-commit round (postable 1617 posts in 36 files, 0 over). The compiler half moved to the main-owned XC005-POSTABLE-BUDGET; the Cells-side weight check stays with X-COMPAT-CHECK's last step")
