inl note_of_x_client_threads_6 () = Note ("X-CLIENT-THREADS", 6u32, "2026-10-18T13:51Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 09:51 bless paths are in the repo now: apps/client/e2e/e2e.ps1 -Bless rewrites the README walkthrough outputs (proven: two perturbed outputs fail without it and are restored byte for byte with it), apps/sim/build.ps1 -Bless rewrites the sim fixtures; the scratch bless script is retired")
inl note_of_x_client_threads_7 () = Note ("X-CLIENT-THREADS", 7u32, "2026-10-18T16:32Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 12:32 threads of any age: search/recent only sees 7 days and returned 0 (exit 0, empty program) for an older thread. Live contract (~$0.17, 34 posts): search/all works on our plan, defaults to the last 30 days unless start_time is sent (0 results for a 47-day-old NASA conversation without it, 8 with it), same shape (root included, newest first, next_token even on a short page), 300 requests/15 min with no 1/s pacing seen. xc thread now looks up the root's created_at and pages search/all from it (wire thread_search record replaces the positional tuple); the stub serves search/all with the 30-day default and search/recent with 7 days against world.now; xsim.world --base-time puts sim-lost in August (78 days), so dropping start_time empties that thread and fails the e2e. All 3 sim threads byte-exact, x-compat 0, 14 crates under the gate (thread 428)")
inl note_of_x_client_threads_8 () = Note ("X-CLIENT-THREADS", 8u32, "2026-10-18T18:52Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 14:52 design for the remaining run step (decided, not built): xc stays a pure X client with no Cells or compiler dependency; running lives on the Cells side as mix xsim.thread_run --file F: read the program a thread carries (xc thread ID > F), evaluate it with Spiral.Cells.Notebook.evaluate and compare each test block's verdict with the same evaluation of the original file (sequential equivalence, as xsim.run already checks), run in apps/sim/build.ps1 outside -fast on thread-sample.txt; README shows the two commands. Waits for a quieter machine (a Cells compile per cell)")
inl note_of_x_client_threads_9 () = Note ("X-CLIENT-THREADS", 9u32, "2026-10-20T03:51Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-19 23:51 run step built (uncommitted in x): apps/sim mix xsim.thread_run --file F (--program P | --expected J) parses both texts as Cells documents, evaluates each with Notebook.evaluate at F's path (memo off) and passes only when the thread carries F's cells and every test's verdict and per-target status match; runs in apps/sim/build.ps1 outside -fast on oauth1.spi against thread-oauth1.expected.json (the program the e2e proves xc thread reads back byte for byte). Probe lab/X-CLIENT-THREADS/thread_run_probe.ps1: oracle exit 0 (6 cells, 4 rust tests), tampered program exit 1 naming the 2 flipped tests. README shows the xc thread ID > program.spi + mix xsim.thread_run commands")
inl note_of_x_client_threads_10 () = Note ("X-CLIENT-THREADS", 10u32, "2026-10-20T10:10Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 06:10 follow-up: xsim.thread_run passed vacuously when both evaluations errored (status=error/error after a package type error); it now also requires the original file to pass, and apps/sim/build.ps1 proves the check both ways on every full build (oauth1 thread passes; the same program with tampered assertions must fail: 'xsim / thread_run rejects a tampered thread'). The lab probe is promoted into the build and deleted")
