inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_3 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 3u32, "2026-10-21T01:46Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 21:46 x-lane backlog refactor: assignee pair. The x half authors the postability profile in the x repo (the 280 budget, weight ranges, 23 per link, the defused-dot rule from splitter.spi and the TLD list now in Kino priv/tlds.txt, as one data file both the compiler and Cells read). The compiler half is main's: XCompat reads the profile instead of constants. 240m covers both halves; the x half goes first so main codes against a real file")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_4 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 4u32, "2026-10-21T02:03Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-20 22:03 x half delivered (uncommitted): x/postability/x.json (profile x, version 1: post weight_limit 280 and link_weight 23; code_point_weight default 2 with the four weight-1 ranges 0-4351, 8192-8205, 8208-8223, 8242-8247; links: domain_pattern, top_level_domains_file tlds.txt, short_domains_always_linked t.co, two-letter TLDs link only when the second label is longer than 2; entities hashtag/mention/cashtag; posting: block, header c{block} {k}/{n}, one-post budget header, defused dot rule [A-Za-z0-9_-] . [A-Za-z] with U+200B and +1 weight, block_limit formula) plus x/postability/tlds.txt. Checked: the four regexes are byte-equal to spiral_compiler.fs xCompat*Pattern, and the TLD list equals both the compiler's xCompatTopLevelDomains and apps/cells/priv/tlds.txt (1,286 entries, 0 differences), so either hardcoded copy can be replaced by the profile with no behavior change. Compiler half (main): XCompat and Cells read the profile path instead of constants")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_5 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 5u32, "2026-10-21T02:04Z", "main", "22:04 main received x's half: C:\\home\\git\\x\\postability\\x.json plus tlds.txt (uncommitted). It covers the 280 limit, 23 per link, the code-point weight ranges, the domain/hashtag/mention/cashtag regexes, t.co, the two-letter TLD label rule, the posting header and the defused-dot block budget. x verified that all four regexes are byte-equal to the compiler's xCompat*Pattern literals and that the TLD list equals xCompatTopLevelDomains and cells/priv/tlds.txt (1,286 entries, 0 differences). Compiler half pending (main): read the profile instead of the constants, with no behavior change; it lands after the postable-budget install that X-COMPAT-BLOCK-WEIGHT waits on.")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_6 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 6u32, "2026-10-21T02:42Z", "main", "22:42 compiler half written: lab/X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE/profile.ps1 (dry run clean on the evening pack core). It replaces the 170-line XCompat region (TLD list, regexes, 280, weight ranges, 23 per link, header and defused-dot budget) with a PostabilityProfile record loaded from JSON with System.Text.Json and cached per path. Discovery: SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE, else the nearest postability/*.json walking up from the checked file, so x/apps/client finds x/postability/x.json and needs no flag. A repo without a profile gets no platform rules (platform-neutral core); only x/apps/client declares edition 3 and nothing else sets SPIRAL_X_COMPAT, so no other lane loses checks. The host --x-compat and xCompatWarnEntry resolve the profile per file. Gate chained after formatter-c9b (it edits the tree host only while nothing else builds): --x-compat finding lines must be identical to the budget-only candidate on x client HEAD copies and the current client, and 0 on dice.")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_7 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 7u32, "2026-10-21T05:45Z", "main", "2026-10-21 01:45 main: compiler half gated on the exact evening pack (core A9A71772B249FB8B, Debug candidate x-profile, host restored byte-for-byte): with x/postability/x.json as the profile, --x-compat finding lines are identical to the budget-only candidate on the x client HEAD copies (29 findings, 27 files) and on the current x client found by location (0 findings, 36 files); dice, which has no postability profile, now gets 0 findings (budget-only reported 396: autolink 222, hashtag 10, overweight 164), so X rules apply only where a profile says so. Installs with the evening pack; x gets told to rerun --x-compat after the install.")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_8 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 8u32, "2026-10-21T07:20Z", "main", "2026-10-21 03:20 main: compiler half INSTALLED with the evening pack at 03:19 (tree core A9A71772B249FB8B, host with profile lookup). x told; x's round4 includes the client build with --x-compat (expect 0).")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_9 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 9u32, "2026-10-21T08:49Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-21 04:49 compiler half landed in main's evening pack (03:19): --x-compat takes its rules from the nearest postability/*.json (x/postability/x.json for the x client) or SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE, and a repo without a profile gets no X findings; verified on x: 0 findings in 36 files on the installed compiler (x-cellid-round4). Cells' own XCompat still carries its constants (the Cells side of the profile is what is left, if main keeps it in scope)")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_10 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 10u32, "2026-10-21T08:53Z", "main", "2026-10-21 04:53 main: confirmed by x on the installed pack (round4, 04:4x): the x client reports 'x-compat report: 0 finding(s) in 36 file(s)' with rules from x/postability/x.json. Cells on the same compiler: 34 of 35 notebook files pass, including the cell_id slice. The one failure, exsss gleam tests hitting the 300 s cell timeout under load, passed on the old compiler tonight; x reruns it on a quiet machine. x marks XC005-POSTABLE-BUDGET done on its side. Left here: the platform-neutral naming of the profile fields and a second profile (a non-X platform) to prove the core holds no X knowledge.")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_11 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 11u32, "2026-10-21T10:41Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-21 06:41 x side: x/postability must be committed: since the evening pack the compiler finds rules only in the nearest postability/*.json (or SPIRAL_POSTABILITY_PROFILE), and a repo without one gets no X findings, so a missing profile would make x's --x-compat gate pass vacuously. x.json trimmed to the 17 keys spiral_compiler.fs postabilityProfileOfFile reads (dropped version, posting.top_level_block, posting.header, posting.block_limit, defused_dot.inserted_before_dot, which nothing reads); tlds.txt stays, the profile names it by path. Also folded apps/sim/frames/.gitignore into apps/sim/.gitignore (the compiler host creates the output folder, so a clone without frames/src is fine)")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_12 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 12u32, "2026-10-21T11:04Z", "x-lane", "2026-10-21 07:04 done (X-DONE deliberation 1 rule): x delivered x/postability/x.json + tlds.txt (trimmed to the 17 keys the compiler reads), main's evening pack made --x-compat read it (0 findings on the x client, round4), so spiral core no longer hardcodes X for the compiler. The Cells half moved to the main-owned CELLS-POSTABILITY-PROFILE")
inl note_of_x_compat_parameterize_13 () = Note ("X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE", 13u32, "2026-10-22T02:23Z", "x", "2026-10-21 22:23 x: lab assimilated. spiral/lab/X-COMPAT-PARAMETERIZE/profile.ps1 (the compiler half's patch) was checked against today's compiler sources: its replaced region and both call-site edits are present (xCompatFindings profile ... in the warning loop and the --x-compat file loop; postable weight from profile.weightLimit minus the profile's header), and the old call texts are gone. Folder deleted. Status back to Done.")
