inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_1 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 1u32, "2026-10-18T17:24Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:24 eoie lane start (user: new eoie code follows the tibia/x granular discipline; migrate the rust_global drift using the type feature set). Baseline: 11166 rust_global blob lines in 108 files (13166 Spiral lines in those files). Slice 1: eoie_archive_tar_runtime/format.spi, archive_format union + classifier, exports eoie_archive_format_code/label, Rust archive_format is now glue (label Rc<str>), 3 Spiral test blocks; regen published, bundle_manifest consumer unchanged, archive_limits/portable_policy/windows tests pass. Slice 2: eoie_bundle_retention/series.spi, series_reading/series_rejection unions with thin primitives, exports eoie_retention_series_error/prefix/alpha, retention_series is glue; 2 test blocks (8 cases incl. u64 overflow text); e2e retention-plan on a scratch series: keep 3 delete 2, rejection text from Spiral, latest-candidate check intact. Both test files registered in eoie_dev_spiral_tests registry. Recipe in memory eoie-granular-spiral")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_2 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 2u32, "2026-10-18T17:38Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:38 slice 3: eoie_bundle_retention/receipt.spi, receipt_status union, the receipt Spiral module template as a block raw string (first real use of the block form in eoie source), export eoie_retention_receipt_source over string*string*u64*u64*u64*string, retention_receipt_source is glue; 2 test blocks incl. a byte-exact expected module; e2e: planned receipt byte-identical to the old format string rebuilt independently, retention-apply passes its readback check, deletes 2, keeps alpha3-5, writes the RetentionApplied receipt; fingerprint unchanged (db54787b1e12c832)")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_3 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 3u32, "2026-10-18T17:50Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 13:50 slice 4: tar_octal field text into format.spi (octal_field union EmptyField/OctalValue/InvalidOctal, trim + base-8 primitives, exports eoie_tar_octal_value/error); Rust keeps only the NUL cut and UTF-8 check; format.spi 4/4, consumer tests green, e2e proxy archive-extract of a real ustar tar.gz: format=tar.gz from the Spiral classifier, sizes through the Spiral octal reader (2 payloads, 14 bytes), contents intact. Whole registry run: 6 notebooks, 19 Spiral tests, all pass. Blob bytes: tar runtime -297 then about -150 more, retention -939. Next candidates by the same recipe: tar_pax_path record validation (typed rejection union), retention_read_receipt field parsing, coverage_union merge, patch_quoted_fields")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_4 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 4u32, "2026-10-18T20:28Z", "claude", "2026-10-18 16:28 slice 5: eoie_coverage_prune/lcov.spi, LCOV parsing as typed Spiral: lcov_line, lcov_state, lcov_rejection (10 messages kept verbatim) and hit_reading unions, a tail-recursive state machine producing normalized rows (bare source rows keep SF blocks without DA lines); exports eoie_lcov_error/rows; coverage_union_records is now glue (validation call plus a trivial row reader into the BTreeMap merge). lcov.spi 2/2 (12 cases), the existing coverage_union_merges_max_hits_and_writes_receipt and the crate's other Rust tests pass. Not migrated: tar_pax_path (payload is bytes and !!!!Export has no byte-slice parameter; a glue-side UTF-8 check would change which non-UTF8 message is reported)")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_5 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 5u32, "2026-10-19T06:40Z", "claude", "2026-10-19 02:40 x lane (git-2c), eoie targets from the five mega samples, for the eoie lane to schedule (cited paths are agent reads, unverified by builds): (1) agile_mutation_policy/model.spi:40-80: agile_status_code plus agile_status_code_valid and the agile_*_decision i32 functions are hand-synced; lean_cic's raw -> verified gate (L:2462-2475) and typed decisions (L:1265-1271) give an Accepted case that carries the agile_status, behind union private. (2) eoie_jobs/model.spi:16-23: replace the JobUnknown catch-all with Known job_command | Unknown string; :43-49 state_exit invents exit 3 for Pending/Running, split job_state into settled and live so the index narrows the match (spiral_proves S:8227-8232). (3) bundle_output_contract/model.spi:25-26: output_pending and output_root_ready are bare nominals; omniledger's chain of custody (3103-3108) makes each stage wrap its predecessor. (4) agile_todo_model/model.spi:187-197 CFamily => 1i32 tables: one prototype instance per union or reflection, never a hand table (EOIE-UNION-REFLECTION). (5) move *_negative_probe folders into in-file fails tests. Features the samples use that eoie lacks: assert_static, and inl")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_6 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 6u32, "2026-10-19T07:36Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-19 03:36 eoie lane on x lane idea (2), measured in a temp copy: job_verb = Known job_command | Unknown string plus job_state = Live job_live | Settled job_settled (settled_exit total over settled states, wait_exit names the 3-while-running convention, output unchanged) compiles and costs +35 lines (eoie_jobs 938 -> 973). Deferred: it is modeling, not missing function, and it would leave 27 lines of headroom in a crate other lanes rely on. Apply it together with a split of eoie_jobs (CLI routing vs registry model). The edit plan is ready as a python JSON-style replacement list (scratchpad jobs-model-edit.py; recreate it if lost).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_7 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 7u32, "2026-10-21T14:19Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 10:19 eoie team: sized the drift first: 46 *terminal*.spi files hold 538 KB of Rust inside Spiral (largest eoie_source_topology_core 40 KB, evidence_currentness 30 KB, bundle zip 33 KB; most serve the GPT-era patch/bundle/proxy surface). Order rule: blobs on today's verbs first (agile, routing, handoff, read), smallest first within that, one blob per slice so a failure pulls one slice. Slice 1 drafted for r31 (scratch apply-agile-terminal-migration.ps1): eoie_agile_mutation's blob (an error helper plus six use-aliases) is gone; the helper is Spiral over workspace_primitives.console.stderr_failure (identical bytes and exit code), aliases become full paths at their single call sites. Next by the rule: eoie_handoff render_terminal (5.8 KB, agile handoff), then agile_state_runtime (agile init/lease/status), then eoie_cli_routing (22 KB, every call).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_8 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 8u32, "2026-10-21T14:19Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 10:20 eoie team (corrected): 'agile handoff' fails on the shared backlog (no state/handoff.spi there) but works on the eoie repo's own root (C:\\home\\git\\eoie\\state\\handoff.spi), and the transcripts show it called there ('eoie agile handoff .': 30 matches in 11 files). So render_terminal (5.8 KB) serves a live verb and stays a migration target, after agile_state_runtime (more callers). Pruning is off the table for it.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_9 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 9u32, "2026-10-21T16:37Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 12:37 eoie team: slice 2 drafted for r32 (scratch apply-handoff-render.ps1; chain-r32 armed behind r31). eoie_handoff's render_terminal blob (agile handoff) is now render.spi in granular Spiral: state reads as a union StateMissing|StateText|StateUnreadable, results as Rendered|Refused, and the optional evidence lines as a ToolchainEvidence|ColdProofEvidence union. handoff_render_owned keeps its &str export. The dead handoff_render() is dropped, and the four std imports the other blobs need move into binary_install_terminal's existing blob, so there is no new rust_global. Measured: inside eoie_handoff the Spiral version generated 1031 lines (render about 400 against the blob's 80), so it got its own crate eoie_handoff_render (render.rs 426, handoff.rs 608). eoie_agile_mutation now depends on it in place of eoie-handoff. Preview, notebook render.spi and cargo check --locked of the 4 crates all pass. The r32 release job adds a handoff parity step (old vs new binary on the eoie root and on a root without handoff.spi; a mismatch blocks the install). series_terminal was skipped by the order rule: agile record is not a verb in use today.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_10 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 10u32, "2026-10-21T20:35Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:35 eoie team: shipped in the combined r28+r29 release, installed 15:38 (one-call spec 34/34, all 67 notebooks green): job_state split into Live job_live | Settled job_settled (x idea 2).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_11 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 11u32, "2026-10-21T20:56Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:56 eoie team: inventory after today's two slices (r31 agile_mutation, r32 handoff render): 44 terminal blobs, 520 KB (was 46, 538 KB). Smallest on today's verbs: rust_std_fs filesystem_terminal (0.6 KB), path_terminal (2.4), presence_terminal (3.0). filesystem_terminal opens a 'mod dense {' that a sibling blob closes and otherwise only re-exports eoie_rust_std_fs_mutation, so the rust_std_fs blobs must move together (dense module, re-exports, then path and presence as typed Spiral), not one by one. The tiny patch-app blobs (rehearsal 0.3, mutation 0.7, gated 1.2 KB) serve GPT-era patch verbs: by the order rule they come after today's verbs, or are pruned once usage shows they're unused (the adoption sweep can count them).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_12 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 12u32, "2026-10-21T20:57Z", "eoie-lane", "2026-10-21 16:57 eoie team, usage evidence for migrate-or-prune (Claude transcripts, 7 days, eoie calls by verb). Top: agile note 1654, job tail 1097, job wait 796, agile show 780, job start 598, agile set 424, job status 291, agile edit 247, window list 242, agile list 226, grep 99, agile add 77, window run 67, agile todos 51. Legacy surface: patch apply/check/rehearse/gated 0; agile record 0; bundle 8 in all. Proxy: text-replace 31, source-topology 27, parallel-search 17, fs-search 8, command-output 5, command-capture 4, fs-write 3, source-stats 3, and about a dozen more at 1-2; the remaining ~50 proxy verbs at 0. Proposed rule, set now and applied next session: a legacy verb with 0 calls in 14 days across all clients, no one-call spec case and no caller in any repo (grep its stem across repos first, per the dangling rule) is pruned rather than migrated, one verb family per slice, with its blob and tests. Verbs with uses migrate by the size order. This turns most of the 520 KB from migration work into deletion.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_13 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 13u32, "2026-10-21T21:09Z", "eoie-lane", "17:09 eoie team, prune evidence for the first family (patch), measured against the 16:57 rule. Calls: 0 real 'eoie patch apply/check/rehearse/gated' in 14 days (Claude Code, 56 transcript files, 880 MB; Codex has no sessions in the window); the 3 hits are prose inside note text. One-call spec: 0 cases. Callers outside eoie: none (grep of 'eoie patch' and the argv form across C:\\home\\git); inside eoie only contracts_entry/cli_driver, eoie_coverage_smoke and the patch crates themselves. Dependency cut (Cargo path deps + spiproj packages): cutting eoie_cli's two edges (eoie_patch_mutation, eoie_patch_rehearsal) makes 19 crates unreachable from eoie_cli; 32 of 34 patch-named crates are unreachable after the cut. patch_control_domain and patch_driver_domain stay (eoie_fs_actions, eoie_batch_write, eoie_legacy_operations, evidence_currentness_domain use them, and proxy fs-write has 28 calls). Slice shape: drop the routing arm and help row, the two cli deps, the 19 crates plus their probes/contracts (backup_domain_probe, patch_*_probe, eoie_patch_*_contracts, eoie_patch_grammar, eoie_patch_scan), the cli_driver/coverage_smoke patch cases; stem-grep each crate across repos first. Side finding: 141 crates are already unreachable from eoie_cli (many are other entries such as eoie_dev and notebook runners); worth a separate census. Scripts: scratch prune-evidence/verb-usage.ps1, exclusive-closure.ps1.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_14 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 14u32, "2026-10-21T21:38Z", "eoie-lane", "17:38 eoie team, orphan census (scratch prune-evidence/orphan-census.ps1, orphan-refs2.ps1; Cargo path deps + spiproj packages; 28,293 text files scanned across C:\\home\\git): 129 crates (499 KB) are unreachable from all three binaries (eoie_cli, eoie_dev, eoie_predicate_lift): 96 probes, 23 contracts, 5 legacy, 5 other; 19 are workspace members. By reference: 87 crates (112 KB) are named only in eoie's own inventories (state/*.spi such as bench, consolidation_fixtures, coverage, owner_growth, runtime_drift; standards/census; review .md), never by a runner, script or other repo; 35 are referenced from other eoie src (eoie_cli_harness via notebook --package headers, contracts run by compiler-contracts); 13 'live' hits are backlog mentions only. Prune rule addition: an inventory-only crate is a prune candidate under the 16:57 rule; its slice removes it from the inventories in the same change and refreshes evidence (state/evidence.spi hashes the coverage files, as found for help_catalog.rs), so the evidence currentness check stays green. Order: the 19 workspace members first (they cost build time), then probes by directory size.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_15 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 15u32, "2026-10-21T21:49Z", "eoie-lane", "17:49 eoie team, patch prune plan for the next session (full text goes to lab/EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION/r36-prune-patch-plan.md after tonight's install). Trap: command_spec_domain numbers commands by union position (declared_code = union_case_index - 1; handler_from_code (code + 1)); today status=0 patch=1 agile=2 bundle=3 proxy=4 help=5, lease denied the literal 7, with 28 numeric sites (11 in eoie_cli_routing/routing_terminal.spi such as eoie_command_descriptor(\"2\") for agile, 14 + 2 in command_spec_domain, 1 in eoie_cli_model). Deleting PatchSpec silently shifts agile to 1. Rule set now: replace every numeric site with a case-based call in the same slice if possible; otherwise give each case an explicit code (code_of) and then delete PatchSpec; never a placeholder case; tie-break the explicit code table. Edits: command spec cases/arms/usage/diagnostic/patch:check effect; eoie_cli_model patch_run; routing EoiePatchAdapter; eoie_cli Cargo deps; workspace members + lock; the 19 crates + their probe/contract dependents (keep patch_control_domain, patch_driver_domain); cli_driver and coverage_smoke patch cases; inventories (state/bench, consolidation_fixtures, coverage, owner_growth, runtime_drift, migration, standards/census) with an evidence refresh in the same release.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_16 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 16u32, "2026-10-22T02:57Z", "eoie", "22:57 heal plan: the migration runs in waves after the r30-r36 train lands (pending slices anchor on today's text). Order: shared packages first by fan-in (rust_std_string, eoie_cli_harness, union_reflection), then crates by host-macro count. Done per crate: references the lib, 0 macros outside the boundary package, 0 $'{ blocks, its tests pass, under the 1000-line gate. Done overall: 376/376 spiproj on the lib, census zeros, ratchet exemptions removed.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_17 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 17u32, "2026-10-22T03:45Z", "eoie", "23:45 migration debt from tonight's release train, by tree delta: live -> r34 +52 host macros / +15 Rc::<str>::from / +7 let-blocks / +7 rust_std_string uses; r34 -> release C +64 / +32 / +14 / +8. Release A absorbs r30-r33's drift into the baseline (its job re-baselines); B and C don't, so their debt shows in the ratchet.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_18 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 18u32, "2026-10-22T05:42Z", "eoie", "01:42 first crate healed end to end in the scratch tree rE (apply-heal-rename-rewrite.ps1, template for the waves): agile_rename_rewrite drops rust_std_string (equals -> =, concat5 -> ++#, trim/replace/starts_with -> sm' with the argument-order flips), replaces two $\" arithmetic macros with plain +, references spiral- and declares HostFree + LibReferenced in standards.spi. Preview exit 0. Measured size cost: rename_rewrite.rs 426 -> 522 lines (+23%: ++# chains and sm' calls inline more than concat5's single host call), so crates above ~800 lines need a split before healing. No test blocks in this crate: its proof is the agile rename CLI notebook in the candidate step of the release that ships it (E).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_19 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 19u32, "2026-10-22T05:45Z", "eoie", "01:45 wave 1 grows (scratch tree rE, slice apply-heal-wave1-small.ps1): agile_record_catalog, proxy_command_output, proxy_file_receipt healed (concat5 -> ++#, spiral- instead of rust_std_string, HostFree + LibReferenced declared); census after: host-macro 0, string-concat 0 for all three. Compile preview deferred until release ABC ends (no eoie-lane compiles meanwhile). With agile_rename_rewrite that's 4 healed crates queued for release E.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_20 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 20u32, "2026-10-22T05:46Z", "eoie", "01:46 wave 1b (apply-heal-wave1b.ps1, scratch tree rE): agile_planning_filters (equals -> =) and agile_state_transient_schema_domain (2 starts_with + 5 contains -> sm' with the needle first) healed, census 0/0; 6 crates now queued for release E (rename_rewrite, record_catalog, command_output, file_receipt, planning_filters, transient_schema). agile_planning_values waits for main's sm'.listed (it uses pipe_lookup).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_21 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 21u32, "2026-10-22T05:48Z", "eoie", "01:48 agile_field_rendering healed too (apply-heal-field-rendering.ps1; equals -> =, two concat5 -> ++#), census 0/0: 7 crates queued for release E. Waiting on main's sm'.listed: agile_planning_values (pipe_lookup) and agile_state_decision_domain (pipe_member). eoie_table_diff opens rust_std_string wholesale (unqualified calls): a later, larger heal.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_22 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 22u32, "2026-10-22T05:52Z", "eoie", "01:52 healing tool written (heal-crate.ps1 -Crate <name> [-DryRun], to lab): an argument tokenizer (string literals with escapes, balanced parenthesized groups, plain tokens) maps concat5 -> ++# chains (empty args dropped), equals -> (a = b), starts_with/ends_with/contains -> sm' with the needle first, replace -> sm'.replace from into text, trim -> sm'.trim; refuses a crate that opens rust_std_string wholesale or keeps unmapped calls; swaps rust_std_string for spiral- in package.spiproj; declares HostFree + LibReferenced when no host macros remain. Applied in the scratch tree rE to agile_state_path_policy, agile_update_receipt, predicate_rules (nested parens + escaped quotes handled), release_hygiene_policy, eoie_source_topology_core (813 lines): census 0/0 each. 12 healed crates queued for release E (compile preview after ABC).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_23 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 23u32, "2026-10-22T06:12Z", "eoie", "02:12 heal tool extended to wholesale 'open rust_std_string.model' crates (unqualified calls, refusing when the file or any opened module defines a same-named function, refusing block strings, replacing indented prelude opens with open sm'_operators) and hardened after a hostile check caught two bugs in the scratch output: multi-line concat5 became empty '++#' operands (tokenizer now skips newlines; multi-line calls keep one operand per line with leading ++#), and rewrites inside $'...' host macros (the string check now tracks macro regions). The 16 affected crates were restored from rD and rehealed; scans show 0 empty operands and macro text unchanged. Release E now carries 28 healed crates: 12 HostFree (rename_rewrite, record_catalog, command_output, file_receipt, planning_filters, transient_schema, field_rendering, state_path_policy, update_receipt, predicate_rules, release_hygiene_policy, source_topology_core) + 16 off rust_std_string with host macros left (job_after, table_measures, memory_query, job_launch, memory_model, receipt, lcov, do_tables, handoff_render, repo_state, do_lab, do_facts, do_process, do_git, command_line, todo_record). Compile proof after ABC.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_24 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 24u32, "2026-10-22T06:17Z", "eoie", "02:17 wave 2 by the hardened tool (scratch tree rE): 39 more crates off rust_std_string (agile_* note/planning/task/title/todo families, canonical_plan_ir_domain, cold_proof_domain, eoie_agile_state, eoie_archive_tar_runtime, eoie_coverage_prune, eoie_dev, eoie_dev_model, eoie_predicate_lift, legacy_operations_entry, proxy_* receipts, workspace_primitives); both hostile scans clean (0 empty operands, macro text unchanged); 8 of them declare HostFree. Release E now carries 67 crates (apply-rE.ps1, 54 tool calls + 4 hand slices + window marker). 15 crates refused by the tool's safety rules (block strings, pipe_member/trim_end_matches waiting for lib helpers, calls it cannot map) stay for hand healing. Risk for E: workspace_primitives is inlined widely and ++# generates more Rust than concat5 (+23% measured), so E's preview must check every crate against the 1000-line gate before it ships.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_25 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 25u32, "2026-10-22T06:19Z", "eoie", "02:19 what the tool leaves (12 crates still on rust_std_string with unmapped calls): trim_end_matches (agile_task_creation, agile_state_runtime_policy_domain) maps onto main's sm'.trim_end_suffix once it lands; pipe_member/pipe_lookup/pipe_index (agile_planning_model, agile_planning_tally, agile_planning_values, agile_state_decision_domain, agile_subcommand_domain, agile_task_listing, agile_task_next, agile_todo_model, command_spec_domain, eoie_agile_mutation) are pipe tables, which the census already counts as drift (pipe-table probe): heal them by replacing each table with a typed union (reflection for the word lists), not with a lib helper. That is per-crate modeling work for hand healing, not for heal-crate.ps1.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_26 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 26u32, "2026-10-22T06:21Z", "eoie", "02:21 first pipe table healed by hand as the template (apply-heal-planning-values.ps1, scratch tree rE): agile_planning_values' pipe_lookup 'yes|pair|no' -> 'agent|pair|user' became union legacy_agent (LegacyYes|LegacyPair|LegacyNo) with legacy_word/legacy_assignee and a union_reflection lookup returning '' for unknown words (same contract); census pipe-table 1 -> 0, rust_std_string dropped. Covered by planning_cli's migrate test ('agent:no' -> assignee=user). E now carries 68 crates.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_27 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 27u32, "2026-10-22T06:23Z", "eoie", "02:23 second pipe table healed by hand (apply-heal-decision-domain.ps1): agile_state_decision_domain's transient pipe table -> union transient_receipt looked up by reflection; its equals chain -> agile_record_file on the existing agile_record_requirement union with a reflection lookup; the v1 catalog string is now derived with union_cases_joined in declaration order (byte-identical 'history.spi|ratings.spi|bench.spi|migration.spi'). Census pipe-table 1 -> 0; no host macros, so it and agile_planning_values now declare HostFree + LibReferenced. E carries 69 crates.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_28 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 28u32, "2026-10-22T06:27Z", "eoie", "02:27 heal tool handles block strings now (tokenizer reads a block literal as one argument; matches inside any block span across lines are skipped; the refusal is gone). Healed in the scratch tree rE: coverage_public_probe (HostFree) and eoie_bundle_retention (7 files, host macros remain); checks: 0 empty operands, every block string byte-identical, macro text unchanged. E carries 71 crates (apply-rE.ps1).")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_29 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 29u32, "2026-10-22T06:28Z", "eoie", "02:28 third pipe table by hand + tool (apply-heal-planning-model.ps1): agile_planning_model's cleared_value 'none|-' -> union cleared_word with a reflection lookup, then heal-crate.ps1 for the ~30 concat5/equals/ends_with/starts_with/replace calls (6 block strings byte-identical, 0 empty operands); census pipe-table 0, string-concat 0, host-macro 3 left. It is a shared model package inlined by the planning crates, so E's preview must re-measure them. E carries 72 crates.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_30 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 30u32, "2026-10-22T13:42Z", "eoie-lane", "09:42 eoie team: a semantic review of heal-crate.ps1's mappings before G ships E's ~75 healed crates (argument-order flips compile fine but invert logic). Legacy rust_std_string takes the text first (starts_with text prefix, ends_with text suffix, contains text needle, replace text from into, trim_end_matches text suffix); lib sm' takes it last (starts_with value s, contains value s, replace old new s, trim_end_suffix suffix input). The tool emits sm'.starts_with a1 a0, ends_with a1 a0, contains a1 a0, replace a1 a2 a0, trim_end_suffix a1 a0: all correct. trim_end_suffix strips every trailing copy like Rust's trim_end_matches (its own lib test says so). pipe_member becomes sm'.listed only for literal, whitespace-free lists. equals becomes (a = b). Residual difference: lib trim covers its own char list rather than all Unicode whitespace, irrelevant for eoie's ASCII inputs. No change needed.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_31 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 31u32, "2026-10-22T14:02Z", "eoie-lane", "10:02 eoie team: heal-crate.ps1's near-gate guard now also measures consumers. A Spiral-only package such as eoie_memory_model has no .rs of its own, so the old guard (skip when the crate's own .rs is at 950+) healed it, even though its code is generated into eoie_memory (994 lines), where every ++# adds a binding. The guard now skips a package when any crate listing it directly in package.spiproj generates 950+ lines. Dry runs: eoie_memory_model is skipped (consumer eoie_memory 994), eoie_receipt is skipped (consumer eoie_do_edit 976). prelaunch-check over F, G and E2 together is still clean. The skipped packages stay on concat5 until main's codegen pack inlines single-use bindings, the same rule as the crates themselves.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_32 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 32u32, "2026-10-22T14:02Z", "eoie-lane", "10:02 measured (package graph only, no compiler): of the 60 packages on E's heal list, none reaches a 950+ line crate only through another Spiral-only package. Every near-gate exposure is a direct consumer, which the extended guard covers, so a transitive guard is not needed for GE2. Re-measure when the heal list grows.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_33 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 33u32, "2026-10-22T21:04Z", "eoie-lane", "17:04 progress measured (package.spiproj and standards.spi read, no compile). Live tree: 377 packages, 5 reference spiral-, 2 declare HostFree + LibReferenced (eoie_tree_lease, eoie_window_claim). GE2+H tree (guard-dry): 384 packages, 107 reference spiral-, 29 declare both (the E2 heal wave plus the new crates). Three more model-only packages drafted today pass both declarations (agile_decision_model, agile_find_model, eoie_release_model in scratch f5). So the GE2+H install would take lib reference from 1.3% to 28% and the declared contract from 0.5% to 7.6% of packages. Progress stays at 3 until GE2 and H are installed (it counts landed packages only); then it moves to about 8.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_34 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 34u32, "2026-10-24T07:37Z", "main", "2026-10-24 03:37 main: raised to P0 under GRANULAR-HEAL (user 10-24: heal once and for all, including eoie). Census: 786 sites, 1,050,302 macro chars, 202 blocks, 337 long, 247 casts, 118 arith; largest files contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi 42/57,982, rust_std_fs_mutation/mutation.spi 6/44,683, eoie_source_topology_core/terminal.spi 7/40,045, eoie_bundle_manifest/bundle_manifest.spi 2/39,539, evidence_currentness_domain/terminal.spi 1/30,037. GRANULAR-HEAL rule (1)-(6) applies; slices land with the lint baseline shrinking.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_35 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 35u32, "2026-10-24T08:50Z", "eoie", "04:5x eoie: slice A of the granular migration is drafted, starting with the largest file. contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi emits 14 Rust #[test]s into eoie_contracts through rust_global; 7 run in every release and 7 are #[ignore]d, reachable only through build.ps1 -CompilerContracts, which nothing automated passes (CI, release scripts and i574n.github scripts have no match). Rule, written before porting: port the release-run tests to Spiral harness notebooks first; keep the ignored ones for a later slice with its own decision; each slice shrinks the file. Slice A (scratch granular-contracts/apply-contracts-slice-a.ps1) moves filesystem_proxy_roundtrip_is_rooted, expired_lease_blocks_first_mutation_but_keeps_wrap_surface and typed_handoff_is_readable_and_versionless into eoie_contracts/contracts_cli.spi (zero host macros; lib sm' plus the harness), registers it with the eoie-contracts notebooks, and deletes their blocks: cli_driver.spi goes from 58,370 to 47,150 chars. Typecheck/run queued as job eoie-typecheck-contracts-slice-a. Next: slice B (bundle_fixture plus flat_bundle, public_rejections, family_contract), then proxy_surface (needs native test tools), then the ignored seven.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_36 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 36u32, "2026-10-24T09:36Z", "eoie", "05:3x eoie: slices B and C drafted. B moves bundle_fixture and the flat-bundle, public-rejections and family-contract tests into eoie_contracts/bundle_cli.spi. C moves proxy_surface into proxy_cli.spi, building its true/false/sleep/printenv tool with the harness rustc_program instead of native_tools.rs. All 7 release-run cli_driver tests are now Spiral, and cli_driver.spi goes from 58,370 to 20,665 chars after A+B+C. Each slice has a rerun guard and the registry parens are checked. Typecheck plus a run against the installed eoie is queued for each (contracts-slice-a/b/c). Rule for slice D, written before drafting: the 7 #[ignore] compiler contracts stay opt-in. Today build.ps1 -CompilerContracts adds cargo --include-ignored, and native_tools.rs' compiler_contracts_remain_registered_after_regeneration guards their registration. They move to eoie_contracts/compiler_contracts_cli.spi, listed in a second registry, contract_registered (), which eoie_dev_spiral_tests runs only when eoie-dev passes --compiler-contracts. The Rust registration guard becomes a registry test that lists all 7 names. Then cli_driver.spi, native_tools.rs and the contracts_entry emit path are deleted, keeping only the typed contract plan in entry.spi, which drops 786 sites by the file's 42 blocks.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_37 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 37u32, "2026-10-24T10:37Z", "eoie", "06:3x eoie: slice A's first run compiled and ran, but all 3 tests failed on one bug of mine. The notebook helper 'inl rec args_from' recursed over sm'.split_list output (runtime), so the compiler unrolled it until EJP0040 (more than 1000 dynamic if branches). Every recursive helper in the four contract notebooks and in slice E's harness helpers is now let rec (13 sites). Slices A and B rerun at the end of runner eoie-serial-checks-2. The gotcha is recorded for own helpers, not just lib's listm' naming.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_38 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 38u32, "2026-10-24T11:18Z", "eoie", "07:1x groom: progress check. Slices A-E for contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi are drafted and packaged in next-train stage S5. Typechecks: A and B rerun after the let rec and parse fixes; C and D are queued. The file's 42 blocks and native_tools.rs go once S5 installs. Still pending under this epic: the eoie_cli_harness legacy macros themselves (eoie_run block etc.), then rust_std_fs_mutation/mutation.spi (6 sites, 44,683 chars) as the next file by violating chars, per GRANULAR-HEAL rule 4.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_39 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 39u32, "2026-10-24T13:30Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:30 main: test placement (SPIRAL-NOTEBOOK-FILES note 1): 77% of eoie's 266 test blocks sit after their file's last definition, and 27 files are fully clustered (model.spi 10/10, notes_cli 9/9, window_model 8/8). User rule: tests interleave with the code they test. Move them while each file is touched for the granular migration.")
inl note_of_eoie_granular_migration_40 () = Note ("EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION", 40u32, "2026-10-25T00:44Z", "eoie", "20:44 Lab drain: the unlanded plan lab/EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION/r36-prune-patch-plan.md moved into this note verbatim (the file is deleted; PatchSpec is still live, so this plan is open work):\n# r36 (next session): prune the patch verb family\n\nRule: EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION note 2026-10-21 16:57 (0 calls in 14 days across clients, no one-call spec case, no caller in any repo). Evidence: note 2026-10-21 17:09 (0 real calls / 14 d, 0 spec cases, only eoie-internal callers; cutting eoie_cli's two edges frees 19 crates).\n\n## The code-shift trap (read before editing)\n\ncommand_spec_domain/model.spi numbers commands by position: `declared_code spec = union_case_index - 1`, and `handler_from_code (code + 1)` picks the case back. PatchSpec is case 2, so today status=0, patch=1, agile=2, bundle=3, proxy=4, help=5, and lease denied is the literal 7. Numeric consumers: 11 sites in eoie_cli_routing/routing_terminal.spi (e.g. `eoie_command_descriptor(\"2\")` for agile), 14 in command_spec_domain/model.spi, 2 in command_spec_domain/main.spi, 1 in eoie_cli_model/model.spi. Deleting the PatchSpec case shifts agile to 1 and breaks every numeric site silently.\n\nDecision rule for the slice (set before editing): if every numeric site can be replaced by a case-based call in the same slice (the routing blob asks by name or case, not by digit), delete the case. Otherwise keep the position stable with an explicit code per case (a `code_of` function matching each case to its number) and delete PatchSpec; never leave a placeholder case. Tie-break: the explicit code table (smaller diff, no blob growth).\n\n## Edits\n\n1. command_spec_domain/model.spi: drop PatchSpec and PatchHandler (and their arms in verb_spec_of, handler_value, command_catalog_witness), \"patch\" from the unknown-verb diagnostic, the usage line `patch: apply ...`, the `patch:check` subcommand effect, the help_catalog section. main.spi's `command_subcommand_effect_code \"patch:check\"` call.\n2. eoie_cli_model/model.spi: `patch_run` and its `PatchHandler => patch_run ()` arm.\n3. eoie_cli_routing/routing_terminal.spi: `EoiePatchAdapter` (lines ~133-151) and the usage text `<status|patch|agile|bundle|proxy|help>`.\n4. eoie_cli/Cargo.toml: eoie-patch-mutation, eoie-patch-rehearsal; workspace Cargo.toml members and Cargo.lock entries for every deleted crate.\n5. Delete the 19 crates newly unreachable from eoie_cli (exclusive-closure.ps1 output: backup_domain, eoie_patch_mutation, eoie_patch_rehearsal, patch_batch, patch_compat_driver, patch_compat_receipts, patch_compat_runtime, patch_compat_test_support, patch_domain, patch_effect_domain, patch_gated_app, patch_model, patch_mutation_app, patch_mutation_contract, patch_orchestration_domain, patch_preflight_contract, patch_rehearsal_app, patch_resume_contract, patch_source_adapter) and their dependents that only test them (backup_domain_probe, patch_authority_probe, patch_preflight_*_probe, patch_resume_*_probe, patch_source_adapter_probe, eoie_patch_mutation_contracts, eoie_patch_transaction_contracts, eoie_patch_grammar, eoie_patch_scan, multi_file_patch_*). Grep each stem across C:\\home\\git first (dangling rule); keep patch_control_domain and patch_driver_domain (eoie_fs_actions, eoie_batch_write, eoie_legacy_operations, evidence_currentness_domain use them).\n6. contracts_entry/cli_driver.spi patch cases (lines ~220-370, 465, 556-567) and eoie_coverage_smoke/smoke.spi patch-success / patch-repeat-failure.\n7. Inventories that name the crates: state/bench.spi, consolidation_fixtures.spi, coverage.spi, owner_growth.spi, runtime_drift.spi, migration.spi, standards/census.spi; then refresh evidence (state/evidence.spi hashes evidence/coverage/*.lcov) in the same release, or the currentness check fails (see help_catalog.rs, EOIE-SPIRAL-TESTS 2026-10-21 09:53).\n8. Checks: preview of every touched crate, the full notebook registry, cargo check --locked --workspace, one-call spec 34+/34+, `eoie help` and `eoie patch` (expect the unknown-verb diagnostic).")
inl fsharp_warm_runner () = Task ("FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER", "F# native tier through one warm process (user 2026-10-18: speed up where F# is redundant). The tier runs each main.fsx in a cold dotnet fsi: in today's accept, 544 rows took 3,151 s summed (median 4.2 s, p90 10.2 s, about 26 min wall on 2 lanes), almost all of it startup. Like kotlin-server: a native-shims fsharp-runner keeps one FSI evaluation session warm, evaluates each script and returns its value and stdout. Target: the same outcomes as the cold tier, row for row, in under 5 min", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "matrix,fsharp,speed", "current", "current")
inl note_of_fsharp_warm_runner_1 () = Note ("FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER", 1u32, "2026-10-18T18:25Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 14:25 main-thread: prototype in lab/FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER. warm.ps1 runs one dotnet fsi --quiet session through stdin and does a #load per row. Each row's copy is main.fsx plus the cold tier's final pipe, which prints an SPIRAL_WARM_END <code> marker instead of exit; a separate printfn SPIRAL_WARM_DONE submission ends the row. A throw prints no END, so the row exits 1, as cold. A dead process (a real exit, a stack overflow) records its exit code, and a timeout kills and restarts the session. stdout uses the cold tier's hashing (CRLF to LF, TrimEnd, sha16). compare.ps1 replays the accepted F# rows of single-flight-20261018-123705. First 40 rows: warm 31 s in one session vs cold 182 s summed (5.9x), 0 differing (native status, exit, stdout hash). Next: all 544 rows after today's accept (no heavy runs during the 15:30-17:00 tibia live block), then fold it into test.ps1's native tier as an F# batch like kotlin-server, behind the native signature.")
inl note_of_fsharp_warm_runner_2 () = Note ("FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER", 2u32, "2026-10-18T18:29Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 14:29 main-thread: integration ready in lab/FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER/apply.py; dry run on a copy of test.ps1 applies and parses. Final runner lab/FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER/fsharp-warm/warm.ps1, which becomes tests/native-shims/fsharp-warm/: stderr is drained with async reads after the DONE marker, and error FS rows are build-fail like cold (checked: FS0027 rows build-fail, ok rows ran with exit; 5 rows in 8 s, first-row session start 5.8 s, then 0.2-0.7 s each). test.ps1 patch: a warm batch before lane construction, 2 sessions in parallel, results into nativeResults (a timeout maps to ran/timeout as in cold), and F# jobs join the memo-store loop. Get-ShimKey Fsharp = fsharp-warm, so a runner edit re-keys only F# rows. SPIRAL_FSHARP_COLD=1 keeps the cold path. It also fixes a glued '}$shimsByBackend' line from my 10:03 shim-key patch. Apply after the 17:00 accept; the first review after that reruns every native row once (the native-tier block is in the signature).")
inl note_of_fsharp_warm_runner_3 () = Note ("FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER", 3u32, "2026-10-19T03:44Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-18 23:44 main-thread: applied after the pack 3 accept (lab apply.py, without the SPIRAL_FSHARP_COLD opt-out, since the user wants no skip switches). In the pack 4 review the warm tier ran 549 F# rows in 2 sessions in 320 s, against the cold tier's ~37 min, but 7 mega rows (6 mega_brzozowski_derivatives roots plus omniledger all_terminals) hit the 60 s per-row budget inside the session, where they used to finish cold (exit 0 / 1). Fixed in test.ps1: a warm timeout is not recorded; the row stays in nativeJobs and reruns cold in a fresh fsi through the normal lanes, and it leaves fsharpWarmJobs so the memo loop counts it once. The pack 4 accept (running) is the proof: the 7 rows should match their accepted exits")
inl note_of_fsharp_warm_runner_4 () = Note ("FSHARP-WARM-RUNNER", 4u32, "2026-10-19T04:29Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 00:29 main-thread: pack 4 ACCEPTED (run single-flight-20261018-234436, 7,007 rows, DISAGREE 0). Against its review, the only changes are the 7 mega F# rows: warm timeouts there, cold reruns now matching their accepted exits. The warm runner plus cold fallback is in the baseline. The pack also carried the 7 Zig rows (ZIG-COVERAGE-C-ONLY), the Infer shadowing fix, Zig main returning any value, the tokens verb and the clearer package and module errors")
inl zig_primary_oracle () = Task ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", "Make Zig the first oracle (-Oracle Zig,C) (user 2026-10-18: promote Zig). Measured 2026-10-17: -Oracle Zig and -Oracle C both give DISAGREE 0 on 5,388 rows; the only difference, dynamic_array_bounds_negative, has Known entries per oracle. Today's accept: C and Zig differ on 1 of 459 shared samples. The switch changes the baseline's oracle column, so it lands with its own reviewed accept", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "matrix,zig,oracle", "current", "current")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_1 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 1u32, "2026-10-19T13:15Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:15 lap 2 grain: predicted the queued -Oracle Zig,C replay from today's results (single-flight-20261019-072348, no run): Zig has 467 rows, 465 agree with C, 1 known, 1 no-c; 65 C samples have no Zig row and fall back to C (detail oracle C (no Zig row)), so they cannot disagree; because Zig and C agree on all shared samples, swapping the first oracle only changes rows whose verdict hinges on a C-scoped Known. Exactly one such row would turn DISAGREE: samples/dynamic_array_bounds_negative on Rust (Rust panics exit 1, Zig traps exit 3); its only Known entry was scoped Oracle = C, while C/Delphi/Wasm/Kotlin/Lua already had Zig-scoped entries and Lean/Bend exit 3 agree with Zig. Added the missing Zig-scoped Rust entry to apps/compiler/tmp/tests/matrix.psd1 (Import-PowerShellDataFile -SkipLimitCheck loads it: 17 Known entries, 11 for this sample). Also zig_lib_console (Zig-only sample) will newly score its Fsharp/Rust/Wasm rows against Zig (all exit 0 today). Expected replay result: DISAGREE 0, 1 more known. Next: when main runs the HEAVY QUEUE replay, compare its verdict counts with this prediction; if DISAGREE 0, make Zig,C the test.ps1 default (main's file)")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_2 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 2u32, "2026-10-19T13:51Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 09:51 measured with -Oracle Zig,C on today's tree (review-keys): round A DISAGREE 1 = dynamic_array_bounds_negative Rust (helper 2 added its Zig-scoped Known entry after round A loaded), round B DISAGREE 1 = samples/zig_lib_console Fsharp, a real lib bug the C-first oracle never compared (the sample has no C row): sm'.obj_to_string on F# printed True/False via .ToString() where Rust, Zig and Wasm print true/false (Python's str() has the same flaw). Fixed in lib sm'.spi: obj_to_string_fsharp and obj_to_string_python print lowercase bools, test obj_to_string_prints_bools_lowercase (fsharp, cuda, rust, zig). With both, Zig-first should reach DISAGREE 0; next: gate sm' then a review with -Oracle Zig,C to confirm, then switch the default order.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_3 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 3u32, "2026-10-19T13:51Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 09:51 lap 3 grain, a cross-platform argument measured from the first Linux CI run (39258592236, see CI-OFFLOAD note 5): C's abort() exits 134 (SIGABRT) on Linux but 3 on Windows, so under the C-first oracle samples/managed_string_invalid_utf8_slice scores agree-fail on F#, Rust, Zig, Python and TypeScript (all exit 3) and the C row itself is the odd one; with Zig first, those 5 rows agree with the Zig oracle on both platforms and only C's own row (134) is off, i.e. the platform dependence lands on the C row where it belongs. Same for exit widths: zig_exit_wide exits 49 (305 mod 256) on Linux C/Rust/Zig/Gleam/Python while F# reports 305, which is DISAGREE under either oracle (an F# tier matter, not an oracle one). So Zig-first also makes Linux CI verdicts closer to Windows ones. Still waiting on the queued Windows replay (prediction from lap 2: DISAGREE 0 with the added Rust Known). Next: when the replay lands, propose the default order Zig,C to main with these two data points")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_4 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 4u32, "2026-10-19T14:01Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 10:01 the obj_to_string bool fix is green: Cells gate of tree lib/spiral/sm'.spi 42/42, 0 type errors (heavy-queue step sm-tree-gate, 09:51-10:00), including obj_to_string_prints_bools_lowercase on fsharp, cuda, rust, zig.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_5 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 5u32, "2026-10-19T15:15Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:15 lap 5 grain: the evidence is complete: main's 09:50 replay with -Oracle Zig,C had DISAGREE 1 = zig_lib_console F# bool text, and that lib fix is green (sm'.spi gate 42/42, 10:01), so Zig-first is DISAGREE 0 on today's tree; plus the Linux data point (lap 3). Staged the flip as lab/ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE/flip-default.py (test.ps1:19 default @('C','Zig') -> @('Zig','C') and the AGENTS.md default sentence; dry run: both anchors match once). Queued for main to apply between runs after the core switch accept, so the switch's own review keeps today's oracle and the flip gets its own reviewed accept. Decision recorded for main: apply after the switch accept, not with it, so the two oracle-column changes stay separable.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_6 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 6u32, "2026-10-19T15:32Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:32 lap 6: read test.ps1's oracle passes (999-1033) to check that the flip keeps the Known scoping working. The first oracle's scoped Known entries (Get-ScopedKnown on line 1007) mask DISAGREE and build-fail rows. Each further oracle gets its own scoped set (lines 1022-1030), and it compares only rows that already agree with the first oracle. With Zig,C, the Zig-scoped dynamic_array_bounds_negative entries for the unchecked backends become the primary mask, and the C-scoped entries for the checked backends cover the second pass, which is the mirror of today's C,Zig. So no matrix.psd1 edit is needed with the flip, and flip-default.py stays a two-line change.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_7 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 7u32, "2026-10-19T15:42Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:42 progress bookkeeping: evidence complete (replay DISAGREE 0 after the lib fix, Linux data point, Known scoping verified) and the flip is staged as flip-default.py; left: main applies it after the switch accept and does the reviewed accept. Progress 80.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_8 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 8u32, "2026-10-19T15:52Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 11:52 lap 7, two facts for the flip. (1) CI picks it up automatically: workflow.ps1 runs test.ps1 -Mode single-flight -Suite <suite> -Native -Parallel 2 -Accept with no -Oracle, so after flip-default.py the Linux job's accepted oracle column is Zig-first too. (2) This narrows lap 3's Linux argument: Test-SharedFailure (test.ps1) scores two failure exits as agree-fail, so C's abort 134 against the others' 3 is agree-fail under either order, never DISAGREE. The flip changes only which rows carry agree-fail (5 rows with C first, C's own row with Zig first), which is cleaner but does not change the DISAGREE count. The case for the flip is still the user's direction plus DISAGREE 0 locally.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_9 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 9u32, "2026-10-19T16:27Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:27 lap 8 grain: flip-default is applied in the tree (test.ps1 Oracle Zig,C). Review prediction from the accepted switch baseline single-flight-20261019-113145 (7,020 rows): 466 samples have both a C and a Zig native run, and exactly 1 differs, dynamic_array_bounds_negative (C exit 0, Zig 3), which has Known entries per oracle; 65 samples run C but not Zig, so C stays their oracle through the fallback; one sample runs Zig without C, zig_lib_console, whose 4 rows are no-c today and gain a Zig oracle after the flip. Corrected 13:0x: this holds for rows of backends other than C and Zig; the flip also fills the oracle column of C's own rows, empties Zig's, and renames no-c to no-zig, which check-flip.ps1 normalizes. Done when that accept shows DISAGREE 0 and this split")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_10 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 10u32, "2026-10-19T16:54Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 12:54 lap 9 grain: the Done check is one call now: lab/ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE/check-flip.ps1 -Run <run dir> compares every row's oracle column with the switch baseline single-flight-20261019-113145, marks a change as expected when it is on dynamic_array_bounds_negative or zig_lib_console (lap 8 prediction) or when that row's own residual, exit or stdout moved (pack 7's changes), requires DISAGREE 0, and prints ZIG-FLIP-OK or exits 1 with the unexplained rows listed. First version compared every row and would have flagged ~1,000 C/Zig/no-c cells on a correct flip; fixed 13:0x: C and Zig rows are left out of the diff, no-c/no-zig count as one verdict, and DISAGREE is checked on every row including C. Positive test on the Zig,C run single-flight-20261019-124451: 10 verdict changes, all on dynamic_array_bounds_negative (7 Known re-scopings) and zig_lib_console (3 no-c to agree), C rows agree 465 known 3 no-zig 32, DISAGREE 0, ZIG-FLIP-OK. A row whose oracle row moved while its own output did not shows as unexplained, which is what the review should look at by hand")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_11 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 11u32, "2026-10-19T17:29Z", "helper-lane-2", "2026-10-19 13:29 lap 10 grain: the three non-run parts of Done are in place: test.ps1:19 defaults -Oracle to @('Zig', 'C'), apps/compiler/tmp/AGENTS.md names the 2026-10-19 flip to Zig,C, and check-flip.ps1 passed on the reviewed run 124451 (10 predicted changes, DISAGREE 0, ZIG-FLIP-OK). Left: accept single-flight-20261019-125623 (compile done 13:01, native tier running, baseline not yet rewritten) -> check-flip.ps1 -Run 125623 -> Done (main)")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_12 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 12u32, "2026-10-19T17:43Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 13:43 pack 7 ACCEPTED single-flight-20261019-125623 (7,020 rows, DISAGREE 0, 0 differing cells vs review 124451, C rows unchanged); test.ps1 defaults to -Oracle Zig,C and check-flip.ps1 on the accept prints ZIG-FLIP-OK: 10 non-oracle verdict changes all on the predicted samples, C rows against Zig agree 465 known 3 no-zig 32, DISAGREE 0.")
inl note_of_zig_primary_oracle_13 () = Note ("ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE", 13u32, "2026-10-22T03:28Z", "main", "23:28 lab drain (user 21:5x-22:0x: finish holders, delete a folder once its item has landed): flip-default.py landed: test.ps1 now defaults to Oracle @(Zig, C); check-flip.ps1 was the one-off verification already in the notes. Removed spiral/lab/ZIG-PRIMARY-ORACLE (2 files).")
