inl note_of_core_lib_consolidate_37 () = Note ("CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE", 37u32, "2026-10-20T02:42Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-19 22:42 main: one more consumer site, found by the hangulize lane: alphabet/apps/documents/documents.spi test blocks at 528 and 561 handed a multi-line ;[ ] literal on the next line to am'.to_vec (the rule only matched the literal and to_vec on one line; the plain compile skips test blocks, so the earlier type check passed); fixed with |> am'.base, Cells gate of documents.spi 1/1, 0 type errors; a sweep of dice, alphabet, polyglot and spiral for ] then |> am'.to_vec finds no other failing site (dice ui, apps/spiral, sm, polyglot chat contract all compile).")
inl note_of_core_lib_consolidate_38 () = Note ("CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE", 38u32, "2026-10-20T06:18Z", "main-thread", "2026-10-20 02:18 main: probe-lib.ps1 under-reported type errors. The ETY counter matched only line-start errors under lib/spiral, so errors in any other package printed type errors: 0, and so did a FatalError, which Cells prints with every error on one ** (Mix) line. Seen on the SEFAZ-XSD lab: 30, 8, 3 and 11 real errors shown as 0. The counter now matches any .spi/.spir path, inline or at line start; rechecked on the four saved raw outputs.")
