inl note_of_lab_sweep_eoie_1 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-EOIE", 1u32, "2026-10-22T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:39 x: filed for eoie from the 21:4x inventory.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_eoie_2 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-EOIE", 2u32, "2026-10-24T11:20Z", "eoie", "07:20 groom (user 10-24 06:56 via main: every repo stops the lab pattern; the formatter halted the user's git loop). Measured now: eoie/lab holds 14 folders and 337 files; EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN alone has 286 (night logs and scripts), all last written by 10-23 15:33. Rule, written before acting: (1) nothing is deleted while an eoie release runs (regen refuses to publish if repo files change mid-run; GE3's release runs now), so start after GE3 installs; (2) per folder, a draft still in flight moves to its committable place (src/spec, or the scratch train folder that applies it) and evidence becomes a summary note on the owning item; then the folder goes, after a stem grep across sibling repos (dangling-check-by-stem); (3) Done items' folders go first; (4) no new lab/ folder from now on: experiments start in their real place. Raised to P0 because the user repeated the request.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_eoie_3 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-EOIE", 3u32, "2026-10-25T00:32Z", "eoie", "20:32 Started late. The 07:20 rule said to start after GE3 installed (11:46), and I let the release train push this back for 9 hours: drift. The user asked again at 20:2x. The drain happens before CLEAN launches, because the regen's publish check takes an inventory of the whole checkout, lab/ included; start-CLEAN waits on scratch clean\\hold until this is done. Rules per folder, written before moving anything: (a) a script a release or after-install check runs (EOIE-JOBS checks, read-e2e, one-call-runner, holder-probe) moves to compiler-contracts/ as test-<subject>.ps1, and every caller is repointed in the same step; (b) a draft crate or doc that already landed, or lands in CLEAN, is deleted after a diff against the CLEAN tree, with a note naming what replaced it; (c) measurement scripts and their TSVs: the finding goes into a note on the owning item, then they are deleted, because the method belongs in an eoie verb, not a script; (d) unlanded patches (EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS' five apply scripts) and unlanded plans (the r36 patch-verb prune) are the next release's first content: the patches move to the next-release folder, and the plan text goes into a note on its item; (e) EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN's night folder holds archived copies of scratch scripts and logs whose facts are in that item's notes, so it goes; (f) a stem grep across eoie, the hooks and sibling repos comes before each delete; (g) lab/ is removed entirely, and no new lab/ folder is created.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_eoie_4 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-EOIE", 4u32, "2026-10-25T00:45Z", "eoie", "20:45 Done: eoie/lab is gone (328 files, 14 folders). (a) 9 checks that releases run moved to compiler-contracts/ as test-job-hidden-window, test-job-orphan-wait, test-job-timeout-tree, test-job-inherit-pipe, test-ps-verb, test-read-verb, test-one-call-spec, test-window-holder and test-window-holder-detail. Relative paths were fixed and 88 scratch callers repointed. Re-run from the new place on the installed eoie: hidden window 2/2, one-call spec 39/46 (same as the 11:46 install). (b) Superseded drafts deleted after a diff against live and the CLEAN tree: eoie_adoption, agile_task_query, eoie_log_sequences (its verb_draft became eoie_table_sequences), eoie_tree_lease, the old AGENTS.md draft, and spec-cases-r33 (cases 38-40 are in spec/one-call.md). (c) Measurement scripts and TSVs deleted; their findings were already in notes on their items. (d) The two plans went into notes verbatim: EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES note 40 (classification) and EOIE-GRANULAR-MIGRATION note 40 (r36 patch-verb prune). EOIE-MEMORY-VERBS' five unlanded apply scripts moved to the scratch next-release folder. (e) EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN's night folder deleted. git shows 4 tracked lab files as deleted (the user commits). No new lab/ from now on.")
inl lab_sweep_gate () = Task ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", "main team: the stop gate enforces the lab rule at the deadline: when an armed run reaches its deadline (or the deadline file is about to be deleted), run eoie lab audit --since <session start> on every repo the session touched and block the final stop with the listed files until each is promoted, pruned or carried with a note naming it; no sleep or poll in the hook (AUTONOMOUS-STOP-GATE rules)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 0u32, Paused, "EOIE-LAB-AUDIT", "lab,main,claude,hooks", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lab_sweep_gate () = Planning ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Unassigned)
inl note_of_lab_sweep_gate_1 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", 1u32, "2026-10-22T01:39Z", "x", "2026-10-21 21:39 x: proposal only; main owns ~/.claude/hooks/autonomous-gate.ps1 and nobody else edits it. Session start = the deadline file's creation time or the session's first transcript entry.")
inl note_of_lab_sweep_gate_2 () = Note ("LAB-SWEEP-GATE", 2u32, "2026-10-22T01:41Z", "main", "21:41 main proposal only (no hook change; a peer cannot grant hook edits and the rule reached me through x): at the deadline pass, the gate would run eoie lab audit --since <deadline file creation time> once (bounded by the 30 s Stop timeout, so the audit must be a fast directory-time scan; no sleep or poll), and block the final stop once with the listed files and the required lab: line, then pass on the next stop if the last message contains a lab: line. Depends on EOIE-LAB-AUDIT existing; until then the gate could print the count from a Get-ChildItem LastWriteTime scan of the touched repos' lab folders, which took 261 ms for 253 files on spiral/lab (107 folders, warm file cache; measured 21:42).")
inl post_1_in_fork () = Task ("POST-1-IN-FORK", "Post 1 moves into the i574n/The-Spiral-Language fork (user 2026-10-21 22:0x: this blog post should be moved to upstream's fork somewhere there, configuring the blog clone somehow as deps, also weird name): the post module and the data and samples behind it live in the fork; the blog repo is cloned into the fork's deps by the fork's init step so the post compiles against blog/engine; the post gets a plain name instead of vanilla_start; then spiral/lab/UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA is drained (and blog/engine/vanilla_start.spi leaves the blog repo)", Story, P1, D3, 100u32, Done, "", "blog,fork,lab-drain,main", "current", "current")
inl note_of_post_1_in_fork_1 () = Note ("POST-1-IN-FORK", 1u32, "2026-10-22T02:03Z", "main", "22:03 current state (read only): the post is in two places, blog repo engine/vanilla_start.spi (module in engine/package.spiproj, first entry of generate.spi; uncommitted with other blog changes) and spiral/lab/UPSTREAM-POST-1-VANILLA (about 30 files: post/vanilla_start.spi, make-post.ps1 generator, post-gate.ps1, fixes.tsv, branch-commits.tsv, before/after result TSVs, 8 patch diffs, 3 regression samples c_array_create_reused, c_self_tail_loop_heap, c_user_global, an F# build driver). Fork: C:\\home\\git\\The-Spiral-Language, branch i574n, origin i574n/The-Spiral-Language plus remote mrakgr; spiral's deps clones are spiral/deps/The-Spiral-Language (mrakgr master) and polyglot/deps/The-Spiral-Language (i574n master). Open: where in the fork the post goes, how its init clones blog into deps, and the new name. Related lab folders: UPSTREAM-CHANGES-POST, UPSTREAM-POST-2-C-SELF-TAIL.")
inl note_of_post_1_in_fork_2 () = Note ("POST-1-IN-FORK", 2u32, "2026-10-22T03:46Z", "main", "23:46 moved (user 23:1x: post in fork too). Fork C:\\home\\git\\The-Spiral-Language (branch i574n, uncommitted for the user): scripts/init.ps1 makes deps/blog and deps/spiral (junctions to sibling checkouts when present, else clones of i574n/blog and i574n/spiral; the blog engine expects spiral beside the blog); .gitignore gains /deps/ and /target/; posts/upstream_consolidation/ holds upstream_consolidation.spi (renamed from vanilla_start: slug upstream-consolidation, title Upstream Consolidation; otherwise byte-identical to the blog copy), make.ps1 (the generator, reading data/), data/ (branch-commits.tsv, decisions.tsv from CORE-LIB-CONSOLIDATE, fixes.tsv) and fixes/ (8 patch diffs, 3 repro samples, before/after results, build-driver/run-fixes/export-fix/make-patch with fork-relative paths, the F# driver); scripts/post.ps1 builds the post inside target/post/engine (an overlay of deps/blog/engine with the post module before build and packageDir pointed at deps/spiral/lib) and runs its tests through deps/spiral Cells. Gate: 2 discovered, 2 executed, 2 passed (job main-fork-post). Blog: post unhooked (package.spiproj back to the index version, generate.spi back to showcase.entries, engine/vanilla_start.spi removed); generate.rs regenerating in job main-blog-regen. Once relative package entries install (PACK-AFTER-NIGHT), the overlay can become a plain package.spiproj listing ../../deps/blog/engine-.")
inl note_of_post_1_in_fork_3 () = Note ("POST-1-IN-FORK", 3u32, "2026-10-22T06:22Z", "main", "02:22 main: every title part is done except the blog regeneration. The post is in the fork with its init deps and plain name, the post gate passes from the fork, the lab is drained, and blog/engine/vanilla_start.spi is gone, with package.spiproj and generate.spi back to the index version. Still open: blog/engine/generate.rs still names the old post (line 76) until it is regenerated. The heavy job main-blog-regen sat queued since 23:xx and was stopped at 02:22 under the compile hold for eoie's release ABC. It reruns next (heavy, cargo release build), then this item is Done (user commits blog and fork).")
inl note_of_post_1_in_fork_4 () = Note ("POST-1-IN-FORK", 4u32, "2026-10-23T16:44Z", "main", "2026-10-23 12:44 main: closed by its own rule (02:22 note: done once blog/engine/generate.rs is regenerated): generate.rs was rewritten 2026-10-22 06:43 and no longer names vanilla_start (grep: 0 hits). The post, its init deps and data live in the fork (uncommitted for the user); committing blog and the fork is the user's.")
