inl note_of_eoie_ci_parity_1 () = Note ("EOIE-CI-PARITY", 1u32, "2026-10-22T22:00Z", "eoie-lane", "18:00 filed from x's candidate (EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES note, 14:28, memory ci-parity-toolchains) plus my own evidence today: eoie CI moved to nightly-2026-10-18 while this laptop's default is nightly-2025-05-09, so a local test-dev-workflow passed while CI was red. The cause (cargo's build-dir layout) only showed after pinning RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN to CI's channel (EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW). x saw the same with zig-dev 0.18 against 0.17.0. Pure model drafted (scratch f5/src/eoie_ci_parity_model: setup_action context per 'uses:' line, typed ci_tool keys, workflow_pins, then parity SameVersion | Differs ci local | MissingLocally; tests on the eoie workflow against today's laptop pins). Standards 0 findings; Cells preview after F (no compile beside F). Generic: no repo names in the code, any workflow that uses those actions.")
inl note_of_eoie_ci_parity_2 () = Note ("EOIE-CI-PARITY", 2u32, "2026-10-23T03:03Z", "eoie-lane", "23:03 from main (RUST-NIGHTLY-EVERYWHERE): bare cargo calls in tracked eoie scripts (compiler-contracts/renew-cold-rebuild.ps1:54, test-dev-workflow.ps1:31, test-selected-build.ps1:14) resolve to the machine default nightly-2025-05-09 (rustc 1.88), while eoie CI pins nightly-2026-10-18, and no repo has a rust-toolchain.toml. That gap is what hid today's CI failure (EOIE-CI-DEV-WORKFLOW). Candidate fix: rust-toolchain.toml with channel = \"nightly-2026-10-18\" at the eoie root, so local and CI match. Rule, written before trying it: adopt it if a scratch copy builds eoie-cli and passes test-dev-workflow and the 9 F-candidate notebooks under the pinned toolchain with no new failures, and its debug build time stays within 1.5x of today's. Then the docs' 'Rust 1.88' mentions are updated in the same change. Not tonight: F6 holds the tree lease, and a pin changes every local build.")
inl note_of_eoie_ci_parity_3 () = Note ("EOIE-CI-PARITY", 3u32, "2026-10-23T14:01Z", "eoie", "10:01 verb drafted (scratch f6/src/eoie_ci_parity: model + parity + entry, HostFree LibReferenced). The model moved from hand-rolled pin lists to core list + listm'.try_find_/listm.map/fold (09:47 check pass on the old shape). Added: version_from_output per tool (rustup active toolchain without the host triple, gleam/rebar3 second word, zig/otp/elixir first line), pin_matches (patch releases match at a dot, never a dev build, Rust channels whole), probes (rustup show active-toolchain, zig or SPIRAL_ZIG, erl OTP_VERSION, elixir --short-version, gleam --version, rebar3 version; .cmd/.bat names tried), workflows joined with a uses: boundary, repeated pins dropped, refusal on no pins. The lib gap went into lib: process.try_capture_combined_list (Rust + Gleam arms, test) in a lib copy, slice ci-parity/apply-lib-try-capture.ps1 (baseline-guarded). Measured on this laptop vs eoie gh-pages.yml: rust nightly-2025-05-09 vs nightly-2026-10-18 differs, zig 0.18.0-dev.146 vs 0.17.0 differs, rebar3 3.28.0 vs 3.27.3 differs, otp 29.1.2, elixir 1.20.4 and gleam 1.19.2 same. Checks (notebooks for model + lib process, standards) are queued for after tibia's live block; then slice ci-parity/apply-ci-parity.ps1 joins the release after L.")
inl note_of_eoie_ci_parity_4 () = Note ("EOIE-CI-PARITY", 4u32, "2026-10-23T15:58Z", "eoie", "11:58 eoie: x's measured table (EOIE-MEMORY-FEATURES note 33) folded in; I had drafted without reading it, now corrected. (1) Rust follows what a harness resolves, not rustc --version: the repo's rust-toolchain.toml or legacy rust-toolchain channel if that toolchain is installed (rustup toolchain list), else missing; no file means rustup's default. A toolchain file also pins CI when the workflow has no setup-rust channel. A Rust mismatch suggests only 'rustup toolchain install <channel>', never a direct-rustc override. (2) Python is a tool (setup-python python-version; python --version). (3) Every mismatched row prints a fix line: for zig, 'fix: SPIRAL_ZIG=<scoop zig matching the pin>'; for others, a 'candidate:' path, both found by scanning ~/scoop/apps/<tool>*/<version>/<tool>.exe with the same dot-boundary match. Tests added for toolchain-file parsing, installed lists, rust_local, the python pin and fix lines. Model and parity notebooks pass (11:52) on the f6 lib copy; ci parity remains in release M.")
inl note_of_eoie_ci_parity_5 () = Note ("EOIE-CI-PARITY", 5u32, "2026-10-23T16:41Z", "eoie", "12:41 eoie: lib gate on the lib-gaps copy (lib_gate.ps1, process compiler, own MIX_BUILD_PATH; job-1792770026831): am' 12/12, testing 8/8, env current_executable passes, sm' concat_array and growable tests pass; process.try_capture_combined_list passes on Rust, but its Gleam arm crashed with Erlang badarg on the third call (after a missing program and a failing exit both passed), the successful stderr_to_stdout capture, while the existing capture_combined_list passes the same case. eoie needs only Rust, so the Gleam arm and the test's gleam tag are dropped from the slice (lib already has Rust-only functions); a Gleam port is a follow-up. Reds in untouched tests (sm' format_fixed_avoids_ties zig, show_floats delphi/lean, range typescript; env get_environment_variable typescript) are being baselined on the tree lib (main has no recorded baseline; job-1792773558090), since the landing must not hide new reds.")
