inl rust_let_immutable () = Task ("RUST-LET-IMMUTABLE", "Rust backend binds a local with let only when the output never mutates it: 14,786 let mut bindings over the 470 matrix main.rs, 98.3% never assigned, mutably borrowed, called or mutated through a non-read-only method; the blanket allow(unused_mut) hid it", TaskKind, P1, D1, 60u32, Active, "PACK-NEXT-4", "compiler,rust,codegen,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_rust_let_immutable () = Planning ("RUST-LET-IMMUTABLE", Minutes 30u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_rust_let_immutable_1 () = Note ("RUST-LET-IMMUTABLE", 1u32, "2026-10-22T22:56Z", "main", "2026-10-22 18:56 main: measured on the next3b pre-matrix snapshot with scratch rust_let_immutable_mirror.py (a conservative whitelist: any assignment or compound assignment to vN or a field/index path of it, &mut vN, a direct call vN(...), or a method on vN or its fields outside a read-only list keeps mut). 12 of the largest transformed files (the mega DFA benches, native_cube, static closure chain) pass rustc --emit=metadata on nightly-2026-10-18, so no E0384/E0596. Implemented as immutableRustLets, the last pass after cacheRustStringLiterals (%TEMP%\\pack-next4\\rust-let-immutable.ps1, in PACK-NEXT-4). Review rule fixed now: Rust outputs differ from the snapshot only by let mut -> let (both sides normalized), no new Rust build-fail, DISAGREE 0.")
inl note_of_rust_let_immutable_2 () = Note ("RUST-LET-IMMUTABLE", 2u32, "2026-10-23T23:28Z", "main", "2026-10-23 19:28 main: status fixed. The change is implemented and staged in PACK-NEXT-4, so it is Active, not Planned. The next4 composite is decided by review-3, requeued in %TEMP%\\cells-pack\\requeue-after-block.ps1 chain B after recompose-stack; this item's review rule (note 1) is applied there.")
inl note_of_rust_let_immutable_3 () = Note ("RUST-LET-IMMUTABLE", 3u32, "2026-10-24T00:09Z", "main", "2026-10-23 20:09 main: Kotlin, Swift and TypeScript already have the same improvement pending: pack-next6's kotlin-swift-ts-locals.ps1 (valAtAssignment) fuses 'var vN: T = dummy' with its single following assignment and emits val/let/const. A Python mirror over today's 452 main.kt measured what such a pass does: 10,600 declarations fused, 10,421 val (about 71% of 14,718 var bindings), and Kotlin output 53,321 -> 42,721 lines (-20%), with the dummy zero allocations gone. My duplicate tree-based draft is deleted.")
inl eoie_show_note_filter () = Task ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", "agile show reads part of an item's notes in one call: --last N (the newest N notes), --since <ISO time>, --grep <regex> (notes whose text matches), so a session resuming an item with 100+ notes reads only what it needs instead of piping the whole item through Select-Object or Select-String", Story, P3, D2, 70u32, Active, "", "eoie,agile", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_show_note_filter () = Planning ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", Minutes 30u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_1 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 1u32, "2026-10-22T23:05Z", "tibia-lane", "Request from tibia-lane, 2026-10-22: TIBIA-EVENT-TIME has 102 notes and TIBIA-PARTY about 50; every resume today used agile show ... | Select-Object -Last N or | Select-String <word>, which is the shell bypass eoie-first forbids. Expected output: the same header lines, then only the selected notes with their original numbers (so note-edit still targets them).")
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_2 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 2u32, "2026-10-23T05:29Z", "eoie", "01:29 eoie: read the code for a design. agile show (agile_task_inspection) gets the notes block preformatted from agile_note_listing::eoie_agile_notes_text and prints it whole; note lines carry no numbers, though note-edit takes them. The filter belongs in agile_note_listing: a typed note_filter union (Newest n | Since iso | Matching regex), folded over the parsed notes, rendering each kept note as '#<n> <time>  <author>  <text>' and the header 'notes (kept/total)'. agile_show_entry reads --last/--since/--grep through an order-free flag fold, like agile_task_query's query_flag GADT, which also migrates its legacy positional '--json' check (AGENTS: touching a legacy function migrates it). Unfiltered output stays byte-identical, since CLI tests assert it. Not drafted tonight: compile previews are blocked while the release batch holds Cells, and it is P3.")
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_3 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 3u32, "2026-10-23T06:22Z", "eoie", "02:22 eoie: phase 1 drafted for release J (scratch note-filter/apply-note-filter.ps1, chained in apply-rJ; dry run clean on the post-K tree). agile_note_listing (HostFree, LibReferenced) gains a note_filter module: AllNotes | NewestNotes n | NotesMatching text (case-insensitive over text and author). It renders kept notes as '#<n> <time>  <author>  <text>' under 'notes (kept/total)', with n the stored note number that note-edit takes. Count parsing uses lib convert.try_convert: no host code, and an unreadable count keeps every note. Exported as eoie_agile_notes_filtered_text(text, id, mode, value); the test block covers newest, text, author and an unreadable count. Phase 2: agile show --last/--grep calls it, done together with agile_task_inspection's lib migration (its show flags are a legacy positional check). --since waits for a lib string comparison.")
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_4 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 4u32, "2026-10-23T18:25Z", "eoie", "14:25 eoie: phase 2 drafted (scratch note-filter/apply-show-note-flags.ps1, in release M after J's phase 1): agile show <root> <id> --last <n> | --grep <word> prints the header and only the kept notes as '#<n> <time>  <author>  <text>' under 'notes (kept/total)', through agile_note_listing's eoie_agile_notes_filtered_text. show_format gains ShowFiltered (mode, value), parsed as typed cases instead of the one positional --json check, and an unknown option says 'options are --json, --last <n> or --grep <word>'. CLI test in agile_task_notes/notes_cli.spi: three notes, --last 1 shows only #3, --grep CLUE (case-insensitive) shows only #2, a bogus option leaves state unchanged. Applies and is idempotent on the post-L tree; typecheck and notes_cli queued behind main's matrix. --since stays open (needs a lib string comparison).")
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_5 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 5u32, "2026-10-24T02:26Z", "main", "2026-10-23 22:1x main: gap hit while grooming: the installed eoie answers agile show <root> <id> --grep with an operand-count error, so --last/--since/--grep are not in the released binary yet; filtered in PowerShell instead. Counts toward releasing this item.")
inl note_of_eoie_show_note_filter_6 () = Note ("EOIE-SHOW-NOTE-FILTER", 6u32, "2026-10-24T23:44Z", "eoie", "19:43 Provisional estimate 30m from the grooming rule (EOIE-AGILE-CHECK-FIELDS note): D2 at 70%. Replace it with milestone sizing.")
inl c_fuse_declarations () = Task ("C-FUSE-DECLARATIONS", "C backend declares and initializes in one line: 13,863 of 16,343 split declarations (T vN; then vN = e;) are directly followed by their single assignment, 14.8% of non-blank C output lines", TaskKind, P1, D1, 60u32, Active, "PACK-NEXT-4", "compiler,c,codegen,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_c_fuse_declarations () = Planning ("C-FUSE-DECLARATIONS", Minutes 30u32, Load Heavy, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_c_fuse_declarations_1 () = Note ("C-FUSE-DECLARATIONS", 1u32, "2026-10-22T23:06Z", "main", "2026-10-22 19:06 main: measured on the next3b pre-matrix snapshot (507 main.c, scratch c_split_decl_census.py). Pass fuseCDeclarations (%TEMP%\\pack-next4\\c-fuse-declarations.ps1, in PACK-NEXT-4) runs on codegenC's finished program text: a line INDENT T vN; directly followed by INDENT vN = e; at the same indent, where e does not name vN and T has no storage class (static/extern/typedef/register: a fused static initializer would run once), becomes INDENT T vN = e;. In C (unlike C++) a jump past an initialized declaration is legal and leaves it as indeterminate as before, and no VLA is emitted, so behavior is unchanged. Mirror (c_fuse_decl_mirror.py): 138,961 -> 125,098 lines (-10.0% on top of blank lines); gcc -fsyntax-only on the 40 largest fused files: 38 pass, 2 fail on poll.h exactly as their originals do. Review rule: C changed only by blank lines plus this fusion (review.ps1 re-applies it to the snapshot); native results equal; DISAGREE 0.")
