inl note_of_gleam_tidy_output_1 () = Note ("GLEAM-TIDY-OUTPUT", 1u32, "2026-10-23T03:50Z", "main", "2026-10-22 23:50 main: format strings in codegenGleam ('v%i( %s  )' x2, 'v%i{i}( {arg_code}(      Nil)  ) ') produce the padding; main was appended unindented. Patch %TEMP%\\pack-next6\\gleam-tidy.ps1 tightens the three strings and indents main's lines by 4, skipping indentation when any line has an odd quote count (a possible multi-line string; the 447 tree main bodies have none). Whitespace only. Review: locals_check.py compares Gleam with all whitespace removed; the matrix's Gleam native rows check build and run. In PACK-NEXT-4 core D38D865FFCB50E17.")
inl note_of_gleam_tidy_output_2 () = Note ("GLEAM-TIDY-OUTPUT", 2u32, "2026-10-25T13:20Z", "main", "10-25 09:19 main groom: DONE by its rule (implemented, reviewed, installed). The slice's gleamIndentedMain + oddQuotes is in the installed tree core apps/compiler/spiral_compiler.fs. Negative control: the 5l'-only luaSpillLocals is absent, so the grep tells installed from staged. It has passed every accepted review since, latest the 5j accept single-flight-20261025-010749 (DISAGREE 0). Uncommitted until the user commits the compiler layer.")
inl rustls_advisories_2026_10 () = Task ("RUSTLS-ADVISORIES-2026-10", "Bring rustls, rustls-webpki and webpki-roots to the versions that resolve the 2026-10-21 RustSec batch (rustls 0.23.46, rustls-webpki 0.103.16, webpki-roots 1.0.10) in our Cargo.lock files", TaskKind, P1, D1, 100u32, Done, "", "security,rust,deps,main", "current", "current")
