inl eoie_job_owner_parent () = Task ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", "eoie processes belong to the session that started them: one job host per owner (the caller's nearest non-shell ancestor), created as its child; explorer only as a named fallback", Story, P0, D3, 60u32, Active, "EOIE-SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE", "eoie,jobs,processes", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_eoie_job_owner_parent () = Planning ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", Minutes 240u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_1 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 1u32, "2026-10-24T02:35Z", "eoie", "22:45 user 22:1x: 'when i asked for a parent to eoie processes, i thought they would be naturally born from our claude process or the pwsh that we're using (bad, slow startup) instead of being forced to spawn from explorer'. Drift traced: EOIE-JOB-HOST-INHERIT turned 'spin up with a parent' into the metric '0 dead parents' and met it with explorer, because the job host is one machine-wide singleton no session can own; memory then recorded explorer as the fix. Live trace 22:14: 52 processes anchored under explorer (the host, 20 supervisors, their job programs and conhosts), none under the session that started them.\nRule, written before drafting: a job's processes belong to the session that started it.\n(1) Owner = walk the calling eoie process's ancestors, skipping shells (cmd, pwsh, powershell, sh, bash, conhost) and eoie itself; the first other process is the owner, identified by pid + creation time. Generic names only (eoie is generic): the skip list is a typed union of launcher kinds, not a product name.\n(2) One host per owner: jobs/hosts/<owner-pid>-<owner-start-ms>/ {pid, requests/}; the host is created with PROC_THREAD_ATTRIBUTE_PARENT_PROCESS = the owner (OpenProcess 0x0080). The tree reads owner -> eoie host -> supervisors (DETACHED_PROCESS, EOIE-SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE) -> job programs.\n(3) Owner exits: the host removes its requests dir (HomeGone), writes owner-ended, takes no new jobs, lets running supervisors finish, then exits; queued jobs it holds are settled as a typed OwnerEnded case (visible in job status and to waiters), never silently dropped.\n(4) Fallback only when the owner can't be opened: explorer, named in the start receipt (parent=fallback-shell).\n(5) Machine-wide coordination (windows, heavy slots, after links across owners) stays file-based and unchanged.\nDone = a live trace shows every eoie process under its owner session, 0 explorer anchors and 0 dead parents while owners live, plus a notebook test of the owner walk (shell skipping, pid reuse via creation time) and an after-install probe that starts a job from a nested shell and finds the host under the calling session.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_2 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 2u32, "2026-10-24T02:58Z", "eoie", "22:58 draft owner-parent\\owner-parent.do (24 replacements over eoie_os_launch launch.spi, host_model, queue, host_run) applies on the post-train tree after supervisor-no-console. Typecheck 22:53: host_model PASS, including the new tests (owner walk skips shells and nested eoie, case-insensitive, pid+start home name, draining when the owner ends); host_run is link-only (E0433 eoie_os_launch). eoie_os_launch run.spi shows E0425, but an unmodified baseline shows the same E0425 (osl-baseline 22:57): module notebooks don't compile 'global' blocks. So the new Rust (eoie_parented_start, eoie_ancestry_text, eoie_process_started_ms) is NOT verified yet and needs the regen + cargo preview before release. Release order: after the train, after EOIE-SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE; after-install probe: a job started from a nested shell finds its host under the calling session.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_3 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 3u32, "2026-10-24T04:18Z", "eoie", "00:18 acceptance probe written: owner-parent\\after-install-owner.ps1. It derives the expected owner the way the code will (walk this shell's ancestors, skip launchers and eoie), starts a job in an isolated jobs home, and checks (1) one per-owner home named <owner-pid>-..., (2) the host's parent is the owner, (3) the job's supervisor is the host's child. Negative control on today's binary: 0/3, each for the right reason (expected owner claude.exe 51360 found; no hosts home; supervisor under an explorer-parented host). A cargo check of eoie-os-launch + eoie-job-host with the draft applied on the post-R tree is running (job-1792815425568); it compiles the new Windows code that notebooks skip.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_4 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 4u32, "2026-10-24T04:34Z", "eoie", "00:34 the new Windows code compiles: regen + cargo check of eoie-os-launch and eoie-job-host with owner-parent.do on the post-R tree PASS (00:33, warnings only). It took the stage-L global fix (EOIE-START-UNDER-SHELL note 4) for codegen to emit the launch Rust at all. Remaining: a release stage after R, then after-install-owner.ps1 (negative control 0/3 recorded).")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_5 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 5u32, "2026-10-24T08:21Z", "eoie", "04:2x eoie: under GRANULAR-HEAL (P0, user 10-24 via main), this draft cannot ship as written. owner-parent.do adds ~70 lines of Rust logic to eoie_os_launch's global block (eoie_process_started_ms, eoie_ancestry_text), and it edits the legacy eoie_shell_parented_start, which per AGENTS.md means migrating it in the same change. My audit of my own draft text (main's macro-rule regexes, scratch granular-audit.ps1) flags its parented_start call too (long, flow, cast). Rule, written before rework: S1 ships owner-parent only once the whole eoie_os_launch boundary is granular. (1) The global block keeps declarations only: repr(C) StartupInfo/StartupInfoEx/ProcessInfo/ToolhelpEntry, const empty values and named constants, and unsafe extern blocks whose items are declared safe fn (Rust 2024), so call sites need no unsafe blocks. (2) Each Win32 call is one named primitive of at most 120 chars, with pointers and out-cells passed as RefCell/Cell as_ptr primitives and no as-casts (convert in Spiral). (3) In Spiral: argument quoting, the flags x parent retry ladder (a union list), the shell-window fallback, FILETIME to unix ms, the toolhelp table and the ancestry walk. Unstable std raw_attribute (rustc 1.88 nightly, feature windows_process_extensions_raw_attribute) is not an option. Consumers call the Spiral functions through the package instead of eoie_os_launch:: Rust paths. Rework drafting starts now in scratch owner-parent-granular/.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_6 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 6u32, "2026-10-24T11:17Z", "eoie", "07:1x groom: the granular rework is drafted (owner-parent-granular/: win32.spi boundary, launch.spi logic, run.spi exports; apply-os-launch-granular.ps1 runs inside S1 after owner-parent.do). The first typecheck caught 'usize' (no such Spiral type) and an unescaped cfg bang, both fixed; the retypecheck is in runner eoie-serial-checks-2. launch-S1 refuses until lib env.process_id and env.command_line_arguments_from land (gates: arguments_from PASS, process_id regate queued).")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_7 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 7u32, "2026-10-25T10:02Z", "eoie", "06:02 eoie: the 4 lib gate drafts are respelled for edition 3 (:~ ^ for a recursive let, :! for nominal, \\\\ lambdas, ? ?> |: conditionals, !+ for true; scratch lib-gaps-3\\env-arguments-and-pid.do and char-code-and-stdin.do, both dry-run clean on the live lib) and typechecked on a real-folder lib copy. env.command_line_arguments_from passes. env.process_id passes, after its test was parenthesized: '(process_id () > 0u64) |> _assert_eq !+'; without parentheses the comparison bound after the pipe and the test failed silently, with no Rust error. console.read_to_end passes. In env only two pre-existing F# environment tests fail. sm'.char_code/of_char: its Rust test failed on the installed 5j with E0507 (5j's move-on-last-use bug, as did 3 other sm' Rust tests), so it is being re-run on the 5k candidate. Next: land all four through one eoie do program plus a lib gate job once heavy capacity allows, then S1 (this item) can go after SLATE.")
inl note_of_eoie_job_owner_parent_8 () = Note ("EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT", 8u32, "2026-10-25T11:18Z", "eoie", "07:18 eoie: all 4 edition-3 lib drafts pass on a real-folder lib copy with the 5k candidate: env.command_line_arguments_from, env.process_id, console.read_to_end, and sm'.char_code/of_char (one-test probe, since the full sm' notebook timed out under machine load). Bug found on the way: of_char's Rust arm (!input).to_string() returned 65 for 'A', because a Spiral char reaches Rust as a numeric code unit. Fixed with char::from(!input).to_string(), still one expression; the draft is updated (scratch lib-gaps-3\\char-code-and-stdin.do). Landing waits until after SLATE: their consumers (S1 here, and EOIE-GAP-INTAKE) are post-SLATE work, and a lib edit now would land under main's 5l' review and the SLATE full measure, both of which read the tree lib (cells-reads-live-tree).")
