inl note_of_eoie_ge2_crate_splits_1 () = Note ("EOIE-GE2-CRATE-SPLITS", 1u32, "2026-10-24T03:07Z", "eoie", "23:07 groom: blocks the whole release train (GE2 to P) and with it EOIE-SUPERVISOR-NO-CONSOLE and EOIE-JOB-OWNER-PARENT, which ship after it. Milestones: (1) supervise split drafted (eoie_job_env crate, ~940 expected) DONE as draft; (2) memory split drafted (eoie_memory_import, ~820 expected) DONE as draft; (3) analysis split: measurement crate for tallied/early_rows/values_of/terms_of/arm_counts (~290 lines) returning a typed tuple; (4) task_listing split: printing (print_json/print_table/json_line ~250); (5) regen + cargo preview on the 22:27 compiler, all four under 950; (6) land in live, chain-emulate GE2..P still applies, relaunch GE2 with a waiter. Details: EOIE-RELEASE-TRAIN notes 134-136.")
inl note_of_eoie_ge2_crate_splits_2 () = Note ("EOIE-GE2-CRATE-SPLITS", 2u32, "2026-10-24T03:08Z", "eoie", "23:08 night rules, written before measuring (autonomous run to 07:00). (R1) Order: finish the analysis + task_listing split drafts, then one regen + cargo preview of all four on a post-train scratch tree, then land and relaunch. (R2) A crate passes at <= 950 generated lines. 951-1000 passes only if removing more needs another crate seam (logged as a follow-up); > 1000 fails, so split again. (R3) Relaunch GE2 only when all four pass, chain-emulate GE2..P has no FAIL row (merged-line check included), and the Q typecheck still PASSes on the current compiler. (R4) Every queued job gets a background waiter in the same step; no compile while a live-gui block is announced; a reaped job is retried with lower parallelism. (R5) If any rule can't be met by 05:30, stop relaunching, leave the train parked with its exact blocker named here, and spend the remaining time on light items: JOB-START-SETTLE indent fix, owner-parent cargo check prep, then the next 'agile next --team eoie' rows.")
inl note_of_eoie_ge2_crate_splits_3 () = Note ("EOIE-GE2-CRATE-SPLITS", 3u32, "2026-10-24T03:46Z", "eoie", "23:46 milestones 1-5 met. Measured regen on the 22:27 compiler (split-measure 4): eoie_job_supervise 1062->534, eoie_memory 1040->647, agile_task_listing 1084->988, eoie_experiment_analysis 1030->986; new or changed crates eoie_job_env 566, eoie_memory_import 763, eoie_experiment_stats 805, agile_task_census 397. Per R2, the two crates at 986/988 pass inside the 951-1000 band; follow-up seams: analysis -> a measurement crate (~290 lines), task_listing -> the task-record parser (~200 lines). Packaged as stage GE3: crate-splits\\apply-crate-splits.ps1 (6 eoie do programs), launch-GE3.ps1 (fmt-rebase -Stage GE3 -RawFrom GE2 -Land, then the heavy release), release-build-job-GE3.ps1 (GE2's script plus the two new crates in the regen filter), after-install-GE3.ps1 (GE2's 10 checks plus agile list table/json and memory import, positive-controlled on today's binary). chain-next order now starts at GE3, launch-HIJK rebases from GE3, and chain-emulate picks the raw of whichever of GE2/GE3 last landed. Emulation GE3..P: 33 ok, 0 FAIL. fmt-rebase GE3 dry run: live matches GE2's landing, 17 writes. Waiting on the Q typecheck with GE3 (R3), then launch with waiters.")
