inl formatter_then_below () = Task ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", "apps/spiral/spiral.spi still has `then` laid on the line below its if: find whether the formatter fix was never reapplied there or the formatter still emits it, fix the source, re-lay the file (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D3, 60u32, Active, "", "formatter,apps,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_then_below () = Planning ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", Minutes 90u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_then_below_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-THEN-BELOW", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:02Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:02 main: found and healed. The installed formatter (5f) keeps `if c then` + block intact (stdin probe), but it also keeps an authored LONE `then` line (`if c` / `then` / block), because it never joins authored breaks. Those lone-then lines are artifacts of the 10-20 formatter runs: 2 in the 10-02 lib+apps/spiral, 37 now (33 at HEAD plus 4 in spiral.spi's unstaged diff). Healed by a token-neutral join (%TEMP%\\lib-lone-then\\apply.ps1: `if/elif cond` + lone `then` -> one line when it fits in 120; whitespace-only, checked per file): apps/spiral/spiral.spi 4 sites now; lib 27 sites in 8 files through the land guard (main-serial-lone-then). async, base, sm', sm'_real and trace come after their heal slices land. Formatter rule for the next formatter pack: a lone `then` line whose previous line is an if/elif condition at the same indent joins it when the result fits, the only case where the formatter joins an authored break (lone then is never an authored habit: 2 in the whole 10-02 corpus).")
inl formatter_lambda_next_line () = Task ("FORMATTER-LAMBDA-NEXT-LINE", "Formatter moved lambdas to the next line in lib/spiral/trace.spi: decide bug or rule, fix the formatter if bug, re-lay (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "formatter,lib,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_formatter_lambda_next_line () = Planning ("FORMATTER-LAMBDA-NEXT-LINE", Minutes 60u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_formatter_lambda_next_line_1 () = Note ("FORMATTER-LAMBDA-NEXT-LINE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:25Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:25 main: it is a bug, and it is reproduced: the installed formatter turns HEAD trace.spi's `| Zig => fun () =>` / `{` into `| Zig =>` / `fun () => {` whenever a line inside the record is over 120 (stdin probe, output identical to the worktree trace.spi). Cause: layoutArm (spiral_compiler.fs ~181137) keeps a lambda body on the arm line only when the lambda's laid head ends in `=>`; a record body lays the head as `fun () => {`, so the whole lambda drops a line. Authored evidence: the 10-02 lib + apps/spiral use only `| p => fun () =>` with `{` below (2 sites, 0 of the other shapes). Fix: %TEMP%\\pack-fmt-next\\fmt-fix\\arm-lambda-opener.ps1 keeps the authored head and lays `{` and the body one indent deeper. Formatter-only pack (core BEECFE432427C57A over tree 095EFD9A4CDB1C0C) in runner main-serial-fmt-next: build, the formatter candidate gate (user/lib/dice/eoie corpora, JOINED 0, token-neutral), and an arm-lambda probe on HEAD trace.spi, then install only on PASS, through the compiler-install window.")
inl note_of_formatter_lambda_next_line_2 () = Note ("FORMATTER-LAMBDA-NEXT-LINE", 2u32, "2026-10-24T15:10Z", "main", "main 11:1x: bug, not rule. The formatter fix (fmt-fix arm-lambda-opener: keep | p => fun () => with the opener below) passed pack-fmt-next chain-gate incl. the trace.spi probe and was installed 10:11 (main-fmt-next-install exit 0; canonical 6 of 6 on alphabet/dice). Re-lay: census over lib finds 3 split arms, all in trace.spi read_state (Zig/Rust/TypeScript; parsing.spi:357 and file_system.spi:894 are curried |> lambdas, not arms). Slice %TEMP%\\lib-trace-arm-lambda joins them token-neutrally; the installed formatter leaves the result unchanged (positive control: it rewrites a misaligned arm). Gate+land queued as job main-serial-trace-arm-lambda; close on land.")
inl note_of_formatter_lambda_next_line_3 () = Note ("FORMATTER-LAMBDA-NEXT-LINE", 3u32, "2026-10-24T16:27Z", "main", "main 12:3x: done. LIB-TRACE-ARM-LAMBDA GREEN 11:56 and landed (live trace.spi read_state: | Zig/Rust/TypeScript => fun () => with { below, lines 28/34/39); the installed formatter (fmt-next, 10:11) keeps that layout and leaves the file unchanged.")
inl lib_format_automation () = Task ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", "Unformatted code still lands in lib: automate formatting at land time (gate kit and lib_land run the formatter on touched files) and measure its cost so it does not clog the queue (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Story, P1, D3, 80u32, Active, "", "formatter,lib,tooling,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_lib_format_automation () = Planning ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", Minutes 120u32, Load Medium, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_lib_format_automation_1 () = Note ("LIB-FORMAT-AUTOMATION", 1u32, "2026-10-24T12:55Z", "main", "2026-10-24 08:55 main: measured: the installed formatter checks all of lib in 22 s on 2 threads (SPIRAL_FORMAT_PARALLEL=2), so it cannot clog the queue. Today 18 files would change, and 86 over-120 lines are strings and macros the formatter leaves alone (sm'_real 51, benchmark 12, trace 5). Automation: the gate kit's land.ps1 now hashes every lib file before the apply and formats exactly the files the apply touched, with the installed formatter, which is token-neutral by its own corpus gate. Every land therefore leaves its files formatted, and no file outside the slice is reflowed under another team's pending anchors. The files no pending slice edits (csv, conversation, cursor_walk, date_time, float_text, lustre, parsing, near_wallet) are formatted by a guarded land now (main-serial-format-idle). The other 10 (env, file_system, json_schema, oauth, otp_actor, otp_supervisor, resultm, sm', xpath_eval, xsd_emit) get formatted by their pending lands. oauth and otp_* are x drafts, so they wait for x.")
inl platform_bound_tsv () = Task ("PLATFORM-BOUND-TSV", "apps/compiler/tmp/tests/platform-bound.tsv: find why it exists and whether it is drift (TSVs are a slippery slope); move the facts into typed Spiral or the matrix table, delete the TSV (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", TaskKind, P1, D2, 100u32, Done, "", "compiler,tests,drift,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_platform_bound_tsv () = Planning ("PLATFORM-BOUND-TSV", Minutes 60u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_platform_bound_tsv_1 () = Note ("PLATFORM-BOUND-TSV", 1u32, "2026-10-24T11:55Z", "main", "2026-10-24 07:55 main: drift confirmed and healed. The TSV (untracked, 4 rows) existed only for ci-classify.ps1, to tag local-vs-CI behavior differences as platform-bound (CI-OFFLOAD notes 13-17). It repeated facts the matrix already holds: tests/matrix.psd1 Known entries scope the 2 POSIX-only C rows with Platform = 'Windows'. Now all_terminals' F# Known entry carries Platform = 'Windows', mega_omniledger_erp_kernel's F# row has a Windows-scoped Known entry (the /bin/sh spawn), ci-classify reads every Platform-scoped Known entry from matrix.psd1 (Import-PowerShellDataFile -SkipLimitCheck, as test.ps1 does), and the TSV is deleted (checked: all 4 rows covered). Rule for later: a new hand-written table goes into matrix.psd1 or typed Spiral, never a TSV. The deeper fix, portable F# macros in the omniledger mega sample, stays with that sample.")
inl compiler_tmp_retire () = Task ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", "Retire apps/compiler/tmp: every script, test and lane folder moves to its proper place (or into Spiral programs), no new folders under tmp (tests/families went in wrongly), tmp/scripts and its new subfolders shrink to zero without losing code; lanes/hopacsota/research and other script euphoria folded or deleted by rule (user 2026-10-24 06:56 review list)", Epic, P1, D7, 5u32, Active, "", "compiler,tmp,drift,structure,main", "current", "current")
inl planning_of_compiler_tmp_retire () = Planning ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", Minutes 2400u32, Load Light, Assigned Agent)
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_1 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:12Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:12 main: from FLAT-FOLDERS: the samples move (apps/compiler/tmp/samples -> top-level samples/, 9,882 files losing 2 levels) is this epic's first and largest step. test.ps1/matrix.psd1 paths, CI and EXPECTED.tsv ids (samples/<name>) are written to keep their `samples/...` ids, so the oracle needs no re-accept beyond the path root.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_2 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 2u32, "2026-10-25T14:06Z", "main", "10-25 10:06 main: inventory (10,015 tracked files under apps/compiler/tmp) and destination rules, written before any move (rule: decide by pre-written rules).\n(1) samples/ (9,855): to top-level samples/ per FLAT-FOLDERS, keeping 'samples/<name>' ids so EXPECTED.tsv only changes its path root. Precondition: no matrix reader live (the 5l' review/install/accept done) and an exclusive window, since test.ps1, matrix.psd1 and CI paths change in the same edit.\n(2) compiler/ (host, core, lib, runtime-compat, Directory.Build.props; 13): product code, so it goes to apps/compiler/host etc., next to spiral_compiler.fs. Precondition: build.ps1 and env.ps1 paths updated in the same edit, and a candidate build proves an identical DLL hash (deterministic build).\n(3) tests/ (matrix.psd1, native-shims 31, rust-exports 5): to apps/compiler/tests/.\n(4) scripts/ (62): each script is classified once by rule: an entry point (build.ps1, test.ps1, env.ps1, probe.ps1) moves to apps/compiler/; a method used by several sessions becomes an eoie verb (memory: generic tools, not per-experiment scripts) and the script is deleted once the verb ships; a script with no caller in any repo or CI and no backlog reference newer than 10-20 is deleted by the dangling-check rule (grep the stem in all repos plus consumer builds, with a positive control).\n(5) formatter/ (30 F#/Python prototype files): the formatter lives in the compiler's '/// ## Formatter' section now. Each file is deleted once a grep shows no caller and its function exists in 'SpiralCompiler format' (format.ps1 corpus modes: check format-corpus covers them first).\n(6) lanes/ (14 docs: hopacsota PLAN.md etc.): facts go into backlog notes on the lane's items (memory: research lives in backlog), then the files are deleted.\nOutside references to update in the same edits: .github/workflows/gh-pages.yml, apps/cells (README.md, compiler_daemon.ex, run_notebook.ps1, run_suite.ps1), apps/lisp (lisp.livemd, membership*.spl), apps/zed (fixtures package.spiproj x2, tasks/test-at-row.ps1), scripts/init-wgsl-run.ps1, scripts/workflow.ps1. Order: (6) and (5) first (docs and dead code, no readers), then (4) by class, (3), (2), and (1) last in its own window.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_3 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 3u32, "2026-10-25T14:19Z", "main", "10-25 10:19 main: step (5), formatter/ classified, with a correction to the plan's method. The repo grep alone was WRONG for 4 files: candidate-gate.ps1 showed no callers in any repo, yet %TEMP%\\pack-next4\\review.ps1:46 calls it on every pack review, and it runs extract-corpus.ps1, fitting_lines_kept.py and complaints_probe.py. Those are LIVE (the pack review's formatter gate). Also live: report.ps1 (CI: scripts/workflow.ps1), corpus.ps1 (scripts/parser-corpus-gate.ps1), format.ps1 and lint.ps1 (documented entry points in tmp/AGENTS.md). Rule amended: the dangling check also greps %TEMP% pack/gate/serial scripts and follows live callers one level down (memory dangling-check-by-stem). Dead: the 8 F# prototypes (Check, Convert, Flatten, Format, Layout, Lexed, Parsed, Spacing .fsx). They form a closed #load cluster rooted at Format.fsx, which nothing outside the cluster loads, and only lanes/formatter/PLAN.md mentions them. Their function lives in 'SpiralCompiler format'. Deletion waits for the %TEMP% caller scan. The live formatter tooling then moves with step (4) to its proper place (probably apps/compiler/formatter/), not deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_4 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 4u32, "2026-10-25T15:11Z", "main", "10-25 11:11 main: step (5) part 1 DONE. Deleted the 8 dead F# formatter prototypes (Check, Convert, Flatten, Format, Layout, Lexed, Parsed, Spacing .fsx; unstaged, copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\formatter-fsx). The rule held on every source: no caller in any of 9 repos, CI or the top-level scripts of 144 %TEMP% job folders (453 scripts; positive control: the same scan finds 13 callers of candidate-gate.ps1); a closed #load cluster rooted at Format.fsx; their function lives in 'SpiralCompiler format'. lanes/formatter/PLAN.md still names them as history, and it goes with step (6). Left in formatter/: the live gate tooling (candidate-gate, extract-corpus, fitting_lines_kept, complaints_probe, report, corpus, format, lint) and synthetic/, all moving with step (4).")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_5 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 5u32, "2026-10-25T15:16Z", "main", "10-25 11:16 main: step (6) started. lanes/bend/w64.bend deleted (a hand-written Bend probe of the w64 helpers; 0 references in the repo; copy in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\lanes), and the empty bend/ folder with it. single-flight/README.md's one unique fact is now CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS; the rest repeats tmp/AGENTS.md. RUST_LIBRARY_PLAN.md is finished history (all steps done 09-28). gpt5parallel/README.md's unique fact is the run-log location + 'Select-String runtime_exception_captured'. These three, plus tmp/NEXT.md, which links to them (NEXT.md:168/185/786, AGENTS.md:124), go together in ONE doc pass so no link dangles: facts to backlog notes, AGENTS.md:124 repointed to FRONTIER.md, then the files deleted.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_6 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 6u32, "2026-10-25T15:18Z", "main", "10-25 11:18 main: lanes/hopacsota/research/ (untracked, 9 per-experiment scripts r3_*/r4_*/tree_paths, 56 KB, all stamped 10-22 00:05, i.e. a lab-drain copy) DELETED; copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\hopacsota-research. Rule basis: per-experiment scripts are not kept (memory generic-tools-not-per-experiment); their findings are cited in backlog notes (r4_deferred 7 lines, r3_simulate 6, r3_instrument 5); the R4 edits they applied are in the tree core (R4 gate met 10-15, seams installed); no job script in %TEMP% calls research/; the only tracked mentions are 2 historical lines in lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md ('job scratch ...r4_deferred.ps1'), which goes in the doc pass.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_7 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 7u32, "2026-10-25T15:29Z", "main", "10-25 11:29 main: step (6) doc pass 1 DONE: tmp/NEXT.md (838 lines, frozen since 10-18), lanes/gpt5parallel/README.md, lanes/single-flight/README.md and RUST_LIBRARY_PLAN.md deleted (unstaged, copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\docs; the files stay in git history). Folded first. NEXT.md's 'Open, in order' entries 0-3 were done or obsolete and entry 4 was overtaken (gpt5parallel met the promotion criterion 10-01); entries 5 and 6 became MUTUAL-TAIL-LOOPS and DELPHI-ARC-MEMORY. The single-flight README's gap is CONTRACT-REJECTION-DIAGNOSTICS, and the gpt5parallel README's run-log facts are a sentence in tmp/AGENTS.md's gpt5parallel paragraph. Links repointed: AGENTS.md (3), README.md (1, now pointing at the backlog), FRONTIER.md (6), all citing NEXT.md@47d1e562 so they still resolve. Left: one code comment in spiral_compiler.fs:186146 mentions NEXT.md; strip it in the next pack (no-comments rule). Still to fold: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md (85 KB), lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (92 KB), lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (90 KB), hopacsota hop-probes, formatter/allowlist.tsv.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_8 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 8u32, "2026-10-25T16:26Z", "main", "10-25 12:26 main: step (6) doc pass 2 DONE: lanes/formatter/PLAN.md (813 lines) and allowlist.tsv (25 rows) deleted (unstaged; copies in %TEMP%\\compiler-tmp-retire\\docs\\lanes-formatter), with the empty lanes/formatter/ folder. Folded first: the measured user style, F1-F10, the keep-breaks additions, the G6 banned list, G1-G7 and the process rules are one note on SPIRAL-FORMATTER. The user decisions were already notes (SPIRAL-FORMATTER 1, FORMATTER-KEEP-BREAKS 1). Scoreboards and the decision-change log are history, kept at PLAN.md@0ec501fb. Dangling check: 0 readers of allowlist.tsv or lanes/formatter in the 9 repos, CI, the compiler, or 858 %TEMP% job scripts (positive control: candidate-gate.ps1 found 19 times). tmp/AGENTS.md:147 now points at the backlog notes plus PLAN.md@0ec501fb. Left in step 6: lanes/hopacsota/PLAN.md (92 KB, the live hopacsota contract that memory and AGENTS.md cite, so it is folded last, after its readers are repointed), lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (90 KB), hopacsota hop-probes.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_9 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 9u32, "2026-10-25T16:30Z", "main", "10-25 12:30 main: lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (1,045 lines, last edit f5e487e0 10-18) is NOT folded yet, by rule (links must resolve): 23 comments in spiral_compiler.fs cite its fix numbers ('FRONTIER.md fix 22/33-47/50/55'; lines 10746, 15806, 55149, 57317, 83125, 87117, 129890, 135213, 137838, 137863, 137926, 146883, 147687, 149237, 149245, 152779, 157437, 157525, 158919, 186182, 186197, 186243, 188866), as do tmp/AGENTS.md:12 and :89 and 13 backlog notes. Order: (a) the pack after 5m strips those comments (the no-comments rule; the code keeps its meaning in names), together with the NEXT.md comment at :186146; (b) AGENTS.md's citations become FRONTIER.md@f5e487e0; (c) the fix list's still-live facts (the fast loop; fixes 22, 57 and 58 named in AGENTS.md) go into notes on HOPACSOTA items; (d) the file is deleted. Backlog notes citing 'FRONTIER.md fix N' stay readable through the pin.")
inl note_of_compiler_tmp_retire_10 () = Note ("COMPILER-TMP-RETIRE", 10u32, "2026-10-25T16:47Z", "main", "10-25 12:47 main: step (a) of the FRONTIER order is staged for pack 5m: %TEMP%\\pack-next5m\\strip-doc-citations.ps1 -Target <core> [-Apply]. It finds by content every pure line-comment block that cites tmp/NEXT.md or lanes/gpt5parallel/FRONTIER.md (24 blocks, 86 lines on today's tree core, including the NEXT.md one at :186146), refuses a block holding a directive or marker, and proves that every non-comment line is unchanged and in order. On a copy, pair-drift found 0 pairs touched on one side only (8 pairs, 2 touched since HEAD by the user's staged work). Proof in the pack review: a comment-only edit, so residuals must be identical (the review's DISAGREE 0 and 0 differing cells cover it). After 5m installs: AGENTS.md:12/:89 citations become FRONTIER.md@f5e487e0, the live facts move to HOPACSOTA notes, and the file is deleted.")
