inl note_of_nested_if_tool_1 () = Note ("NESTED-IF-TOOL", 1u32, "2026-10-24T13:22Z", "main", "2026-10-24 09:22 main: prototype (scratch nested-if-census.ps1: an indentation stack per definition; elif/else/then continue a chain, so flat elif chains count as one level). With threshold 4 over lib, x, tibia and fiscal: 11 definitions, which is little, because elif chains dominate. Deepest: tibia map.spi ids_with (7), tibia map walk_tiles, competitor tick, random tick (5), lib decimal.spi rec, parsing.spi many_chars_till (5), unicode.char_of (5, all inside the old C macro text the unicode heal removes), xsd_regex.spi let (4), tibia steps/observer/step_away (4). x and fiscal have none at 4+. Candidates for typefeatureset modeling: lib decimal.rec and parsing.many_chars_till (main; the parsing one with FPARSEC-RETIRE), xsd_regex (main), the tibia ones (tibia team, TIBIA-GRANULAR-HEAL). As a lint, depth >= 4 belongs in GRANULAR-LINT's eoie verb next to the macro rules, with the census as its baseline.")
