inl note_of_tibia_edition3_1 () = Note ("TIBIA-EDITION3", 1u32, "2026-10-25T03:12Z", "tibia-lane", "2026-10-24 23:12 User directive (via main, 23:0x): edition 3 spreads to every repo, and the tibia repo is tibia's to respell. Done 23:2x: respell-repo.ps1 on copies GREEN (51 of 52 .spi files, 0 errors, words round trip byte-identical, 0 installed-formatter changes); the Cells round-trip scan covered 51 files per side with the same 33 failures, all a pre-existing Document drop of line 2 'test <module> static ='; reported to main. Land queued as heavy job-1792897922037-tibia-respell-land: apply as an unstaged layer over the user's staged files, the arena build with compiled Lua byte-identical to the pre-respell hashes, the full build.ps1 with SPIRAL_CELLS_MEMO=0, and a restore of all 51 originals on any failure. Excluded: src/terrain.spi, which apps/map/run.ps1 generates in words and matches by 'let <name> '. The installed compiler (10:08) ignores format --spelling. Left after the land: (a) once a spelling-capable formatter is installed, run.ps1 formats its generated text with --spelling symbols and matches ':~ <name> ', then terrain.spi respells (about 20 min); (b) re-derive the tibia drafts on edition-3 text: client-heal footing and batch2 (stale anyway against the staged base), batch3, and the CELLS-APPS candidates (about 40 min, folded into GRANULAR-HEAL and CELLS-APPS).")
